de répertoires d''état","alternatives au gestionnaire de répertoires d''état","installation du gestionnaire de répertoires d''état"],"de":["AI-Tools","zentrales Verzeichnis-Management","GitHub","Repository-Verwaltung","modulares Design","wie man den zentralen Verzeichnis-Manager verwendet","Alternativen zum zentralen Verzeichnis-Manager","Installation des zentralen Verzeichnis-Managers"],"pt":["como usar state-directory-manager","o que é state-directory-manager","alternativas para state-directory-manager","state-directory-manager vs git","instalar state-directory-manager","guia de configuração do state-directory-manager","ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial para desenvolvedores","gerenciamento de repositórios GitHub"],"ru":["как использовать state-directory-manager","что такое state-directory-manager","альтернативы state-directory-manager","state-directory-manager vs git","установить state-directory-manager","руководство по настройке state-directory-manager","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков","управление репозиториями GitHub"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام state-directory-manager","ما هو state-directory-manager","بديل ل state-directory-manager","state-directory-manager مقابل git","تثبيت state-directory-manager","دليل إعداد state-directory-manager","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","إدارة مستودعات جيثب"]}},"owner":"vamseeachanta","repo":"workspace-hub","repoPath":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T13:18:49.023Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"state-directory-manager","description":"Manage persistent state directories for bash scripts","version":"1.0.0","tags":["bash","state","persistence","config","directory","xdg"],"bodyPreview":"# State Directory Manager\n\nPatterns for managing persistent state, configuration, and cache directories in bash scripts following XDG Base Directory specification.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n✅ **Use when:**\n- Scripts need to persist data between runs\n- Storing user preferences or configuration\n- Caching results for performance\n- Managing log files with rotation\n- Creating portable CLI tools\n\n❌ **Avoid when:**\n- One-time scripts that don''t need state\n- Scripts that should be purely stateless\n- W","body":"# State Directory Manager\n\nPatterns for managing persistent state, configuration, and cache directories in bash scripts following XDG Base Directory specification.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n✅ **Use when:**\n- Scripts need to persist data between runs\n- Storing user preferences or configuration\n- Caching results for performance\n- Managing log files with rotation\n- Creating portable CLI tools\n\n❌ **Avoid when:**\n- One-time scripts that don''t need state\n- Scripts that should be purely stateless\n- When environment variables are sufficient\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. XDG Base Directory Standard\n\nFollow the XDG specification for directory locations:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: XDG Base Directory compliant state management\n# ABOUTME: Cross-platform directory locations\n\n# XDG Base Directories with fallbacks\nXDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}\"\nXDG_DATA_HOME=\"${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}\"\nXDG_STATE_HOME=\"${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}\"\nXDG_CACHE_HOME=\"${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}\"\n\n# Application-specific directories\nAPP_NAME=\"my-tool\"\nCONFIG_DIR=\"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/$APP_NAME\"\nDATA_DIR=\"$XDG_DATA_HOME/$APP_NAME\"\nSTATE_DIR=\"$XDG_STATE_HOME/$APP_NAME\"\nCACHE_DIR=\"$XDG_CACHE_HOME/$APP_NAME\"\nLOG_DIR=\"$STATE_DIR/logs\"\n\n# Initialize directories\ninit_directories() {\n    mkdir -p \"$CONFIG_DIR\"\n    mkdir -p \"$DATA_DIR\"\n    mkdir -p \"$STATE_DIR\"\n    mkdir -p \"$CACHE_DIR\"\n    mkdir -p \"$LOG_DIR\"\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Workspace-Hub Pattern\n\nAlternative using home directory (from workspace-hub scripts):\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: Workspace-hub style state directory management\n# ABOUTME: Simple $HOME/.app-name pattern\n\nAPP_NAME=\"workspace-hub\"\nAPP_DIR=\"${HOME}/.${APP_NAME}\"\n\n# Directory structure\nCONFIG_DIR=\"$APP_DIR/config\"\nDATA_DIR=\"$APP_DIR/data\"\nLOGS_DIR=\"$APP_DIR/logs\"\nCACHE_DIR=\"$APP_DIR/cache\"\nTEMP_DIR=\"$APP_DIR/tmp\"\n\n# Initialize with proper permissions\ninit_app_dirs() {\n    local dirs=(\"$CONFIG_DIR\" \"$DATA_DIR\" \"$LOGS_DIR\" \"$CACHE_DIR\" \"$TEMP_DIR\")\n\n    for dir in \"${dirs[@]}\"; do\n        if [[ ! -d \"$dir\" ]]; then\n            mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n            chmod 700 \"$dir\"  # Private by default\n        fi\n    done\n}\n\n# Clean old temp files\nclean_temp() {\n    find \"$TEMP_DIR\" -type f -mtime +1 -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Configuration File Management\n\nRead and write configuration files:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: Configuration file management\n# ABOUTME: Key-value pairs with defaults\n\nCONFIG_FILE=\"$CONFIG_DIR/config\"\n\n# Default configuration\ndeclare -A DEFAULT_CONFIG=(\n    [\"parallel_workers\"]=\"5\"\n    [\"log_level\"]=\"INFO\"\n    [\"auto_sync\"]=\"true\"\n    [\"timeout\"]=\"30\"\n)\n\n# Initialize config with defaults\ninit_config() {\n    if [[ ! -f \"$CONFIG_FILE\" ]]; then\n        {\n            echo \"# Configuration for $APP_NAME\"\n            echo \"# Generated: $(date)\"\n            echo \"\"\n            for key in \"${!DEFAULT_CONFIG[@]}\"; do\n                echo \"${key}=${DEFAULT_CONFIG[$key]}\"\n            done\n        } > \"$CONFIG_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Read config value\nget_config() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local default=\"${2:-${DEFAULT_CONFIG[$key]:-}}\"\n\n    if [[ -f \"$CONFIG_FILE\" ]]; then\n        local value\n        value=$(grep \"^${key}=\" \"$CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d''='' -f2-)\n        echo \"${value:-$default}\"\n    else\n        echo \"$default\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Write config value\nset_config() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n\n    init_config\n\n    if grep -q \"^${key}=\" \"$CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        # Update existing\n        sed -i \"s|^${key}=.*|${key}=${value}|\" \"$CONFIG_FILE\"\n    else\n        # Add new\n        echo \"${key}=${value}\" >> \"$CONFIG_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Load all config into associative array\nload_config() {\n    declare -gA CONFIG\n\n    # Start with defaults\n    for key in \"${!DEFAULT_CONFIG[@]}\"; do\n        CONFIG[$key]=\"${DEFAULT_CONFIG[$key]}\"\n    done\n\n    # Override with file values\n    if [[ -f \"$CONFIG_FILE\" ]]; then\n        while IFS=''='' read -r key value; do\n            [[ \"$key\" =~ ^#.*$ || -z \"$key\" ]] && continue\n            CONFIG[$key]=\"$value\"\n        done < \"$CONFIG_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Usage\ninit_config\nload_config\necho \"Parallel workers: ${CONFIG[parallel_workers]}\"\nset_config \"parallel_workers\" \"10\"\n```\n\n### 4. State File Operations\n\nTrack persistent state between runs:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: State file operations\n# ABOUTME: Track last run, progress, etc.\n\nSTATE_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/state.json\"\n\n# Initialize state\ninit_state() {\n    if [[ ! -f \"$STATE_FILE\" ]]; then\n        cat > \"$STATE_FILE\" << EOF\n{\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n    \"created\": \"$(date -Iseconds)\",\n    \"last_run\": null,\n    \"run_count\": 0,\n    \"last_status\": null\n}\nEOF\n    fi\n}\n\n# Get state value (requires jq)\nget_state() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local default=\"${2:-null}\"\n\n    if [[ -f \"$STATE_FILE\" ]] && command -v jq &>/dev/null; then\n        jq -r \".$key // $default\" \"$STATE_FILE\"\n    else\n        echo \"$default\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Update state value (requires jq)\nset_state() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n\n    init_state\n\n    if command -v jq &>/dev/null; then\n        local temp=$(mktemp)\n        jq \".$key = $value\" \"$STATE_FILE\" > \"$temp\" && mv \"$temp\" \"$STATE_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Record run\nrecord_run() {\n    local status=\"$1\"\n\n    set_state \"last_run\" \"\\\"$(date -Iseconds)\\\"\"\n    set_state \"last_status\" \"\\\"$status\\\"\"\n    set_state \"run_count\" \"$(($(get_state run_count 0) + 1))\"\n}\n\n# Simple key-value state (no jq required)\nSTATE_KV_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/state.kv\"\n\nget_state_kv() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local default=\"$2\"\n\n    if [[ -f \"$STATE_KV_FILE\" ]]; then\n        grep \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_KV_FILE\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d''='' -f2- || echo \"$default\"\n    else\n        echo \"$default\"\n    fi\n}\n\nset_state_kv() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n\n    mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$STATE_KV_FILE\")\"\n\n    if [[ -f \"$STATE_KV_FILE\" ]] && grep -q \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_KV_FILE\"; then\n        sed -i \"s|^${key}=.*|${key}=${value}|\" \"$STATE_KV_FILE\"\n    else\n        echo \"${key}=${value}\" >> \"$STATE_KV_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Cache Management\n\nImplement caching with expiration:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: Cache management with TTL\n# ABOUTME: Store and retrieve cached data\n\nCACHE_TTL=\"${CACHE_TTL:-3600}\"  # 1 hour default\n\n# Get cache file path\ncache_path() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local hash=$(echo -n \"$key\" | md5sum | cut -c1-16)\n    echo \"$CACHE_DIR/${hash}\"\n}\n\n# Check if cache is valid\ncache_valid() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local ttl=\"${2:-$CACHE_TTL}\"\n    local path=$(cache_path \"$key\")\n\n    if [[ -f \"$path\" ]]; then\n        local age=$(($(date +%s) - $(stat -c %Y \"$path\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f %m \"$path\")))\n        [[ $age -lt $ttl ]]\n    else\n        return 1\n    fi\n}\n\n# Get from cache\ncache_get() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local ttl=\"${2:-$CACHE_TTL}\"\n    local path=$(cache_path \"$key\")\n\n    if cache_valid \"$key\" \"$ttl\"; then\n        cat \"$path\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n    return 1\n}\n\n# Set cache\ncache_set() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n    local path=$(cache_path \"$key\")\n\n    mkdir -p \"$CACHE_DIR\"\n    echo \"$value\" > \"$path\"\n}\n\n# Delete cache\ncache_delete() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local path=$(cache_path \"$key\")\n    rm -f \"$path\"\n}\n\n# Clear all cache\ncache_clear() {\n    rm -rf \"$CACHE_DIR\"/*\n}\n\n# Clean expired cache entries\ncache_clean() {\n    local ttl=\"${1:-$CACHE_TTL}\"\n    find \"$CACHE_DIR\" -type f -mmin \"+$((ttl / 60))\" -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n\n# Usage with automatic caching\nget_with_cache() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local command=\"$2\"\n    local ttl=\"${3:-$CACHE_TTL}\"\n\n    if cache_valid \"$key\" \"$ttl\"; then\n        cache_get \"$key\"\n    else\n        local result\n        result=$(eval \"$command\")\n        cache_set \"$key\" \"$result\"\n        echo \"$result\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Example\nresult=$(get_with_cache \"api_response\" \"curl -s https://api.example.com/data\" 300)\n```\n\n### 6. Log File Management\n\nManage logs with rotation:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: Log file management with rotation\n# ABOUTME: Automatic cleanup of old logs\n\nLOG_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/app.log\"\nLOG_MAX_SIZE=$((10 * 1024 * 1024))  # 10MB\nLOG_MAX_FILES=5\n\n# Initialize logging\ninit_logging() {\n    mkdir -p \"$LOG_DIR\"\n    touch \"$LOG_FILE\"\n}\n\n# Write to log\nlog_to_file() {\n    local level=\"$1\"\n    shift\n    local message=\"$*\"\n    local timestamp=$(date ''+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')\n\n    echo \"[$timestamp] $level: $message\" >> \"$LOG_FILE\"\n\n    # Check if rotation needed\n    maybe_rotate_logs\n}\n\n# Rotate logs if needed\nmaybe_rotate_logs() {\n    if [[ -f \"$LOG_FILE\" ]]; then\n        local size=$(stat -c %s \"$LOG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f %z \"$LOG_FILE\")\n\n        if [[ $size -gt $LOG_MAX_SIZE ]]; then\n            rotate_logs\n        fi\n    fi\n}\n\n# Perform log rotation\nrotate_logs() {\n    # Remove oldest\n    rm -f \"${LOG_FILE}.${LOG_MAX_FILES}\"\n\n    # Shift existing\n    for ((i=LOG_MAX_FILES-1; i>=1; i--)); do\n        if [[ -f \"${LOG_FILE}.$i\" ]]; then\n            mv \"${LOG_FILE}.$i\" \"${LOG_FILE}.$((i+1))\"\n        fi\n    done\n\n    # Rotate current\n    if [[ -f \"$LOG_FILE\" ]]; then\n        mv \"$LOG_FILE\" \"${LOG_FILE}.1\"\n        touch \"$LOG_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# Clean old logs\nclean_old_logs() {\n    local days=\"${1:-30}\"\n    find \"$LOG_DIR\" -name \"*.log*\" -mtime \"+$days\" -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n\n# View recent logs\ntail_logs() {\n    local lines=\"${1:-50}\"\n    tail -n \"$lines\" \"$LOG_FILE\"\n}\n\n# Search logs\nsearch_logs() {\n    local pattern=\"$1\"\n    grep -h \"$pattern\" \"$LOG_DIR\"/*.log* 2>/dev/null | tail -100\n}\n```\n\n## Complete Example: State Manager Module\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# ABOUTME: Complete state directory manager\n# ABOUTME: Reusable module for bash scripts\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# State Directory Manager v1.0.0\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Application identity (override in your script)\n: \"${STATE_APP_NAME:=my-app}\"\n\n# Directory setup\nSTATE_BASE_DIR=\"${HOME}/.${STATE_APP_NAME}\"\nSTATE_CONFIG_DIR=\"$STATE_BASE_DIR/config\"\nSTATE_DATA_DIR=\"$STATE_BASE_DIR/data\"\nSTATE_CACHE_DIR=\"$STATE_BASE_DIR/cache\"\nSTATE_LOG_DIR=\"$STATE_BASE_DIR/logs\"\nSTATE_TMP_DIR=\"$STATE_BASE_DIR/tmp\"\n\n# File paths\nSTATE_CONFIG_FILE=\"$STATE_CONFIG_DIR/config\"\nSTATE_STATE_FILE=\"$STATE_DATA_DIR/state\"\nSTATE_LOG_FILE=\"$STATE_LOG_DIR/app.log\"\n\n# Settings\nSTATE_CACHE_TTL=\"${STATE_CACHE_TTL:-3600}\"\nSTATE_LOG_MAX_SIZE=\"${STATE_LOG_MAX_SIZE:-10485760}\"\nSTATE_LOG_MAX_FILES=\"${STATE_LOG_MAX_FILES:-5}\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Initialization\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_init() {\n    local dirs=(\n        \"$STATE_CONFIG_DIR\"\n        \"$STATE_DATA_DIR\"\n        \"$STATE_CACHE_DIR\"\n        \"$STATE_LOG_DIR\"\n        \"$STATE_TMP_DIR\"\n    )\n\n    for dir in \"${dirs[@]}\"; do\n        if [[ ! -d \"$dir\" ]]; then\n            mkdir -p \"$dir\"\n            chmod 700 \"$dir\"\n        fi\n    done\n\n    # Initialize files\n    [[ -f \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\" ]] || touch \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\"\n    [[ -f \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\" ]] || touch \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\"\n    [[ -f \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\" ]] || touch \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\"\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Config Functions\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_config_get() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local default=\"$2\"\n    grep \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d''='' -f2- || echo \"$default\"\n}\n\nstate_config_set() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n\n    if grep -q \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        sed -i \"s|^${key}=.*|${key}=${value}|\" \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\"\n    else\n        echo \"${key}=${value}\" >> \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\nstate_config_list() {\n    cat \"$STATE_CONFIG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v ''^#'' | grep -v ''^$''\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# State Functions\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_get() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local default=\"$2\"\n    grep \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d''='' -f2- || echo \"$default\"\n}\n\nstate_set() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n\n    if grep -q \"^${key}=\" \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        sed -i \"s|^${key}=.*|${key}=${value}|\" \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\"\n    else\n        echo \"${key}=${value}\" >> \"$STATE_STATE_FILE\"\n    fi\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Cache Functions\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_cache_key() {\n    echo -n \"$1\" | md5sum | cut -c1-16\n}\n\nstate_cache_get() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local ttl=\"${2:-$STATE_CACHE_TTL}\"\n    local path=\"$STATE_CACHE_DIR/$(state_cache_key \"$key\")\"\n\n    if [[ -f \"$path\" ]]; then\n        local age=$(($(date +%s) - $(stat -c %Y \"$path\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f %m \"$path\")))\n        if [[ $age -lt $ttl ]]; then\n            cat \"$path\"\n            return 0\n        fi\n    fi\n    return 1\n}\n\nstate_cache_set() {\n    local key=\"$1\"\n    local value=\"$2\"\n    local path=\"$STATE_CACHE_DIR/$(state_cache_key \"$key\")\"\n    echo \"$value\" > \"$path\"\n}\n\nstate_cache_clear() {\n    rm -rf \"$STATE_CACHE_DIR\"/*\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Log Functions\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_log() {\n    local level=\"$1\"\n    shift\n    local message=\"$*\"\n    echo \"[$(date ''+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'')] $level: $message\" >> \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\"\n\n    # Auto-rotate\n    local size=$(stat -c %s \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n    if [[ $size -gt $STATE_LOG_MAX_SIZE ]]; then\n        state_log_rotate\n    fi\n}\n\nstate_log_rotate() {\n    rm -f \"${STATE_LOG_FILE}.${STATE_LOG_MAX_FILES}\"\n    for ((i=STATE_LOG_MAX_FILES-1; i>=1; i--)); do\n        [[ -f \"${STATE_LOG_FILE}.$i\" ]] && mv \"${STATE_LOG_FILE}.$i\" \"${STATE_LOG_FILE}.$((i+1))\"\n    done\n    mv \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\" \"${STATE_LOG_FILE}.1\"\n    touch \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\"\n}\n\nstate_log_tail() {\n    tail -n \"${1:-50}\" \"$STATE_LOG_FILE\"\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Cleanup Functions\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_cleanup() {\n    # Clean temp files older than 1 day\n    find \"$STATE_TMP_DIR\" -type f -mtime +1 -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n\n    # Clean expired cache\n    find \"$STATE_CACHE_DIR\" -type f -mmin \"+$((STATE_CACHE_TTL / 60))\" -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n\n    # Clean old logs\n    find \"$STATE_LOG_DIR\" -name \"*.log.*\" -mtime +30 -delete 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n\nstate_reset() {\n    rm -rf \"$STATE_BASE_DIR\"\n    state_init\n}\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Auto-initialize\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstate_init\n```\n\n## Usage in Scripts\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# Your script that uses the state manager\n\n# Set app name before sourcing\nSTATE_APP_NAME=\"my-tool\"\n\n# Source the state manager\nsource /path/to/state-manager.sh\n\n# Now use it\nstate_config_set \"api_key\" \"abc123\"\napi_key=$(state_config_get \"api_key\")\n\nstate_set \"last_run\" \"$(date -Iseconds)\"\nstate_log \"INFO\" \"Script started\"\n\n# Use cache\nif ! result=$(state_cache_get \"api_response\"); then\n    result=$(curl -s https://api.example.com/data)\n    state_cache_set \"api_response\" \"$result\"\nfi\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use Standard Locations** - Follow XDG or `$HOME/.app-name`\n2. **Initialize Early** - Call init before any operations\n3. **Handle Permissions** - Use 700 for private data\n4. **Clean Up Regularly** - Remove old temp/cache files\n5. **Rotate Logs** - Prevent unbounded growth\n\n## Resources\n\n- [XDG Base Directory Spec](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest.html)\n- [File Hierarchy Standard](https://refspecs.linuxfoundation.org/FHS_3.0/fhs/index.html)\n\n---\n\n## Version History\n\n- **1.0.0** (2026-01-14): Initial release - extracted from workspace-hub patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T13:42:52.650Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for CLI Agents requiring modular and standardized management of persistent state, configuration, and cache directories following the XDG Base Directory specification.","zh":"适用于需要模块化和标准化管理持久状态、配置和缓存目录的CLI代理，按照XDG Base Directory规范。","ja":"CLIエージェントが持続的な状態、構成、およびキャッシュディレクトリをXDG Base Directory仕様に従ってモジュラーに標準化して管理する必要がある場合に適しています。","ko":"CLI 에이전트가 지속적인 상태, 구성 및 캐시 디렉토리를 XDG Base Directory 사양에 따라 모듈화하고 표준화하여 관리하는 데 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes CLI que requieren una gestión modular y estandarizada del estado persistente, la configuración y los directorios de caché siguiendo la especificación de directorios base de XDG.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents CLI nécessitant une gestion modulaire et standardisée de l''état persistant, de la configuration et des répertoires de cache suivant la spécification des répertoires de base XDG.","de":"Ideal für CLI-Agents, die eine modulare und standardisierte Verwaltung des persistenten Zustands, der Konfiguration und der Cache-Verzeichnisse gemäß der XDG-Base-Directory-Spezifikation erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes CLI que exigem gestão modular e padronizada de estado persistente, configuração e diretórios de cache seguindo a especificação do XDG Base Directory.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов CLI, требующих модульного и стандартизированного управления постоянным состоянием, конфигурацией и кэш-директориями в соответствии со спецификацией XDG Base Directory.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) الذي يتطلب إدارة متجانسة ومتعددة الوحدات للحالة الثابتة وتفاصيل الإعداد ومجلدات الذاكرة المؤقتة حسب مواصفات دليل قاعدة XDG."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage multiple GitHub repositories with centralized configuration, leveraging bash scripts for persistent data storage, user preference handling, and performance caching via XDG-compliant directory structures.","zh":"赋予代理管理多个GitHub仓库的能力，具有集中配置，并利用bash脚本实现持久数据存储、用户首选项处理和通过XDG兼容目录结构的性能缓存。","ja":"エージェントが複数のGitHubリポジトリを中央管理された構成で管理できるようにし、bashスクリプトを使用して永続的なデータストレージ、ユーザー設定の処理、およびXDG準拠のディレクトリ構造を介したパフォーマンスキャッシングを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 여러 개의 GitHub 저장소를 중앙 집중식 구성으로 관리할 수 있도록 하며, bash 스크립트를 사용하여 지속적인 데이터 저장, 사용자 기본 설정 처리 및 XDG 호환 디렉토리 구조를 통해 성능 캐싱을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar múltiples repositorios de GitHub con una configuración centralizada, aprovechando scripts de bash para el almacenamiento de datos persistentes, el manejo de preferencias de usuario y la caché de rendimiento a través de estructuras de directorios compatibles con XDG.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer plusieurs dépôts GitHub avec une configuration centralisée, en exploitant les scripts bash pour le stockage de données persistantes, la gestion des préférences utilisateur et le cache de performances via des structures de répertoires conformes à XDG.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, mehrere GitHub-Repositorys mit einer zentralisierten Konfiguration zu verwalten, indem bash-Skripte für den persistenten Datenspeicher, die Benutzervoreinstellungsverwaltung und die Leistungs-Caching über XDG-konforme Verzeichnisstrukturen genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar vários repositórios GitHub com configuração centralizada, aproveitando scripts bash para armazenamento de dados persistentes, tratamento de preferências do usuário e cache de desempenho por meio de estruturas de diretório compatíveis com o XDG.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять несколькими репозиториями GitHub с централизованной конфигурацией, используя скрипты bash для хранения постоянных данных, обработки предпочтений пользователя и кэширования производительности через структуры директорий, соответствующие XDG.","ar":"يُمنح العميل القدرة على إدارة عدة مستودعات جيثب مع إعداد مركزي، ويستفيد من سكريبتات باش لتحويل بيانات ثابتة وتحويل تفضيلات المستخدم وتخزين أداء عبر هياكل مجلدات متوافقة مع مواصفات XDG."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating repository setup with standardized directory management","Generating modular configurations for CLI tools","Implementing cache rotation for improved performance in data-intensive scripts"],"zh":["使用标准化的目录管理自动设置仓库","为CLI工具生成模块化配置","实现缓存轮换以提高数据密集型脚本的性能"],"ja":["標準化されたディレクトリ管理を使用してリポジトリを自動設定する","CLIツール用のモジュラー構成を生成する","パフォーマンスを向上させるためにデータ集中型スクリプトのキャッシュローテーションを実装する"],"ko":["표준화된 디렉토리 관리를 사용하여 저장소를 자동 설정하는 것","CLI 도구를 위한 모듈 구성 생성","데이터 집중型 스크립트의 성능을 개선하기 위한 캐시 회전 구현"],"es":["Automatización de la configuración del repositorio con gestión de directorios estandarizados","Generación de configuraciones modulares para herramientas CLI","Implementación de la rotación de caché para mejorar el rendimiento en scripts intensivos en datos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la configuration du dépôt avec une gestion de répertoires standardisés","Génération de configurations modulaires pour les outils CLI","Mise en œuvre de la rotation de cache pour améliorer les performances dans les scripts intensifs en données"],"de":["Automatisierung der Repository-Konfiguration mit standardisierter Verzeichnisverwaltung","Erzeugung von modularen Konfigurationen für CLI-Tools","Implementierung der Cache-Rotation für verbesserte Leistung in datenintensiven Skripten"],"pt":["Automatizar configuração de repositório com gestão de diretório padronizada","Gerar configurações modulares para ferramentas CLI","Implementar rotação de cache para melhorar o desempenho em scripts intensivos de dados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать настройку репозитория с стандартизированным управлением директориями","Генерировать модульные конфигурации для инструментов CLI","Реализовать ротацию кэша для улучшения производительности в данных интенсивных скриптах"],"ar":["تأتمة إعداد المستودع بإدارة مجلدات موحدة","توليد إعدادات وحداتية لأدوات CLI","تنفيذ دورة تخزين مؤقت لتحسين الأداء في سكريبتات كثيفة البيانات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires bash script compatibility","Limited to scripts needing persistent state management","Adherence to XDG Base Directory specification may limit cross-platform compatibility"],"zh":["需要bash脚本兼容性","仅限于需要持久状态管理的脚本","遵守XDG Base Directory规范可能会限制跨平台兼容性"],"ja":["bashスクリプトの互換性が必要","永続的な状態管理が必要なスクリプトのみ","XDG Base Directory仕様に準拠することでクロスプラットフォームの互換性が制限される可能性"],"ko":["bash 스크립트 호환성이 필요함","지속적인 상태 관리가 필요한 스크립트에만 국한됨","XDG Base Directory 사양을 준수하면 크로스 플랫폼 호환성이 제한될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con scripts de bash","Limitado a scripts que necesitan gestión de estado persistente","La adherencia a la especificación de directorios base de XDG puede limitar la compatibilidad entre plataformas"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec les scripts bash","Limité aux scripts nécessitant une gestion d''état persistant","Le respect de la spécification des répertoires de base XDG peut limiter la compatibilité entre les plates-formes"],"de":["Erfordert bash-Skript-Kompatibilität","Begrenzt auf Skripte, die eine persistente Zustandsverwaltung benötigen","Die Einhaltung der XDG-Base-Directory-Spezifikation kann die Plattformübergreifende Kompatibilität einschränken"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com scripts bash","Limitado a scripts que necessitam de gestão de estado persistente","A adesão à especificação do XDG Base Directory pode limitar a compatibilidade entre plataformas"],"ru":["Требует совместимости со скриптами bash","Ограничен скриптами, требующими управления постоянным состоянием","Соблюдение спецификации XDG Base Directory может ограничить совместимость между платформами"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقاً مع سكريبتات باش","محدود بسكريبتات تحتاج إلى إدارة حالة ثابتة","الامتثال لمواصفات دليل قاعدة XDG قد يقيد التوافق بين المنصات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8f7d8b1f282e83826f6fb54180381c3bfb5f821edee1c9ae5bc11c0396de2d08","qualityScore":64}');
