ed application designed to manage accounts and processes for the Antigravity application. It provides a seamless interface for switching accounts, backing up progress, and controlling the application lifecycle."},"features":{"zh":["账户管理","进程控制","备份和恢复","Electron基础架构","支持Antigravity应用程序"],"ja":["アカウント管理","プロセス制御","バックアップと復元","Electronベースのインフラストラクチャ","Antigravityアプリケーションのサポート"],"ko":["계정 관리","프로세스 제어","백업 및 복원","Electron 기반 인프라","Antigravity 애플리케이션 지원"],"es":["Gestión de cuentas y procesos de Antigravity","Interfaz intuitiva para cambiar cuentas","Control del ciclo de vida de la aplicación","Soporte para Electron","Integración con Gemini API"],"fr":["Gestion des comptes et des processus d''Antigravity","Interface intuitive pour changer de comptes","Contrôle du cycle de vie de l''application","Support pour Electron","Intégration avec Gemini API"],"de":["Konto- und Prozessmanagement von Antigravity","Benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche zum Wechseln von Konten","Steuerung des Lebenszyklus der Anwendung","Unterstützung für Electron","Integration mit Gemini API"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de contas","Controle de processos","Interface intuitiva","Suporte à aplicação Antigravity","Desenvolvido com Electron"],"ru":["Управление учетными записями","Контроль процессов","Интуитивный интерфейс","Поддержка приложения Antigravity","Разработан на Electron"],"ar":["إدارة الحسابات","مراقبة العمليات","واجهة مستخدم سهلة","دعم تطبيق Antigravity","تم تطويره باستخدام Electron"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用openspec-bulk-archive-change","什么是Antigravity应用程序","openspec-bulk-archive-change安装","Antigravity应用程序替代品","Electron开发框架","AI智能工具下载","账户管理工具","进程控制软件"],"ja":["openspec-bulk-archive-changeの使い方","Antigravityアプリケーションとは","openspec-bulk-archive-changeのインストール","Antigravityアプリケーションの代替","Electron開発フレームワーク","AIエージェントのダウンロード","アカウント管理ツール","プロセス制御ソフト"],"ko":["openspec-bulk-archive-change 사용법","Antigravity 애플리케이션是什么","openspec-bulk-archive-change 설치","Antigravity 애플리케이션 대체","Electron 개발 프레임워크","AI 에이전트 다운로드","계정 관리 도구","프로세스 제어 소프트웨어"],"es":["herramientas de AI","gestión de cuentas","Antigravity Manager"," Electron","Gemini API","cómo usar Antigravity","alternativas a Antigravity","instalación de Antigravity"],"fr":["outils d''IA","gestion de comptes","Antigravity Manager","Electron","Gemini API","comment utiliser Antigravity","alternatives à Antigravity","installation d''Antigravity"],"de":["KI-Tools","Konto-Verwaltung","Antigravity Manager","Electron","Gemini API","wie man Antigravity verwendet","Alternativen zu Antigravity","Installation von Antigravity"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","gerenciamento de contas","controle de processos","antigravity","electron","como usar openspec-bulk-archive-change","alternativas ao openspec-bulk-archive-change","instalação do openspec-bulk-archive-change"],"ru":["инструменты ии","управление учетными записями","контроль процессов","antigravity","electron","как использовать openspec-bulk-archive-change","альтернативы openspec-bulk-archive-change","установка openspec-bulk-archive-change"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","إدارة الحسابات","مراقبة العمليات","antigravity","electron","كيفية استخدام openspec-bulk-archive-change","بديلات openspec-bulk-archive-change","تثبيت openspec-bulk-archive-change"]}},"owner":"Draculabo","repo":"AntigravityManager","repoPath":"Draculabo/AntigravityManager","stars":927,"forks":130,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T07:25:51Z","topics":["account-manager","antigravity","antigravity-ai","antigravity-ide","antigravity-tools","antigravity2api","electron","gemini","gemini-api","gemini-pro"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-bulk-archive-change","description":"Archive multiple completed changes at once. Use when archiving several parallel changes.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Archive multiple completed changes in a single operation.\n\nThis skill allows you to batch-archive changes, handling spec conflicts intelligently by checking the codebase to determine what''s actually implemented.\n\n**Input**: None required (prompts for selection)\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Get active changes**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get all active changes.\n\n   If no active changes exist, inform user and stop.\n\n2. **Prompt for change selection**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with multi-select t","body":"Archive multiple completed changes in a single operation.\n\nThis skill allows you to batch-archive changes, handling spec conflicts intelligently by checking the codebase to determine what''s actually implemented.\n\n**Input**: None required (prompts for selection)\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Get active changes**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get all active changes.\n\n   If no active changes exist, inform user and stop.\n\n2. **Prompt for change selection**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with multi-select to let user choose changes:\n   - Show each change with its schema\n   - Include an option for \"All changes\"\n   - Allow any number of selections (1+ works, 2+ is the typical use case)\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT auto-select. Always let the user choose.\n\n3. **Batch validation - gather status for all selected changes**\n\n   For each selected change, collect:\n\n   a. **Artifact status** - Run `openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json`\n   - Parse `schemaName` and `artifacts` list\n   - Note which artifacts are `done` vs other states\n\n   b. **Task completion** - Read `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`\n   - Count `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - If no tasks file exists, note as \"No tasks\"\n\n   c. **Delta specs** - Check `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/` directory\n   - List which capability specs exist\n   - For each, extract requirement names (lines matching `### Requirement: <name>`)\n\n4. **Detect spec conflicts**\n\n   Build a map of `capability -> [changes that touch it]`:\n\n   ```\n   auth -> [change-a, change-b]  <- CONFLICT (2+ changes)\n   api  -> [change-c]            <- OK (only 1 change)\n   ```\n\n   A conflict exists when 2+ selected changes have delta specs for the same capability.\n\n5. **Resolve conflicts agentically**\n\n   **For each conflict**, investigate the codebase:\n\n   a. **Read the delta specs** from each conflicting change to understand what each claims to add/modify\n\n   b. **Search the codebase** for implementation evidence:\n   - Look for code implementing requirements from each delta spec\n   - Check for related files, functions, or tests\n\n   c. **Determine resolution**:\n   - If only one change is actually implemented -> sync that one''s specs\n   - If both implemented -> apply in chronological order (older first, newer overwrites)\n   - If neither implemented -> skip spec sync, warn user\n\n   d. **Record resolution** for each conflict:\n   - Which change''s specs to apply\n   - In what order (if both)\n   - Rationale (what was found in codebase)\n\n6. **Show consolidated status table**\n\n   Display a table summarizing all changes:\n\n   ```\n   | Change               | Artifacts | Tasks | Specs   | Conflicts | Status |\n   |---------------------|-----------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|\n   | schema-management   | Done      | 5/5   | 2 delta | None      | Ready  |\n   | project-config      | Done      | 3/3   | 1 delta | None      | Ready  |\n   | add-oauth           | Done      | 4/4   | 1 delta | auth (!)  | Ready* |\n   | add-verify-skill    | 1 left    | 2/5   | None    | None      | Warn   |\n   ```\n\n   For conflicts, show the resolution:\n\n   ```\n   * Conflict resolution:\n     - auth spec: Will apply add-oauth then add-jwt (both implemented, chronological order)\n   ```\n\n   For incomplete changes, show warnings:\n\n   ```\n   Warnings:\n   - add-verify-skill: 1 incomplete artifact, 3 incomplete tasks\n   ```\n\n7. **Confirm batch operation**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with a single confirmation:\n   - \"Archive N changes?\" with options based on status\n   - Options might include:\n     - \"Archive all N changes\"\n     - \"Archive only N ready changes (skip incomplete)\"\n     - \"Cancel\"\n\n   If there are incomplete changes, make clear they''ll be archived with warnings.\n\n8. **Execute archive for each confirmed change**\n\n   Process changes in the determined order (respecting conflict resolution):\n\n   a. **Sync specs** if delta specs exist:\n   - Use the openspec-sync-specs approach (agent-driven intelligent merge)\n   - For conflicts, apply in resolved order\n   - Track if sync was done\n\n   b. **Perform the archive**:\n\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p openspec/changes/archive\n   mv openspec/changes/<name> openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n   ```\n\n   c. **Track outcome** for each change:\n   - Success: archived successfully\n   - Failed: error during archive (record error)\n   - Skipped: user chose not to archive (if applicable)\n\n9. **Display summary**\n\n   Show final results:\n\n   ```\n   ## Bulk Archive Complete\n\n   Archived 3 changes:\n   - schema-management-cli -> archive/2026-01-19-schema-management-cli/\n   - project-config -> archive/2026-01-19-project-config/\n   - add-oauth -> archive/2026-01-19-add-oauth/\n\n   Skipped 1 change:\n   - add-verify-skill (user chose not to archive incomplete)\n\n   Spec sync summary:\n   - 4 delta specs synced to main specs\n   - 1 conflict resolved (auth: applied both in chronological order)\n   ```\n\n   If any failures:\n\n   ```\n   Failed 1 change:\n   - some-change: Archive directory already exists\n   ```\n\n**Conflict Resolution Examples**\n\nExample 1: Only one implemented\n\n```\nConflict: specs/auth/spec.md touched by [add-oauth, add-jwt]\n\nChecking add-oauth:\n- Delta adds \"OAuth Provider Integration\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/auth/oauth.ts implementing OAuth flow\n\nChecking add-jwt:\n- Delta adds \"JWT Token Handling\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... no JWT implementation found\n\nResolution: Only add-oauth is implemented. Will sync add-oauth specs only.\n```\n\nExample 2: Both implemented\n\n```\nConflict: specs/api/spec.md touched by [add-rest-api, add-graphql]\n\nChecking add-rest-api (created 2026-01-10):\n- Delta adds \"REST Endpoints\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/api/rest.ts\n\nChecking add-graphql (created 2026-01-15):\n- Delta adds \"GraphQL Schema\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/api/graphql.ts\n\nResolution: Both implemented. Will apply add-rest-api specs first,\nthen add-graphql specs (chronological order, newer takes precedence).\n```\n\n**Output On Success**\n\n```\n## Bulk Archive Complete\n\nArchived N changes:\n- <change-1> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-1>/\n- <change-2> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-2>/\n\nSpec sync summary:\n- N delta specs synced to main specs\n- No conflicts (or: M conflicts resolved)\n```\n\n**Output On Partial Success**\n\n```\n## Bulk Archive Complete (partial)\n\nArchived N changes:\n- <change-1> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-1>/\n\nSkipped M changes:\n- <change-2> (user chose not to archive incomplete)\n\nFailed K changes:\n- <change-3>: Archive directory already exists\n```\n\n**Output When No Changes**\n\n```\n## No Changes to Archive\n\nNo active changes found. Use `/opsx:new` to create a new change.\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n\n- Allow any number of changes (1+ is fine, 2+ is the typical use case)\n- Always prompt for selection, never auto-select\n- Detect spec conflicts early and resolve by checking codebase\n- When both changes are implemented, apply specs in chronological order\n- Skip spec sync only when implementation is missing (warn user)\n- Show clear per-change status before confirming\n- Use single confirmation for entire batch\n- Track and report all outcomes (success/skip/fail)\n- Preserve .openspec.yaml when moving to archive\n- Archive directory target uses current date: YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n- If archive target exists, fail that change but continue with others\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:27:19.609Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring efficient change management and batch archiving capabilities in Electron-based applications","zh":"适用于需要高效变更管理和批量归档功能的Electron-based应用程序的开发代理","ja":"Electronベースのアプリケーションで効率的な変更管理とバッチアーカイブ機能を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"효율적인 변경 관리 및 일괄 아카이브 기능이 필요한 Electron 기반 애플리케이션 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que requieren un manejo de cambios eficiente y capacidades de archivado por lotes en aplicaciones basadas en Electron","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion de changement efficace et des capacités d''archivage par lot dans les applications basées sur Electron","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine effiziente Änderungsverwaltung und Batch-Archivierungsfunktionen in Electron-basierten Anwendungen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem gerenciamento de alterações eficiente e capacidades de arquivamento em lote em aplicações baseadas em Electron","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих эффективного управления изменениями и пакетного архивирования в приложениях на основе Electron","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يتطلب إدارة تغييرات فعالة وقدرات أرشفة مجزأة في التطبيقات المستندة إلى Electron"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to intelligently handle spec conflicts by checking the codebase, providing a seamless interface for archiving multiple completed changes in a single operation using the `openspec list --json` command and the AskUserQuestion tool with multi-select functionality","zh":"赋予代理智能处理规范冲突的能力，通过检查代码库，提供一个无缝的界面来使用`openspec list --json`命令和AskUserQuestion工具的多选功能来一次性归档多个已完成的更改","ja":"エージェントに、コードベースをチェックして、`openspec list --json`コマンドとAskUserQuestionツールのマルチセレクト機能を使用して複数の完了した変更を一括でアーカイブするためのシームレスなインターフェイスを提供することで、仕様のコンフリクトを智能的に処理する能力を付与する","ko":"에이전트가 코드베이스를 검사하고 `openspec list --json` 명령과 AskUserQuestion 도구의 멀티 선택 기능을 사용하여 여러 개의 완료된 변경 사항을 한 번에 아카이브할 수 있는 무결점 인터페이스를 제공함으로써 에이전트가 사양 충돌을 지능적으로 처리할 수 있는 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar inteligentemente conflictos de especificaciones verificando la base de código, proporcionando una interfaz sin problemas para archivar múltiples cambios completados en una sola operación utilizando el comando `openspec list --json` y la herramienta AskUserQuestion con funcionalidad de selección múltiple","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer de manière intelligente les conflits de spécifications en vérifiant la base de code, en fournissant une interface transparente pour archiver plusieurs changements complets en une seule opération en utilisant la commande `openspec list --json` et l''outil AskUserQuestion avec une fonctionnalité de sélection multiple","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, Spezifikationskonflikte intelligent zu handhaben, indem es den Codebestand überprüft, eine nahtlose Schnittstelle für das Archivieren mehrerer abgeschlossener Änderungen in einem einzigen Vorgang mit dem Befehl `openspec list --json` und dem Tool AskUserQuestion mit Multi-Auswahlfunktion bietet","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidar inteligentemente com conflitos de especificações, verificando a base de código, fornecendo uma interface sem interrupções para arquivar várias alterações concluídas em uma única operação usando o comando `openspec list --json` e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion com funcionalidade de seleção múltipla","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью интеллектуально обрабатывать конфликты спецификаций, проверяя кодовую базу, обеспечивая бесперебойный интерфейс для архивирования нескольких завершенных изменений в одной операции с помощью команды `openspec list --json` и инструмента AskUserQuestion с функцией многообразного выбора","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من التعامل بذكاء مع تضارب المواصفات من خلال فحص قاعدة الشفرة، وتوفير واجهة بدون انقطاع لأرشفة التغييرات المكتملة المتعددة في عملية واحدة باستخدام الأمر `openspec list --json` وأداة AskUserQuestion مع وظيفة تحديد متعدد"},"useCases":{"en":["Batch-archiving completed changes","Automating change management workflows","Resolving spec conflicts in Electron applications"],"zh":["