Datalog","ما هي Datalog","Datalog مقابل Datomic","بديلات Datalog","تثبيت Datalog","دليل إعداد Datalog","تطوير التطبيقات مع Datalog","دمج Datalog في المشاريع"]}},"owner":"wbrown","repo":"janus-datalog","repoPath":"wbrown/janus-datalog","stars":35,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T03:11:48Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"datalog","description":">","bodyPreview":"# Datalog Query\n\nQuery janus-datalog databases for debugging and data exploration.\n\nThe user will provide a database path and describe what they want to know. Use the `datalog` CLI to run queries against the database.\n\n## Data Model\n\njanus-datalog is a **Datomic-style EAV (Entity-Attribute-Value) store**. All data is stored as datoms: `[entity attribute value tx]`. There are no tables — entities are just collections of attribute-value pairs, connected by shared entity IDs.\n\nAttributes follow a n","body":"# Datalog Query\n\nQuery janus-datalog databases for debugging and data exploration.\n\nThe user will provide a database path and describe what they want to know. Use the `datalog` CLI to run queries against the database.\n\n## Data Model\n\njanus-datalog is a **Datomic-style EAV (Entity-Attribute-Value) store**. All data is stored as datoms: `[entity attribute value tx]`. There are no tables — entities are just collections of attribute-value pairs, connected by shared entity IDs.\n\nAttributes follow a namespaced keyword convention: `:namespace/name` (e.g., `:person/name`, `:order/total`). This means attributes cluster by namespace, which is useful when exploring unknown databases.\n\n**Storage is CRDT-backed** (Conflict-free Replicated Data Types). Every write is preserved with a unique ElementID. Attribute cardinality determines conflict resolution:\n\n| Cardinality | Behavior | Example |\n|-------------|----------|---------|\n| One | Last-Writer-Wins — only the latest value is returned by default | `:person/name`, `:person/age` |\n| Many | Add-Wins Set — all distinct values are returned | `:person/tag`, `:person/role` |\n| Vector | RGA — ordered list with deterministic merge | `:product/tags`, `:playlist/songs` |\n\nBecause all writes are preserved, you can time-travel: `db.History()` returns all raw datoms (no CRDT resolution), and `db.AsOf(elementID)` queries CRDT-resolved state as of a specific transaction.\n\n## Tool\n\nBinary: `~/go/bin/datalog`\n\nInstall if missing:\n```bash\ngo install github.com/wbrown/janus-datalog/cmd/datalog@latest\n```\n\n## Invocation\n\n```bash\n# Run a query\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query ''<EDN query>''\n\n# With input bindings (repeatable, one per :in parameter after $)\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query ''<EDN query with :in>'' -in ''<EDN value>'' [-in ''<EDN value>'' ...]\n\n# With performance annotations\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -verbose -query ''<EDN query>''\n\n# Export entire database to readable EDN (useful for small DBs)\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -export <output.edn>\n```\n\nOutput is a markdown table. Errors go to stderr.\n\nIf the user says `/datalog <path>`, treat `$ARGUMENTS` as the database path. Start by discovering what''s in the database, then ask what they want to explore.\n\n## Finding Databases\n\n- Prebuilt benchmark DB: `datalog/storage/testdata/ohlc_benchmark.db`\n- Default path when unspecified: `datalog.db` in current directory\n- Test databases are created in temp directories by tests (look for `t.TempDir()` calls)\n- Ask the user if the path is unclear\n\n## EDN Query Syntax\n\nQueries are EDN vectors. The basic form:\n\n```clojure\n[:find <find-spec>\n :in <input-spec>       ;; optional, $ is implicit\n :where <clauses>]\n```\n\n### Find Spec\n\n```clojure\n;; Return specific variables\n[:find ?name ?age :where ...]\n\n;; With aggregations (non-aggregated vars become group-by keys)\n[:find ?dept (sum ?salary) (count ?e) :where ...]\n\n;; Available: sum, count, avg, min, max\n```\n\n### Where Clauses\n\n**Data patterns** — match entity-attribute-value triples:\n```clojure\n[?entity :attribute ?value]          ;; basic pattern\n[?entity :attribute \"literal\"]       ;; match literal value\n[?entity :attribute _]               ;; wildcard (attribute exists)\n[?entity :attribute ?value ?tx]      ;; with transaction ID\n```\n\n**Predicates** — filter results:\n```clojure\n[(> ?age 25)]\n[(< ?price 100.0)]\n[(!= ?name \"Alice\")]\n[(< 0 ?x 100)]          ;; chained: 0 < ?x < 100\n```\n\n**Expressions** — compute values:\n```clojure\n[(+ ?age 5) ?future-age]\n[(- ?price ?discount) ?net]\n[(* ?qty ?price) ?total]\n[(str ?first \" \" ?last) ?fullname]\n[(ground 42) ?answer]\n[(identity ?x) ?y]                       ;; pass-through binding\n```\n\n**Time extraction** — extract components from `time.Time` values:\n```clojure\n[(year ?timestamp) ?y]\n[(month ?timestamp) ?m]\n[(day ?timestamp) ?d]\n[(hour ?timestamp) ?h]\n[(minute ?timestamp) ?min]\n[(second ?timestamp) ?sec]\n```\n\n**NOT clauses** — exclude matches:\n```clojure\n(not [?p :person/deleted true])\n(not-join [?p]\n  [?p :person/status \"inactive\"])\n```\n\n**OR clauses** — alternative patterns:\n```clojure\n(or [?p :person/city \"New York\"]\n    [?p :person/city \"Boston\"])\n(or-join [?p]\n  [?p :role/admin true]\n  [?p :role/superuser true])\n```\n\n**Vector functions** — operate on cardinality-vector attributes:\n```clojure\n[(nth ?vec 0) ?first-element]           ;; get element by index\n[(first ?vec) ?head]                     ;; first element\n[(last ?vec) ?tail]                      ;; last element\n[(length ?vec) ?len]                     ;; number of elements\n[(contains? ?vec \"value\") ?found]        ;; boolean membership test\n[(index-of ?vec \"value\") ?pos]           ;; index of first match\n[(subvec ?vec 1 3) ?slice]               ;; sub-vector [start, end)\n```\n\n**`enumerate`** — expands a vector into one tuple per element with index. This is the primary way to query vector contents:\n```clojure\n;; Given :product/tags is a vector [\"electronics\" \"sale\" \"new\"]\n[:find ?tag ?idx\n :where [?e :product/label \"Widget\"]\n        [?e :product/tags ?vec]\n        [(enumerate ?vec) [?idx ?tag]]]\n;; Returns: [0 \"electronics\"], [1 \"sale\"], [2 \"new\"]\n```\n\nImportant: `enumerate` produces **multiple output tuples** from a single input tuple. The binding `[?idx ?tag]` is required — it destructures each element into an index and value. The data pattern that binds `?vec` must appear **before** the enumerate expression in the where clause, and the planner must not reorder it ahead of the pattern that provides the vector.\n\n**Database functions:**\n```clojure\n[(get-else $ ?e :person/nickname \"unknown\") ?nick]\n[(missing? $ ?e :person/email)]\n[(get-some $ ?e :person/nick :person/name :person/email) ?display]\n```\n\n**Subqueries** — nested queries that bind results into the outer query:\n```clojure\n;; Tuple binding — subquery returns one tuple, binds to variables\n[(q [:find (max ?h)\n     :in $ ?sym\n     :where [?p :price/symbol ?sym]\n            [?p :price/high ?h]]\n    $ ?s) [[?max-high]]]\n\n;; Relation binding — subquery returns multiple tuples\n[(q [:find ?p ?h\n     :in $ ?sym\n     :where [?p :price/symbol ?sym]\n            [?p :price/high ?h]]\n    $ ?s) [[?price ?high] ...]]\n```\n\nThe subquery `(q [...] $ ?var1 ?var2)` takes a full query, then lists the inputs to pass (matching the subquery''s `:in` clause). The binding after `)` determines how results are captured: `[[?x]]` for a single tuple, `[[?x ?y] ...]` for multiple tuples.\n\n**Tagged literals** — use typed constants directly in patterns and predicates:\n```clojure\n[#identity \"L85hash...\" :person/name ?name]   ;; match specific entity\n[?e :event/date #inst \"2024-06-15T10:30:00Z\"] ;; match timestamp\n[(> ?d #inst \"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\")]          ;; compare against timestamp\n```\n\n### Input Parameters\n\n```clojure\n;; Scalar input\n[:find ?name :in $ ?target-age\n :where [?p :person/age ?target-age]\n        [?p :person/name ?name]]\n\n;; Collection input\n[:find ?name :in $ [?city ...]\n :where [?p :person/city ?city]\n        [?p :person/name ?name]]\n```\n\nPass `:in` values with the `-in` flag (one per binding, order matches `:in` after `$`):\n\n```bash\n# Scalar input\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> \\\n  -query ''[:find ?name :in $ ?age :where [?p :person/age ?age] [?p :person/name ?name]]'' \\\n  -in 30\n\n# String input (quote in EDN)\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> \\\n  -query ''[:find ?age :in $ ?name :where [?p :person/name ?name] [?p :person/age ?age]]'' \\\n  -in ''\"Alice\"''\n\n# Collection input\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> \\\n  -query ''[:find ?name :in $ [?city ...] :where [?p :person/city ?city] [?p :person/name ?name]]'' \\\n  -in ''[\"New York\" \"Boston\"]''\n\n# Multiple inputs\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> \\\n  -query ''[:find ?name :in $ ?min ?max :where [?p :person/age ?a] [(>= ?a ?min)] [(<= ?a ?max)] [?p :person/name ?name]]'' \\\n  -in 20 -in 30\n```\n\nEach `-in` value is parsed as EDN, so tagged literals work too: `-in ''#inst \"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\"''`.\n\n### Order By\n\n```clojure\n[:find ?name ?age\n :order-by [?age :desc] [?name :asc]\n :where [?p :person/name ?name]\n        [?p :person/age ?age]]\n```\n\n### Time-Travel\n\n```go\n// Open a database\nd, _ := db.Open(\"path/to/db\")\n\n// History — all raw datoms, no CRDT resolution\nhist := d.History()\nhist.Query(`[:find ?name ?tx :where [?p :person/name ?name ?tx]]`)\n\n// As-of — CRDT-resolved state at a specific transaction\ntxID, _ := tx.Commit()  // returns datalog.ElementID\nasOf := d.AsOf(txID)\nasOf.Query(`[:find ?name :where [?p :person/name ?name]]`)\n```\n\n## Common Debugging Patterns\n\n### 1. Explore an unknown database\n\nStart by discovering the schema shape:\n\n```bash\n# What attributes exist?\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query ''[:find ?a :where [_ ?a _]]''\n\n# How many entities per attribute?\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query ''[:find ?a (count ?e) :where [?e ?a _]]''\n```\n\nThen sample values for attributes that look interesting:\n\n```bash\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query ''[:find ?v :where [_ :person/status ?v]]''\n```\n\n### 2. Inspect an entity through a known value\n\nDon''t query for entity IDs and copy them. Instead, join through a known value to see everything about an entity:\n\n```bash\n# All attributes and values for the entity named \"Alice\"\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?a ?v :where [?e :person/name \"Alice\"] [?e ?a ?v]]''\n```\n\nThis works for any attribute — find the entity through something you know, then fan out:\n\n```bash\n# Everything about the order with ID \"ORD-1234\"\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?a ?v :where [?e :order/id \"ORD-1234\"] [?e ?a ?v]]''\n```\n\n### 3. Follow references\n\nEntities reference other entities. Use variable joins to traverse:\n\n```bash\n# Who are Alice''s friends, and what cities do they live in?\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?friend-name ?city\n    :where [?p :person/name \"Alice\"]\n           [?p :person/friend ?f]\n           [?f :person/name ?friend-name]\n           [?f :person/city ?city]]''\n```\n\nChain as many hops as needed — each shared variable (`?f` above) is a join.\n\n### 4. Find missing or unexpected data\n\n```bash\n# People without an email\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?name\n    :where [?p :person/name ?name]\n           (not [?p :person/email _])]''\n\n# People in neither New York nor Boston\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?name ?city\n    :where [?p :person/name ?name]\n           [?p :person/city ?city]\n           [(!= ?city \"New York\")]\n           [(!= ?city \"Boston\")]]''\n```\n\n### 5. Aggregate to find outliers\n\n```bash\n# Which cities have the most people?\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?city (count ?p)\n    :where [?p :person/city ?city]]''\n\n# Average age by city\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -query \\\n  ''[:find ?city (avg ?age)\n    :where [?p :person/city ?city]\n           [?p :person/age ?age]]''\n```\n\n### 6. For small databases, just export\n\n```bash\n~/go/bin/datalog -db <path> -export dump.edn\n```\n\nExport format is one datom per line: `[#identity \"hash\" :attribute value txid]`\n\n## Output Format\n\nResults are printed as markdown tables:\n\n```\n| ?name   | ?age |\n|---------|------|\n| Alice   |   30 |\n| Bob     |   25 |\n| Charlie |   35 |\n\n_3 tuples (1.234ms)_\n```\n\nWith `-verbose`, stderr gets annotation events showing index selection, join stats, and timing.\n\n## Entity Identity\n\nEntities are identified by an **Identity** — a SHA1 hash of a seed string, displayed as a 25-character L85-encoded string (a sort-order-preserving Base85 encoding).\n\nWhen you query for an entity variable like `?e`, the result symbol shows the L85 hash. You don''t normally need to use these directly — join through known attribute values instead (see debugging patterns above).\n\nThe `#identity \"L85hash\"` tagged literal exists for cases where you have a hash from logs or export output and need to look it up directly. This is the exception, not the normal workflow.\n\n## Notes\n\n- All attribute names are keywords starting with `:` (e.g., `:person/name`)\n- Integer literals are int64, float literals are float64\n- String literals use double quotes: `\"value\"`\n- The `_` wildcard matches any value without binding\n- Empty results return a table with headers but no tuples\n- Tagged literals: `#identity \"L85...\"`, `#inst \"RFC3339...\"`, `#bytes \"L85...\"`"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:31:13.831Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced Datalog query capabilities for EAV data models.","zh":"非常适合需要高级Datalog查询功能的数据分析代理，特别是那些使用EAV数据模型的代理。","ja":"EAVデータモデルを使用するデータ分析エージェントが高度なDatalogクエリ機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"EAV 데이터 모델을 사용하는 데이터 분석 에이전트가 고급 Datalog 쿼리 기능을 필요로 할 때 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades de consulta de Datalog avanzadas para modelos de datos EAV.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Données nécessitant des capacités de requête Datalog avancées pour les modèles de données EAV.","de":"Perfekt für Datenanalyse-Agents, die erweiterte Datalog-Abfragefunktionen für EAV-Datenmodelle benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que precisam de capacidades de consulta Datalog avançadas para modelos de dados EAV.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы расширенные возможности запросов Datalog для моделей данных EAV.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى قدرات استعلام Datalog متقدمة لأنماط البيانات EAV."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to run Datalog queries against janus-datalog databases using the datalog CLI, enabling efficient data exploration and debugging with Datomic-inspired architecture and EAV (Entity-Attribute-Value) store.","zh":"赋予代理运行Datalog查询的能力，使用datalog CLI对janus-datalog数据库进行查询，从而实现高效的数据探索和调试，采用Datomic启发的架构和EAV（实体-属性-值）存储。","ja":"エージェントにDatalogクエリを実行する能力を与え、datalog CLIを使用してjanus-datalogデータベースを照会できるようにし、Datomicに触発されたアーキテクチャとEAV（エンティティ-属性-値）ストアを使用して、効率的なデータの探索とデバッグを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 Datalog 쿼리를 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 datalog CLI를 사용하여 janus-datalog 데이터베이스를 조회할 수 있게 하여, Datomic에서 영감을 받은 아키텍처와 EAV(엔티티-속성-값) 저장소를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 탐색과 디버깅을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar consultas de Datalog en bases de datos janus-datalog utilizando la CLI de datalog, lo que permite una exploración y depuración de datos eficientes con arquitectura inspirada en Datomic y almacén EAV (Entidad-Atributo-Valor).","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des requêtes Datalog sur des bases de données janus-datalog en utilisant la CLI de datalog, ce qui permet une exploration et un débogage de données efficaces avec une architecture inspirée de Datomic et un magasin EAV (Entité-Attribut-Valeur).","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Datalog-Abfragen gegen janus-datalog-Datenbanken mit der datalog-CLI auszuführen, was eine effiziente Datenerforschung und -fehlerbehebung mit einer von Datomic inspirierten Architektur und einem EAV-Speicher (Entität-Attribut-Wert) ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar consultas Datalog em bancos de dados janus-datalog usando o CLI Datalog, permitindo uma exploração eficiente de dados e depuração com arquitetura inspirada em Datomic e loja EAV (Entidade-Atributo-Valor).","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять запросы Datalog к базам данных janus-datalog с помощью CLI Datalog, обеспечивая эффективное исследование данных и отладку с архитектурой, вдохновленной Datomic, и хранилищем EAV (Сущность-Атрибут-Значение).","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تشغيل استعلامات Datalog على قواعد بيانات janus-datalog باستخدام واجهة سطر الأوامر Datalog، مما يُمكِّن من استكشاف بيانات فعال وتصحيح الأخطاء باستخدام هندسة متأثرة ب Datomic ومخزن EAV (كيان-سمة-قيمة)."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging janus-datalog databases with Datalog queries","Exploring EAV data models for entity relationships","Querying datoms for specific attribute-value pairs"],"zh":["使用Datalog查询调试janus-datalog数据库","探索EAV数据模型以发现实体关系","查询datoms以获取特定的属性-值对"],"ja":["Datalogクエリを使用してjanus-datalogデータベースをデバッグする","EAVデータモデルを探索してエンティティ関係を発見する","特定の属性-値のペアを取得するためにdatomsを照会する"],"ko":["Datalog 쿼리를 사용하여 janus-datalog 데이터베이스를 디버깅하는 것","EAV 데이터 모델을 탐색하여 엔티티 관계를 발견하는 것","특정 속성-값 쌍을 얻기 위해 datoms를 조회하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de bases de datos janus-datalog con consultas de Datalog","Exploración de modelos de datos EAV para relaciones de entidades","Consulta de datoms para pares de atributo-valor específicos"],"fr":["Débogage de bases de données janus-datalog avec des requêtes Datalog","Exploration de modèles de données EAV pour les relations d''entités","Requête de datoms pour des paires attribut-valeur spécifiques"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von janus-datalog-Datenbanken mit Datalog-Abfragen","Erforschung von EAV-Datenmodellen für Entitätsbeziehungen","Abfrage von Datoms für bestimmte Attribut-Wert-Paare"],"pt":["Depuração de bancos de dados janus-datalog com consultas Datalog","Exploração de modelos de dados EAV para relações de entidades","Consulta de datoms para pares de atributo-valor específicos"],"ru":["Отладка баз данных janus-datalog с помощью запросов Datalog","Изучение моделей данных EAV для отношений сущностей","Запрос датома для конкретных пар атрибут-значение"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء قواعد البيانات janus-datalog باستخدام استعلامات Datalog","استكشاف أنماط البيانات EAV للعلاقات بين الكيانات","استعلام Datoms لأزواج السمة-القيمة المحددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires janus-datalog database setup","Written in Golang, may require additional dependencies"],"zh":["需要janus-datalog数据库设置","使用Golang编写，可能需要额外的依赖项"],"ja":["janus-datalogデータベースの設定が必要","Golangで書かれており、追加の依存項目が必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["janus-datalog 데이터베이스 설정이 필요","Golang으로 작성되어 추가 종속성이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere configuración de base de datos janus-datalog","Escrito en Golang, puede requerir dependencias adicionales"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de base de données janus-datalog","Écrit en Golang, peut nécessiter des dépendances supplémentaires"],"de":["Benötigt janus-datalog-Datenbank-Setup","In Golang geschrieben, kann zusätzliche Abhängigkeiten erfordern"],"pt":["Requer configuração do banco de dados janus-datalog","Escrito em Golang, pode requerer dependências adicionais"],"ru":["Требует настройки базы данных janus-datalog","Написано на Golang, может требовать дополнительных зависимостей"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد قاعدة البيانات janus-datalog","مكتوب بلغة Golang، قد يتطلب تبعيات إضافية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"42b93efb0e1788f8c11f4c8a6fd42149e72110a2cc532e47e1ac742f223b4d2b","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Agents2AgentsAI/ata/babysit-pr', 'community', 'Agents2AgentsAI', 'ata', 'Agents2AgentsAI/ata', 'babysit-pr', 23, 0, 60, '2026-02-26T07:21:46Z', '2026-02-26T13:21:11.994Z', '165e7c05a4d5a7d1ba58afca15c3539f48b2b0cf0c3c251a0e644b2a1434ecf5', '{"id":"Agents2AgentsAI/ata/babysit-pr","name":"babysit-pr","description":{"zh":"babysit-pr是一种AI智能代理，能够解决工程和研究问题。它提供了一种简单易用的方式来解决复杂问题。","ja":"babysit-prは、エンジニアリングと研究の問題を解決するためのAIエージェントです。複雑な問題を解決するためのシンプルで使いやすい方法を提供します。","ko":"babysit-pr은 엔지니어링 및 연구 문제를 해결하는 AI 에이전트입니다. 복잡한 문제를 해결하는 간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 방법을 제공합니다.","es":"Los agentes de IA como babysit-pr ofrecen soluciones integrales para problemas de ingeniería y investigación","fr":"Les agents IA comme babysit-pr offrent des solutions intégrales pour les problèmes d''ingénierie et de recherche","de":"KI-Agenten wie babysit-pr bieten umfassende Lösungen für Ingenieur- und Forschungsprobleme","pt":"Os agentes de IA do babysit-pr resolvem problemas de engenharia de forma completa","ru":"ИИ агенты babysit-pr решают инженерные задачи комплексно","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي من babysit-pr لحل المشكلات الهندسية بشكل شامل","en":"AI agents for solving engineering and research problems end to end"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理babysit-pr：解决工程与研究问题","ja":"AIエージェントbabysit-pr：エンジニアリングと研究の問題解決","ko":"AI 에이전트 babysit-pr: 엔지니어링 및 연구 문제 해결","es":"Agentes de IA para solucionar problemas de ingeniería","fr":"Agents IA pour résoudre les problèmes d''ingénierie","de":"KI-Agenten für die Lösung von Ingenieurproblemen","pt":"Ferramentas de IA para Resolução de Problemas de Engenharia","ru":"ИИ Агенты для решения инженерных задач","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لحل المشكلات الهندسية","en":"babysit-pr"},"description":{"zh":"babysit-pr是一种AI智能代理，能够解决工程和研究问题。它提供了一种简单易用的方式来解决复杂问题。","ja":"babysit-prは、エンジニアリングと研究の問題を解決するためのAIエージェントです。複雑な問題を解決するためのシンプルで使いやすい方法を提供します。","ko":"babysit-pr은 엔지니어링 및 연구 문제를 해결하는 AI 에이전트입니다. 복잡한 문제를 해결하는 간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 방법을 제공합니다.","es":"Los agentes de IA como babysit-pr ofrecen soluciones integrales para problemas de ingeniería y investigación","fr":"Les agents IA comme babysit-pr offrent des solutions intégrales pour les problèmes d''ingénierie et de recherche","de":"KI-Agenten wie babysit-pr bieten umfassende Lösungen für Ingenieur- und Forschungsprobleme","pt":"Os agentes de IA do babysit-pr resolvem problemas de engenharia de forma completa","ru":"ИИ агенты babysit-pr решают инженерные задачи комплексно","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي من babysit-pr لحل المشكلات الهندسية بشكل شامل","en":"AI agents for solving engineering and research problems end to end"},"definition":{"en":"AI agents for solving engineering and research problems end to end"},"features":{"zh":["自动化问题解决","简单易用的界面","支持多种编程语言","高性能计算能力","实时数据分析"],"ja":["自動化問題解決","シンプルで使いやすいインターフェース","複数のプログラミング言語をサポート","高性能計算能力","リアルタイムデータ分析"],"ko":["자동화된 문제 해결","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 인터페이스","다중 프로그래밍 언어 지원","고성능 컴퓨팅 능력","실시간 데이터 분석"],"es":["Resolución de problemas de ingeniería y investigación","Soluciones integrales y personalizadas","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como React y Python","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI) para una mayor flexibilidad","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas y sistemas operativos"],"fr":["Résolution de problèmes d''ingénierie et de recherche","Solutions intégrales et personnalisées","Intégration avec des outils de développement comme React et Python","Interface de ligne de commande (CLI) pour une plus grande flexibilité","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes et systèmes d''exploitation"],"de":["Lösung von Ingenieur- und Forschungsproblemen","Umfassende und maßgeschneiderte Lösungen","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Python","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI) für eine größere Flexibilität","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen und Betriebssystemen"],"pt":["Resolução de problemas de engenharia de forma completa","Uso de inteligência artificial para melhorar a eficiência","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento como React e Node.js","Suporte a linguagens de programação como Python","Interface de linha de comando (CLI) para controle fácil","Agentes de IA personalizáveis para atender às necessidades específicas"],"ru":["Комплексное решение инженерных задач","Использование искусственного интеллекта для повышения эффективности","Интеграция с инструментами разработки seperti React и Node.js","Поддержка языков программирования seperti Python","Интерфейс командной строки (CLI) для простого управления","Настраиваемые ИИ агенты для удовлетворения конкретных потребностей"],"ar":["حل المشكلات الهندسية بشكل شامل","استخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الكفاءة","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير مثل React و Node.js","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Python","واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) للتحكم السهل","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي قابلية للتخصيص لتلبيه الاحتياجات المحددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用babysit-pr","什么是AI智能代理","babysit-pr替代品","babysit-pr与其他工具的比较","babysit-pr安装","babysit-pr设置指南","AI工具","工程问题解决","研究问题解决"],"ja":["babysit-prの使い方","AIエージェントとは","babysit-prの代替品","babysit-prと他のツールの比較","babysit-prのインストール","babysit-prの設定ガイド","AIツール","エンジニアリング問題解決","研究問題解決"],"ko":["babysit-pr 사용법","AI 에이전트란","babysit-pr 대체품","babysit-pr와 다른 도구의 비교","babysit-pr 설치","babysit-pr 설정 가이드","AI 도구","엔지니어링 문제 해결","연구 문제 해결"],"es":["cómo usar agentes de IA","qué es un agente de IA","alternativas a babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs otros agentes de IA","instalación de babysit-pr","guía de configuración de babysit-pr","desarrollo de soluciones de IA","herramientas de IA para ingenieros"],"fr":["comment utiliser les agents IA","qu''est-ce qu''un agent IA","alternatives à babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs d''autres agents IA","installation de babysit-pr","guide de configuration de babysit-pr","développement de solutions d''IA","outils d''IA pour les ingénieurs"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs andere KI-Agenten","Installation von babysit-pr","Konfigurationsanleitung für babysit-pr","Entwicklung von KI-Lösungen","KI-Tools für Ingenieure"],"pt":["como usar agentes de IA","o que é agente de IA","ferramentas de IA para engenharia","babysit-pr alternative","babysit-pr vs outros","instalar babysit-pr","guia de configuração do babysit-pr"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ агенты","что такое ИИ агент","инструменты ИИ для инженерии","альтернативы babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs другие","установка babysit-pr","руководство по настройке babysit-pr"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للهندسة","بديل babysit-pr","babysit-pr مقابل الآخرين","تثبيت babysit-pr","دليل إعداد babysit-pr"]}},"owner":"Agents2AgentsAI","repo":"ata","repoPath":"Agents2AgentsAI/ata","stars":23,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T07:21:46Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"babysit-pr","description":"Babysit a GitHub pull request after creation by continuously polling CI checks/workflow runs, new review comments, and mergeability state until the PR is ready to merge (or merged/closed). Diagnose failures, retry likely flaky failures up to 3 times, auto-fix/push branch-related issues when appropriate, and stop only when user help is required (for example CI infrastructure issues, exhausted flaky retries, or ambiguous/blocking situations). Use when the user asks Codex to monitor a PR, watch CI, handle review comments, or keep an eye on failures and feedback on an open PR.","bodyPreview":"# PR Babysitter\n\n## Objective\nBabysit a PR persistently until one of these terminal outcomes occurs:\n\n- The PR is merged or closed.\n- CI is successful, there are no unaddressed review comments surfaced by the watcher, required review approval is not blocking merge, and there are no potential merge conflicts (PR is mergeable / not reporting conflict risk).\n- A situation requires user help (for example CI infrastructure issues, repeated flaky failures after retry budget is exhausted, permission pr","body":"# PR Babysitter\n\n## Objective\nBabysit a PR persistently until one of these terminal outcomes occurs:\n\n- The PR is merged or closed.\n- CI is successful, there are no unaddressed review comments surfaced by the watcher, required review approval is not blocking merge, and there are no potential merge conflicts (PR is mergeable / not reporting conflict risk).\n- A situation requires user help (for example CI infrastructure issues, repeated flaky failures after retry budget is exhausted, permission problems, or ambiguity that cannot be resolved safely).\n\nDo not stop merely because a single snapshot returns `idle` while checks are still pending.\n\n## Inputs\nAccept any of the following:\n\n- No PR argument: infer the PR from the current branch (`--pr auto`)\n- PR number\n- PR URL\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n1. When the user asks to \"monitor\"/\"watch\"/\"babysit\" a PR, start with the watcher''s continuous mode (`--watch`) unless you are intentionally doing a one-shot diagnostic snapshot.\n2. Run the watcher script to snapshot PR/CI/review state (or consume each streamed snapshot from `--watch`).\n3. Inspect the `actions` list in the JSON response.\n4. If `diagnose_ci_failure` is present, inspect failed run logs and classify the failure.\n5. If the failure is likely caused by the current branch, patch code locally, commit, and push.\n6. If `process_review_comment` is present, inspect surfaced review items and decide whether to address them.\n7. If a review item is actionable and correct, patch code locally, commit, and push.\n8. If the failure is likely flaky/unrelated and `retry_failed_checks` is present, rerun failed jobs with `--retry-failed-now`.\n9. If both actionable review feedback and `retry_failed_checks` are present, prioritize review feedback first; a new commit will retrigger CI, so avoid rerunning flaky checks on the old SHA unless you intentionally defer the review change.\n10. On every loop, verify mergeability / merge-conflict status (for example via `gh pr view`) in addition to CI and review state.\n11. After any push or rerun action, immediately return to step 1 and continue polling on the updated SHA/state.\n12. If you had been using `--watch` before pausing to patch/commit/push, relaunch `--watch` yourself in the same turn immediately after the push (do not wait for the user to re-invoke the skill).\n13. Repeat polling until the PR is green + review-clean + mergeable, `stop_pr_closed` appears, or a user-help-required blocker is reached.\n14. Maintain terminal/session ownership: while babysitting is active, keep consuming watcher output in the same turn; do not leave a detached `--watch` process running and then end the turn as if monitoring were complete.\n\n## Commands\n\n### One-shot snapshot\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --once\n```\n\n### Continuous watch (JSONL)\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --watch\n```\n\n### Trigger flaky retry cycle (only when watcher indicates)\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --retry-failed-now\n```\n\n### Explicit PR target\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr <number-or-url> --once\n```\n\n## CI Failure Classification\nUse `gh` commands to inspect failed runs before deciding to rerun.\n\n- `gh run view <run-id> --json jobs,name,workflowName,conclusion,status,url,headSha`\n- `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed`\n\nPrefer treating failures as branch-related when logs point to changed code (compile/test/lint/typecheck/snapshots/static analysis in touched areas).\n\nPrefer treating failures as flaky/unrelated when logs show transient infra/external issues (timeouts, runner provisioning failures, registry/network outages, GitHub Actions infra errors).\n\nIf classification is ambiguous, perform one manual diagnosis attempt before choosing rerun.\n\nRead `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/heuristics.md` for a concise checklist.\n\n## Review Comment Handling\nThe watcher surfaces review items from:\n\n- PR issue comments\n- Inline review comments\n- Review submissions (COMMENT / APPROVED / CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nIt intentionally surfaces Codex reviewer bot feedback (for example comments/reviews from `chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`) in addition to human reviewer feedback. Most unrelated bot noise should still be ignored.\nFor safety, the watcher only auto-surfaces trusted human review authors (for example repo OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR, plus the authenticated operator) and approved review bots such as Codex.\nOn a fresh watcher state file, existing pending review feedback may be surfaced immediately (not only comments that arrive after monitoring starts). This is intentional so already-open review comments are not missed.\n\nWhen you agree with a comment and it is actionable:\n\n1. Patch code locally.\n2. Commit with `codex: address PR review feedback (#<n>)`.\n3. Push to the PR head branch.\n4. Resume watching on the new SHA immediately (do not stop after reporting the push).\n5. If monitoring was running in `--watch` mode, restart `--watch` immediately after the push in the same turn; do not wait for the user to ask again.\n\nIf you disagree or the comment is non-actionable/already addressed, record it as handled by continuing the watcher loop (the script de-duplicates surfaced items via state after surfacing them).\nIf a code review comment/thread is already marked as resolved in GitHub, treat it as non-actionable and safely ignore it unless new unresolved follow-up feedback appears.\n\n## Git Safety Rules\n\n- Work only on the PR head branch.\n- Avoid destructive git commands.\n- Do not switch branches unless necessary to recover context.\n- Before editing, check for unrelated uncommitted changes. If present, stop and ask the user.\n- After each successful fix, commit and `git push`, then re-run the watcher.\n- If you interrupted a live `--watch` session to make the fix, restart `--watch` immediately after the push in the same turn.\n- Do not run multiple concurrent `--watch` processes for the same PR/state file; keep one watcher session active and reuse it until it stops or you intentionally restart it.\n- A push is not a terminal outcome; continue the monitoring loop unless a strict stop condition is met.\n\nCommit message defaults:\n\n- `codex: fix CI failure on PR #<n>`\n- `codex: address PR review feedback (#<n>)`\n\n## Monitoring Loop Pattern\nUse this loop in a live Codex session:\n\n1. Run `--once`.\n2. Read `actions`.\n3. First check whether the PR is now merged or otherwise closed; if so, report that terminal state and stop polling immediately.\n4. Check CI summary, new review items, and mergeability/conflict status.\n5. Diagnose CI failures and classify branch-related vs flaky/unrelated.\n6. Process actionable review comments before flaky reruns when both are present; if a review fix requires a commit, push it and skip rerunning failed checks on the old SHA.\n7. Retry failed checks only when `retry_failed_checks` is present and you are not about to replace the current SHA with a review/CI fix commit.\n8. If you pushed a commit or triggered a rerun, report the action briefly and continue polling (do not stop).\n9. After a review-fix push, proactively restart continuous monitoring (`--watch`) in the same turn unless a strict stop condition has already been reached.\n10. If everything is passing, mergeable, not blocked on required review approval, and there are no unaddressed review items, report success and stop.\n11. If blocked on a user-help-required issue (infra outage, exhausted flaky retries, unclear reviewer request, permissions), report the blocker and stop.\n12. Otherwise sleep according to the polling cadence below and repeat.\n\nWhen the user explicitly asks to monitor/watch/babysit a PR, prefer `--watch` so polling continues autonomously in one command. Use repeated `--once` snapshots only for debugging, local testing, or when the user explicitly asks for a one-shot check.\nDo not stop to ask the user whether to continue polling; continue autonomously until a strict stop condition is met or the user explicitly interrupts.\nDo not hand control back to the user after a review-fix push just because a new SHA was created; restarting the watcher and re-entering the poll loop is part of the same babysitting task.\nIf a `--watch` process is still running and no strict stop condition has been reached, the babysitting task is still in progress; keep streaming/consuming watcher output instead of ending the turn.\n\n## Polling Cadence\nUse adaptive polling and continue monitoring even after CI turns green:\n\n- While CI is not green (pending/running/queued or failing): poll every 1 minute.\n- After CI turns green: start at every 1 minute, then back off exponentially when there is no change (for example 1m, 2m, 4m, 8m, 16m, 32m), capping at every 1 hour.\n- Reset the green-state polling interval back to 1 minute whenever anything changes (new commit/SHA, check status changes, new review comments, mergeability changes, review decision changes).\n- If CI stops being green again (new commit, rerun, or regression): return to 1-minute polling.\n- If any poll shows the PR is merged or otherwise closed: stop polling immediately and report the terminal state.\n\n## Stop Conditions (Strict)\nStop only when one of the following is true:\n\n- PR merged or closed (stop as soon as a poll/snapshot confirms this).\n- PR is ready to merge: CI succeeded, no surfaced unaddressed review comments, not blocked on required review approval, and no merge conflict risk.\n- User intervention is required and Codex cannot safely proceed alone.\n\nKeep polling when:\n\n- `actions` contains only `idle` but checks are still pending.\n- CI is still running/queued.\n- Review state is quiet but CI is not terminal.\n- CI is green but mergeability is unknown/pending.\n- CI is green and mergeable, but the PR is still open and you are waiting for possible new review comments or merge-conflict changes per the green-state cadence.\n- The PR is green but blocked on review approval (`REVIEW_REQUIRED` / similar); continue polling on the green-state cadence and surface any new review comments without asking for confirmation to keep watching.\n\n## Output Expectations\nProvide concise progress updates while monitoring and a final summary that includes:\n\n- During long unchanged monitoring periods, avoid emitting a full update on every poll; summarize only status changes plus occasional heartbeat updates.\n- Treat push confirmations, intermediate CI snapshots, and review-action updates as progress updates only; do not emit the final summary or end the babysitting session unless a strict stop condition is met.\n- A user request to \"monitor\" is not satisfied by a couple of sample polls; remain in the loop until a strict stop condition or an explicit user interruption.\n- A review-fix commit + push is not a completion event; immediately resume live monitoring (`--watch`) in the same turn and continue reporting progress updates.\n- When CI first transitions to all green for the current SHA, emit a one-time celebratory progress update (do not repeat it on every green poll). Preferred style: `🚀 CI is all green! 33/33 passed. Still on watch for review approval.`\n- Do not send the final summary while a watcher terminal is still running unless the watcher has emitted/confirmed a strict stop condition; otherwise continue with progress updates.\n\n- Final PR SHA\n- CI status summary\n- Mergeability / conflict status\n- Fixes pushed\n- Flaky retry cycles used\n- Remaining unresolved failures or review comments\n\n## References\n\n- Heuristics and decision tree: `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/heuristics.md`\n- GitHub CLI/API details used by the watcher: `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/github-api-notes.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T13:21:11.994Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for DevOps Automation Agents managing continuous integration and deployment pipelines.","zh":"对于管理持续集成和部署流水线的DevOps自动化Agent至关重要。","ja":"継続的インテグレーションおよびデプロイメントパイプラインを管理するDevOps Automation Agentに不可欠です。","ko":"지속적 통합 및 배포 파이프라인을 관리하는 DevOps 자동화 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los Agentes de Automatización de DevOps que gestionan pipelines de integración y despliegue continuos.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents d''automatisation DevOps gérant les pipelines d''intégration et de déploiement continus.","de":"Wesentlich für DevOps-Automatisierungsagenten, die kontinuierliche Integration- und Bereitstellungspipelines verwalten.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Automação de DevOps que gerenciam pipelines de integração e implantação contínua.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов автоматизации DevOps, которые управляют непрерывной интеграцией и развертыванием конвейеров.","ar":"ضروري للوكلاء الآليين في DevOps الذين يديرون خطوط أنابيب التكامل والنشر المستمر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Persistently monitors pull requests until terminal outcomes like merge, closure, or CI success with no unaddressed review comments. Handles flaky test retries and surfaces infrastructure issues requiring user intervention.","zh":"持续监控拉取请求，直到达到最终结果，如合并、关闭或CI成功且没有未处理的审查评论。处理不稳定的测试重试，并呈现需要用户干预的基础设施问题。","ja":"マージ、クローズ、または未対応のレビューコメントがないCI成功などの最終結果が得られるまで、プルリクエストを持続的に監視します。不安定なテストの再試行を処理し、ユーザーの介入が必要なインフラストラクチャの問題を表面化させます。","ko":"병합, 종료 또는 미처리 검토 코멘트 없이 CI 성공과 같은 최종 결과가 나올 때까지 풀 리퀘스트를 지속적으로 모니터링합니다. 불안정한 테스트 재시도를 처리하고 사용자 개입이 필요한 인프라 문제를 표면화합니다.","es":"Monitorea persistentemente las solicitudes de extracción hasta los resultados finales como la fusión, el cierre o el éxito de la integración continua sin comentarios de revisión no abordados. Maneja reintentos de pruebas defectuosas y presenta problemas de infraestructura que requieren intervención del usuario.","fr":"Surveille en permanence les demandes d''extraction jusqu''aux résultats finaux tels que la fusion, la fermeture ou la réussite de l''intégration continue sans commentaires de révision non abordés. Gère les réessais de tests instables et met en surface les problèmes d''infrastructure nécessitant une intervention utilisateur.","de":"Überwacht persistente Pull-Anfragen bis zu endgültigen Ergebnissen wie Merge, Schließung oder CI-Erfolg ohne unbehandelte Review-Kommentare. Behandelt erneute Ausführungen von fehlerhaften Tests und zeigt Infrastrukturprobleme an, die eine Benutzereingabe erfordern.","pt":"Monitora persistentemente solicitações de pull até resultados terminais, como mesclagem, fechamento ou sucesso da CI sem comentários de revisão não abordados. Lida com reexecuções de testes instáveis e revela problemas de infraestrutura que exigem intervenção do usuário.","ru":"Постоянно отслеживает запросы на включение до терминальных результатов, таких как слияние, закрытие или успех CI без необработанных комментариев к рассмотрению. Обрабатывает повторные запуски нестабильных тестов и выявляет проблемы инфраструктуры, требующие вмешательства пользователя.","ar":"يراقب بانتظام طلبات السحب حتى النتائج النهائية مثل الدمج أو الإغلاق أو نجاح CI بدون تعليقات استعراض غير معلنة. يتعامل مع إعادة التشغيل الفاشل للاختبارات غير المستقرة ويrought قضايا البنية التحتية التي تتطلب تدخل المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Monitoring CI pipeline completion","Retrying flaky test failures within budget","Surfacing unaddressed review comments","Checking PR mergeability status","Detecting CI infrastructure issues"],"zh":["监控CI流水线完成","在预算内重试不稳定的测试失败","呈现未处理的审查评论","检查PR可合并状态","检测CI基础设施问题"],"ja":["CIパイプラインの完了の監視","予算内での不安定なテスト失敗の再試行","未対応のレビューコメントの表面化","PRのマージ可能性ステータスの確認","CIインフラストラクチャ問題の検出"],"ko":["CI 파이프라인 완료 모니터링","예산 내에서 불안정한 테스트 실패 재시도","미처리 검토 코멘트 표면화","PR 병합 가능 상태 확인","CI 인프라 문제 감지"],"es":["Monitoreo de la finalización de la canalización de integración continua","Reintento de fallos de pruebas defectuosas dentro del presupuesto","Presentación de comentarios de revisión no abordados","Comprobación del estado de combinación de la solicitud de extracción","Detección de problemas de infraestructura de la integración continua"],"fr":["Surveillance de l''achèvement du pipeline d''intégration continue","Réessai des échecs de tests instables dans le budget","Mise en surface des commentaires de révision non abordés","Vérification du statut de fusion de la demande d''extraction","Détection des problèmes d''infrastructure d''intégration continue"],"de":["Überwachung der Fertigstellung der kontinuierlichen Integration-Pipeline","Erneute Ausführung von fehlerhaften Testfehlern im Budget","Darstellung unbehandelter Review-Kommentare","Prüfung des Merge-Status der Pull-Anfrage","Erkennung von Infrastrukturproblemen der kontinuierlichen Integration"],"pt":["Monitoramento da conclusão do pipeline de CI","Reexecução de falhas de testes instáveis dentro do orçamento","Revelação de comentários de revisão não abordados","Verificação do status de mesclagem do PR","Detecção de problemas de infraestrutura de CI"],"ru":["Мониторинг завершения конвейера CI","Повторный запуск нестабильных тестов в рамках бюджета","Выявление необработанных комментариев к рассмотрению","Проверка статуса слияния PR","Обнаружение проблем инфраструктуры CI"],"ar":["مراقبة إكمال خط أنابيب CI","إعادة تشغيل اختبارات فاشلة غير مستقرة في الإطار المالي"," Raises تعليقات استعراض غير معلنة","فحص حالة دمج PR","كشف مشاكل البنية التحتية ل CI"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to repository and CI systems","Limited to PR-related terminal outcomes","Depends on CI system API reliability"],"zh":["需要访问代码库和CI系统","仅限于PR相关的最终结果","依赖于CI系统API的可靠性"],"ja":["リポジトリおよびCIシステムへのアクセスが必要","PR関連の最終結果に限定される","CIシステムAPIの信頼性に依存"],"ko":["저장소 및 CI 시스템에 대한 액세스 필요","PR 관련 최종 결과로 제한됨","CI 시스템 API 신뢰성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio y a los sistemas de integración continua","Limitado a resultados finales relacionados con la solicitud de extracción","Depende de la confiabilidad de la API del sistema de integración continua"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel et aux systèmes d''intégration continue","Limité aux résultats finaux liés à la demande d''extraction","Dépend de la fiabilité de l''API du système d''intégration continue"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Repository und die kontinuierliche Integration-Systeme","Begrenzt auf endgültige Ergebnisse im Zusammenhang mit der Pull-Anfrage","Hängt von der Zuverlässigkeit der API des kontinuierlichen Integration-Systems ab"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao repositório e sistemas de CI","Limitado a resultados terminais relacionados ao PR","Depende da confiabilidade da API do sistema de CI"],"ru":["Требует доступа к репозиторию и системам CI","Ограничен результатами, связанными с PR","Зависит от надежности API системы CI"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى المستودع ونظم CI","محدود بنتائج نهائية متعلقة بالسحب","يعتمد على موثوقية واجهة برمجة تطبيقات نظام CI"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"165e7c05a4d5a7d1ba58afca15c3539f48b2b0cf0c3c251a0e644b2a1434ecf5","qualityScore":60}');
