e":["Schnelles Bereitstellen von KI-Modellen und -Agenten","Unterstützung für Datenbanken und Pipelines","Lokale und remote Implementierung","Kompatibilität mit RAG und anderen KI-Modellen","Einfache Konfiguration und Verwendung"],"pt":["Implantação rápida de modelos de IA","Suporte a implantação local e remota","Integração com bancos de dados e RAG","Otimização de pipelines para melhor desempenho","Fácil integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento existentes"],"ru":["Быстрое развертывание моделей ИИ","Поддержка локального и удаленного развертывания","Интеграция с базами данных и RAG","Оптимизация пайплайнов для лучшей производительности","Легкая интеграция с существующими инструментами разработки"],"ar":["نشر سريع لنماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم النشر المحلي والعن بُعد","التكامل مع قواعد البيانات و RAG","تحسين الأنابيب لأداء أفضل","التكامل السهل مع أدوات التطوير الحالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 fix-ci","什么是 AI 代理","fix-ci 替代品","fix-ci 安装","fix-ci 教程","AI 工具比较","fix-ci vs 其他工具","如何部署 AI 模型","fix-ci 文档"],"ja":["fix-ci の使用方法","AI エージェントとは","fix-ci の代替品","fix-ci のインストール","fix-ci チュートリアル","AI ツールの比較","fix-ci vs 他のツール","AI モデルのデプロイ方法","fix-ci ドキュメント"],"ko":["fix-ci 사용법","AI 에이전트란","fix-ci 대체품","fix-ci 설치","fix-ci 튜토리얼","AI 툴 비교","fix-ci vs 다른 툴","AI 모델 배포 방법","fix-ci 문서"],"es":["herramientas de AI","despliegue de modelos de AI","fix-ci alternative","cómo usar fix-ci","guias de instalación de fix-ci","fix-ci vs otros herramientas de AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA","déploiement de modèles d''IA","fix-ci alternative","comment utiliser fix-ci","guides d''installation de fix-ci","fix-ci vs autres outils d''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","Bereitstellung von KI-Modellen","fix-ci Alternative","wie man fix-ci verwendet","Installationsanleitungen für fix-ci","fix-ci vs andere KI-Tools"],"pt":["como usar fix-ci","o que é fix-ci","fix-ci alternative","fix-ci vs jenkins","instalar fix-ci","guia de configuração do fix-ci","desenvolvimento de ia","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать fix-ci","что такое fix-ci","fix-ci альтернатива","fix-ci vs jenkins","установить fix-ci","руководство по настройке fix-ci","разработка ии","инструменты ии для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيف استخدام fix-ci","ما هو fix-ci","fix-ci بديل","fix-ci vs jenkins","تثبيت fix-ci","دليل إعداد fix-ci","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للطورين"]}},"owner":"llama-farm","repo":"llamafarm","repoPath":"llama-farm/llamafarm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.892Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fix-ci","description":"Fetch GitHub CI failure information, analyze root causes, reproduce locally, and propose a fix plan. Use `/fix-ci` for current branch or `/fix-ci <run-id>` for a specific run.","bodyPreview":"# Fix CI Skill\n\nAutomates CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan for user approval.\n\n---\n\n## Execution Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Prerequisites Check\n\nVerify the GitHub CLI is installed and authenticated:\n\n```bash\ngh --version && gh auth status\n```\n\n**If gh is not installed:**\n- Inform user: \"GitHub CLI is required. Install with: `brew install gh`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n**If not authenticated:**\n- Inform user: \"Please a","body":"# Fix CI Skill\n\nAutomates CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan for user approval.\n\n---\n\n## Execution Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Prerequisites Check\n\nVerify the GitHub CLI is installed and authenticated:\n\n```bash\ngh --version && gh auth status\n```\n\n**If gh is not installed:**\n- Inform user: \"GitHub CLI is required. Install with: `brew install gh`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n**If not authenticated:**\n- Inform user: \"Please authenticate with: `gh auth login`\"\n- Exit gracefully\n\n### Step 2: Parse Arguments\n\nDetermine the mode based on arguments:\n\n- **No arguments** (`/fix-ci`): Fetch failures for the current branch only\n- **With run-id** (`/fix-ci <run-id>`): Fetch specific run (bypasses branch scoping)\n\n### Step 3: Fetch Failed Run\n\n**Default mode (current branch):**\n\n```bash\nBRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\ngh run list --branch \"$BRANCH\" --status failure --limit 1 --json databaseId,name,headBranch,workflowName,createdAt\n```\n\n**Specific run mode:**\n\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --json databaseId,name,headBranch,workflowName,jobs,conclusion\n```\n\n**If no failures found:**\n- Report: \"No failed runs found for branch `$BRANCH`. CI is green!\"\n- Optionally show recent successful runs:\n```bash\ngh run list --branch \"$BRANCH\" --limit 3 --json databaseId,conclusion,workflowName,createdAt\n```\n- Exit gracefully\n\n### Step 4: Get Failure Details\n\nOnce a failed run is identified, gather comprehensive details:\n\n```bash\nRUN_ID=<the-run-id>\n\n# Get failed jobs with their steps\ngh run view $RUN_ID --json jobs --jq ''.jobs[] | select(.conclusion == \"failure\") | {name, conclusion, steps: [.steps[] | select(.conclusion == \"failure\")]}''\n\n# Get failed step logs (critical for debugging)\ngh run view $RUN_ID --log-failed 2>&1 | head -500\n\n# Get verbose run info\ngh run view $RUN_ID --verbose\n```\n\n**Log handling:**\n- Truncate logs to 500 lines to avoid context overflow\n- Note to user: \"Showing first 500 lines of failed logs. Full logs available on GitHub.\"\n\n### Step 5: Download Artifacts (if available)\n\nAttempt to download any debug artifacts:\n\n```bash\n# Try common artifact names - failures are OK (not all runs have artifacts)\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"coverage\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"test-results\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\ngh run download $RUN_ID -n \"logs\" -D /tmp/ci-debug/ 2>/dev/null || true\n```\n\nIf artifacts downloaded, read them for additional context.\n\n### Step 6: Analyze Failure Type\n\nCategorize the failure based on log patterns:\n\n| Pattern | Failure Type | Root Cause Area |\n|---------|--------------|-----------------|\n| `FAIL:`, `--- FAIL`, `FAILED` | Test Failure | Specific test case |\n| `ruff check`, `ruff format` | Lint Error | Code style/formatting |\n| `ModuleNotFoundError`, `ImportError` | Import Error | Missing dependency |\n| `TypeError`, `AttributeError` | Runtime Error | Type mismatch |\n| `SyntaxError` | Syntax Error | Invalid code |\n| `AssertionError` | Assertion Failure | Test expectation mismatch |\n| `TimeoutError`, `timed out` | Timeout | Performance/hang |\n| `PermissionError`, `EACCES` | Permission Error | File/resource access |\n| `ConnectionError`, `ECONNREFUSED` | Network Error | External service |\n\nExtract key information:\n- Failed test name/file (if applicable)\n- Error message\n- Stack trace location (file:line)\n- Environment variables or config issues\n\n### Step 7: Map to Local Test Commands\n\nDetermine the appropriate local command based on the CI job:\n\n| CI Workflow/Job | Local Command |\n|-----------------|---------------|\n| `test-cli` | `cd cli && go test ./...` |\n| `test-python` (server) | `cd server && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (rag) | `cd rag && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (config) | `cd config && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `test-python` (runtime) | `cd runtimes/universal && uv run pytest -v` |\n| `lint` (python) | `uv run ruff check .` |\n| `lint` (go) | `cd cli && golangci-lint run` |\n| `type-check` | `uv run mypy .` |\n| `build-cli` | `nx build cli` |\n| `build-designer` | `cd designer && npm run build` |\n\n**For specific test failures**, narrow down the command:\n- Python: `cd <dir> && uv run pytest -v <test_file>::<test_name>`\n- Go: `cd cli && go test -v -run <TestName> ./...`\n\n### Step 8: Reproduce Locally\n\nRun the mapped local command to confirm the failure reproduces:\n\n```bash\n# Example for Python test\ncd server && uv run pytest -v tests/test_api.py::test_health_check\n```\n\n**Outcome A - Failure reproduces locally:**\n- Good! Continue to fix plan\n- Report: \"Successfully reproduced failure locally\"\n\n**Outcome B - Failure does NOT reproduce locally:**\n- Note: \"Could not reproduce locally. Possible causes:\"\n  - Flaky test (timing-dependent)\n  - Environment difference (CI has different deps/config)\n  - Race condition\n- Suggest: \"Consider re-running CI with `gh run rerun $RUN_ID`\"\n- Ask user how to proceed (investigate further or skip)\n\n### Step 9: Analyze Root Cause\n\nBased on the failure type and logs, identify:\n\n1. **What failed**: Specific test, lint rule, or build step\n2. **Why it failed**: The actual error condition\n3. **Where to fix**: File(s) and line(s) that need changes\n4. **How to fix**: Proposed changes\n\nUse available tools to explore:\n- Read the failing test file\n- Read the code being tested\n- Search for related patterns in the codebase\n- Check recent changes that might have caused the failure\n\n### Step 10: Enter Plan Mode\n\nUse `EnterPlanMode` to create a formal fix plan. The plan should include:\n\n```markdown\n# CI Fix Plan\n\n## Problem Statement\n[Summary of the CI failure from logs]\n\n## Failure Details\n- **Run ID**: <run-id>\n- **Workflow**: <workflow-name>\n- **Job**: <job-name>\n- **Error Type**: <categorized-type>\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n[Explanation of why the failure occurred]\n\n## Affected Files\n- `path/to/file1.py` (line X)\n- `path/to/file2.py` (line Y)\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Change 1: [Brief description]\n[Specific edit to make]\n\n### Change 2: [Brief description]\n[Specific edit to make]\n\n## Verification Steps\n1. Run: `<local-test-command>`\n2. Expected: All tests pass\n3. Optional: Run full test suite with `<full-suite-command>`\n\n## Notes\n- [Any caveats or considerations]\n```\n\n### Step 11: User Approval Gate\n\nPresent the plan and wait for explicit user approval:\n- User approves: Proceed to execute fixes\n- User modifies: Incorporate feedback, update plan\n- User rejects: Exit gracefully without changes\n\n**CRITICAL**: Never make code changes without user approval.\n\n### Step 12: Execute Fix (after approval only)\n\n1. Make the proposed code changes using Edit tool\n2. Run local tests to verify the fix:\n```bash\n<local-test-command>\n```\n3. Report results:\n   - Success: \"Fix verified locally. Tests pass.\"\n   - Failure: \"Fix did not resolve the issue. [details]\"\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT auto-commit changes. Leave committing to the user or `/commit-push-pr` skill.\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Scenario | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| gh CLI not installed | Direct user to install: `brew install gh` |\n| gh not authenticated | Direct user to: `gh auth login` |\n| No failures found | Report CI is green, exit gracefully |\n| Rate limit exceeded | Suggest waiting or using `gh auth refresh` |\n| Run not found | Verify run ID, suggest `gh run list` to find valid IDs |\n| Large logs (>500 lines) | Truncate, note full logs on GitHub |\n| Local reproduction fails | Note as flaky/env issue, offer re-run option |\n| Network errors | Suggest retry, check connection |\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n**On finding a failure:**\n```\nCI Failure Found\nRun: #12345 (workflow-name)\nBranch: feature-branch\nFailed Job: test-python\nError Type: Test Failure\n\nAnalyzing logs...\n[Summary of failure]\n\nReproducing locally...\n[Result]\n\nEntering plan mode to propose fix...\n```\n\n**On success (after fix):**\n```\nFix Applied\n- Modified: path/to/file.py\n- Verification: Tests pass locally\n\nNext steps:\n- Review the changes\n- Run `/commit-push-pr` to commit and push\n- CI will re-run automatically on push\n```\n\n---\n\n## Notes for the Agent\n\n1. **Always scope to current branch by default** - Users expect `/fix-ci` to fix their current work, not random failures\n2. **Truncate logs wisely** - CI logs can be huge; extract the relevant error sections\n3. **Reproduce before fixing** - Don''t propose fixes for issues that can''t be reproduced\n4. **Plan mode is mandatory** - Always use EnterPlanMode before making changes\n5. **Never auto-commit** - The user controls when changes are committed\n6. **Be specific in analysis** - Generic advice isn''t helpful; identify exact files and lines\n7. **Handle flaky tests** - If reproduction fails, acknowledge it might be flaky\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:10:15.899Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing automated CI troubleshooting and GitHub Actions failure analysis.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化 CI 故障排除和 GitHub Actions 失败分析的 DevOps Agents。","ja":"CIの自動トラブルシューティングとGitHub Actionsの障害分析を必要とするDevOps Agentsに最適です。","ko":"자동화된 CI 문제 해결 및 GitHub Actions 실패 분석이 필요한 DevOps Agents에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan una solución automatizada de depuración de CI y análisis de fallos de GitHub Actions.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin d''une solution automatisée de dépannage de CI et d''analyse des échecs de GitHub Actions.","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agenten, die eine automatisierte Lösung für die Fehlersuche von CI und die Analyse von GitHub Actions-Fehlern benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes DevOps que precisam de solução de problemas de CI automatizados e análise de falhas de GitHub Actions.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым необходима автоматизированная устранение неполадок CI и анализ сбоев GitHub Actions.","ar":"مثالي untuk وكلاء DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى تصحيح أوتوماتيكي لاختبار CI وتحليل فشل إجراءات GitHub."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate CI troubleshooting by fetching GitHub Actions failures, analyzing logs, reproducing issues locally, and creating a fix plan using GitHub CLI and authentication protocols like gh auth.","zh":"通过获取 GitHub Actions 失败信息、分析日志、在本地复现问题并使用 GitHub CLI 和 gh auth 等身份验证协议创建修复计划，使代理能够自动化 CI 故障排除。","ja":"GitHub Actionsの障害を取得し、ログを分析し、問題をローカルで再現し、GitHub CLIやgh authなどの認証プロトコルを使用して修正計画を作成することで、エージェントがCIトラブルシューティングを自動化することを可能にします。","ko":"GitHub Actions 실패를 가져오고, 로그를 분석하며, 문제를 로컬에서 재현하고, GitHub CLI 및 gh auth와 같은 인증 프로토콜을 사용하여 수정 계획을 생성함으로써 에이전트가 CI 문제 해결을 자동화할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar la depuración de CI al recuperar fallos de GitHub Actions, analizar registros, reproducir problemas de forma local y crear un plan de solución utilizando GitHub CLI y protocolos de autenticación como gh auth.","fr":"Permet aux agents de dépanner automatiquement les échecs de CI en récupérant les échecs de GitHub Actions, en analysant les journaux, en reproduisant les problèmes localement et en créant un plan de correction à l''aide de GitHub CLI et de protocoles d''authentification tels que gh auth.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, die Fehlersuche von CI zu automatisieren, indem sie GitHub Actions-Fehler abrufen, Protokolle analysieren, Probleme lokal reproduzieren und einen Behebungsplan mithilfe von GitHub CLI und Authentifizierungsprotokollen wie gh auth erstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a solução de problemas de CI, buscando falhas de GitHub Actions, analisando logs, reproduzindo problemas localmente e criando um plano de correção usando GitHub CLI e protocolos de autenticação como gh auth.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать устранение неполадок CI, получая сбои GitHub Actions, анализируя журналы, воспроизводя проблемы локально и создавая план исправления с помощью GitHub CLI и протоколов аутентификации, таких как gh auth.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تشغيل أوتوماتيكي لتصحيح اختبار CI، عن طريق الحصول على فشل إجراءات GitHub، وتحليل السجلات، وإعادة إنتاج المشاكل محليًا، وإنشاء خطة تصحيح باستخدام GitHub CLI وبروتوكولات المصادقة مثل gh auth."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating CI pipeline failure analysis","Reproducing and debugging GitHub Actions issues locally","Generating fix plans for user approval"],"zh":["自动化 CI 流水线失败分析","在本地复现和调试 GitHub Actions 问题","生成供用户批准的修复计划"],"ja":["CIパイプライン障害分析の自動化","GitHub Actionsの問題をローカルで再現およびデバッグ","ユーザー承認のための修正計画の生成"],"ko":["CI 파이프라인 실패 분석 자동화","GitHub Actions 문제를 로컬에서 재현 및 디버깅","사용자 승인을 위한 수정 계획 생성"],"es":["Automatización del análisis de fallos de la canalización de CI","Reproducción y depuración de problemas de GitHub Actions de forma local","Generación de planes de solución para la aprobación del usuario"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''analyse des échecs de pipeline de CI","Reproduction et débogage des problèmes de GitHub Actions localement","Génération de plans de correction pour l''approbation de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Automatisierung der Analyse von Fehlern in der CI-Pipeline","Reproduktion und Fehlersuche von GitHub Actions-Problemen lokal","Erstellung von Behebungsplänen für die Benutzerzustimmung"],"pt":["Automatizar análise de falha de pipeline CI","Reproduzir e depurar problemas de GitHub Actions localmente","Gerar planos de correção para aprovação do usuário"],"ru":["Автоматизировать анализ сбоев конвейера CI","Воспроизводить и отлаживать проблемы GitHub Actions локально","Генерировать планы исправления для утверждения пользователя"],"ar":["أتمتة تحليل فشل أنابيب اختبار CI","إعادة إنتاج ومعالجة مشاكل إجراءات GitHub محليًا","توليد خطط تصحيح للموافقة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub CLI installation","Needs GitHub authentication","Limited to GitHub Actions failures"],"zh":["需要安装 GitHub CLI","需要 GitHub 身份验证","仅限于 GitHub Actions 失败"],"ja":["GitHub CLIのインストールが必要","GitHub認証が必要","GitHub Actionsの障害に限定される"],"ko":["GitHub CLI 설치 필요","GitHub 인증 필요","GitHub Actions 실패로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de GitHub CLI","Necesita autenticación de GitHub","Limitado a fallos de GitHub Actions"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de GitHub CLI","Besoin d''une authentification GitHub","Limité aux échecs de GitHub Actions"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von GitHub CLI","Benötigt GitHub-Authentifizierung","Begrenzt auf GitHub Actions-Fehler"],"pt":["Requer instalação do GitHub CLI","Necessita de autenticação do GitHub","Limitado a falhas de GitHub Actions"],"ru":["Требует установки GitHub CLI","Требует аутентификации GitHub","Ограничен сбоями GitHub Actions"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت GitHub CLI","يحتاج إلى مصادقة GitHub","محدود بفشل إجراءات GitHub"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"89979bcb7209ce5f004d35dc404d5355f537896c5e90ef82e480a5041948d80a","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('manutej/categorical-meta-prompting/meta-self', 'community', 'manutej', 'categorical-meta-prompting', 'manutej/categorical-meta-prompting', 'meta-self', 0, 0, 60, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.894Z', '2026-03-02T02:10:27.762Z', '1f98417c0054c7606924c734d6cdd8587a9fe3c042fd368b7c03bb0ec3947ebe', '{"id":"manutej/categorical-meta-prompting/meta-self","name":"meta-self","description":{"zh":"meta-self是为AI元提示提供分类基础的技术，已经在Game of 24中证明其正确性和质量改进","ja":"meta-selfはAIメタプロンプティングの基礎となる技術で、Game of 24でその正しさと品質の改善を実証","ko":"meta-self는 AI 메타 프롬프트의 분류 기반을 제공하는 기술로, Game of 24에서 그 올바름과 품질 개선을 입증했습니다","es":"meta-self es una habilidad de agente de IA que proporciona fundamentos categoriales para mejorar la calidad de los prompts con comprobada corrección y mejoras medibles","fr":"meta-self est une compétence d''agent d''IA qui fournit des fondements catégoriels pour améliorer la qualité des prompts avec une correction prouvée et des améliorations mesurables","de":"meta-self ist eine Fähigkeit des KI-Agents, die kategoriale Grundlagen für die Verbesserung der Qualität von Prompts mit nachweisbarer Korrektheit und messbaren Verbesserungen bietet","pt":"O meta-self fornece fundamentos categoriais para meta-prompting de IA com provas de correção e melhorias de qualidade mensuráveis","ru":"Meta-self обеспечивает категориальные основы для meta-prompting ИИ с доказательствами правильности и измеримыми улучшениями качества","ar":"ال meta-self يوفر الأسس الفئوية لتحفيز الذكاء الاصطناعي مع الأدلة على الصحة والتحسينات القابلة للقياس","en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理meta-self","ja":"AIエージェントmeta-self","ko":"AI 에이전트 meta-self","es":"Herramientas de AI: meta-self para desarrolladores","fr":"Outils d''IA : meta-self pour les développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: meta-self für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: meta-self para melhorias de qualidade","ru":"ИИ Агенты: meta-self для улучшения качества","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: meta-self لتحسين الجودة","en":"meta-self"},"description":{"zh":"meta-self是为AI元提示提供分类基础的技术，已经在Game of 24中证明其正确性和质量改进","ja":"meta-selfはAIメタプロンプティングの基礎となる技術で、Game of 24でその正しさと品質の改善を実証","ko":"meta-self는 AI 메타 프롬프트의 분류 기반을 제공하는 기술로, Game of 24에서 그 올바름과 품질 개선을 입증했습니다","es":"meta-self es una habilidad de agente de IA que proporciona fundamentos categoriales para mejorar la calidad de los prompts con comprobada corrección y mejora...","fr":"meta-self est une compétence d''agent d''IA qui fournit des fondements catégoriels pour améliorer la qualité des prompts avec une correction prouvée et des amé...","de":"meta-self ist eine Fähigkeit des KI-Agents, die kategoriale Grundlagen für die Verbesserung der Qualität von Prompts mit nachweisbarer Korrektheit und messba...","pt":"O meta-self fornece fundamentos categoriais para meta-prompting de IA com provas de correção e melhorias de qualidade mensuráveis","ru":"Meta-self обеспечивает категориальные основы для meta-prompting ИИ с доказательствами правильности и измеримыми улучшениями качества","ar":"ال meta-self يوفر الأسس الفئوية لتحفيز الذكاء الاصطناعي مع الأدلة على الصحة والتحسينات القابلة للقياس","en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"definition":{"en":"Categorical foundations for AI meta-prompting with proven correctness and measurable quality improvements (100% on Game of 24)"},"features":{"zh":["提供AI元提示的分类基础","已经在Game of 24中证明其正确性","带来可衡量的质量改进","支持Python和Node.js开发","提供CLI接口"],"ja":["AIメタプロンプティングの基礎を提供","Game of 24でその正しさを実証","品質の改善を実現","PythonとNode.jsの開発をサポート","CLIインターフェースを提供"],"ko":["AI 메타 프롬프트의 분류 기반을 제공","Game of 24에서 그 올바름을 입증","품질 개선을 실현","Python과 Node.js 개발을 지원","CLI 인터페이스를 제공"],"es":["Fundamentos categoriales para mejorar la calidad de los prompts","Corrección comprobada y mejoras medibles","Compatibilidad con juegos de 24","Mejora de la calidad de los resultados","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Fondements catégoriels pour améliorer la qualité des prompts","Correction prouvée et améliorations mesurables","Compatibilité avec les jeux de 24","Amélioration de la qualité des résultats","Intégration avec les outils de développement"],"de":["Kategoriale Grundlagen für die Verbesserung der Qualität von Prompts","Nachweisbare Korrektheit und messbare Verbesserungen","Kompatibilität mit Spielen von 24","Verbesserung der Qualität der Ergebnisse","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Fundamentos categoriais para meta-prompting de IA","Provas de correção e melhorias de qualidade mensuráveis","100% de sucesso no Jogo de 24","Melhorias de qualidade comprovadas","Técnica de IA inovadora"],"ru":["Категориальные основы для meta-prompting ИИ","Доказательства правильности и измеримые улучшения качества","100% успеха в Игре 24","Проверенные улучшения качества","Инновационная техника ИИ"],"ar":["الأسس الفئوية لتحفيز الذكاء الاصطناعي","الأدلة على الصحة والتحسينات القابلة للقياس","100% نجاح في لعبة 24","تحسينات الجودة المثبتة","تقنية ذكاء اصطناعي مبتكرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用AI智能代理","什么是AI元提示","meta-self替代品","meta-self vs 其他AI工具","meta-self安装","meta-self设置指南","AI元提示的优点","如何提高AI元提示的质量"],"ja":["AIエージェントの使い方","AIメタプロンプティングとは","meta-selfの代替","meta-selfと他のAIツールの比較","meta-selfのインストール","meta-selfの設定ガイド","AIメタプロンプティングの利点","AIメタプロンプティングの品質を高める方法"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 사용 방법","AI 메타 프롬프트란","meta-self 대체","meta-self와 다른 AI 도구 비교","meta-self 설치","meta-self 설정 가이드","AI 메타 프롬프트의 이점","AI 메타 프롬프트의 품질을 높이는 방법"],"es":["cómo usar meta-self","qué es meta-self","herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","meta-self alternativa","meta-self vs otros agentes de IA","instalación de meta-self","guía de configuración de meta-self"],"fr":["comment utiliser meta-self","qu''est-ce que meta-self","outils d''IA pour les développeurs","alternative à meta-self","meta-self vs autres agents d''IA","installation de meta-self","guide de configuration de meta-self"],"de":["wie man meta-self verwendet","was ist meta-self","KI-Tools für Entwickler","Alternative zu meta-self","meta-self vs andere KI-Agents","Installation von meta-self","Konfigurationsanleitung für meta-self"],"pt":["como usar meta-self","o que é meta-self","ferramentas de IA","melhorias de qualidade","meta-prompting de IA","alternativas para meta-self","instalação do meta-self","guia de configuração do meta-self"],"ru":["как использовать meta-self","что такое meta-self","ИИ агенты","улучшения качества","meta-prompting ИИ","альтернативы для meta-self","установка meta-self","руководство по настройке meta-self"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام ال meta-self","ما هو ال meta-self","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسينات الجودة","تحفيز الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل لتحفيز","تثبيت ال meta-self","دليل إعداد ال meta-self"]}},"owner":"manutej","repo":"categorical-meta-prompting","repoPath":"manutej/categorical-meta-prompting","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.894Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"meta-self","description":"Master reference for categorical meta-prompting unified syntax. Contains all modifiers, operators, composition patterns, and execution protocols. Use this skill for self-reference when executing any prompt workflow, ensuring consistent syntax across all commands and skills.","bodyPreview":"# Meta-Self: Unified Categorical Syntax Reference\n\nThis skill serves as the authoritative reference for the categorical meta-prompting framework. All commands and skills should align with this specification.\n\n## Categorical Foundation\n\n```\nF: Task → Prompt        (Functor - structure-preserving transformation)\nM: Prompt →^n Prompt    (Monad - iterative refinement)\nW: History → Context    (Comonad - context extraction)\nα: F ⇒ G                (Natural Transformation - strategy switching)\nE: Eithe","body":"# Meta-Self: Unified Categorical Syntax Reference\n\nThis skill serves as the authoritative reference for the categorical meta-prompting framework. All commands and skills should align with this specification.\n\n## Categorical Foundation\n\n```\nF: Task → Prompt        (Functor - structure-preserving transformation)\nM: Prompt →^n Prompt    (Monad - iterative refinement)\nW: History → Context    (Comonad - context extraction)\nα: F ⇒ G                (Natural Transformation - strategy switching)\nE: Either Error A       (Exception Monad - error handling)\n[0,1]: Quality → Quality (Enriched - quality tracking)\n```\n\n### Categorical Laws (Must Be Satisfied)\n\n```\n1. Functor Identity:     F(id) = id\n2. Functor Composition:  F(g ∘ f) = F(g) ∘ F(f)\n3. Monad Left Identity:  return >=> f = f\n4. Monad Right Identity: f >=> return = f\n5. Monad Associativity:  (f >=> g) >=> h = f >=> (g >=> h)\n6. Comonad Left Id:      extract ∘ duplicate = id\n7. Comonad Associativity: duplicate ∘ duplicate = fmap duplicate ∘ duplicate\n8. Naturality Condition: α_B ∘ F(f) = G(f) ∘ α_A  for all f: A → B\n9. Exception Catch Id:   catch(Right(a), h) = Right(a)  (Phase 3)\n10. Exception Catch Err: catch(Left(e), h) = h(e)       (Phase 3)\n11. Exception Assoc:     Error handling preserves Kleisli associativity\n12. Quality Monotonicity: quality(A ⊗ B) ≤ min(quality(A), quality(B))\n```\n\n### Exception Monad E (Phase 3)\n\n**Type**: `Either<Error, A> = Left(Error) | Right(A)`\n\n**Operations**:\n1. **return**: `a → Right(a)` (pure success)\n2. **bind (>=>)**: Error-propagating composition\n   ```\n   m >>= f = case m of\n     Left(e) → Left(e)        -- error propagates\n     Right(a) → f(a)          -- continue on success\n   ```\n3. **catch**: Error recovery\n   ```\n   catch(m, handler) = case m of\n     Left(e) → handler(e)     -- recover from error\n     Right(a) → Right(a)      -- pass through success\n   ```\n\n**Laws**:\n- **Left Identity**: `return(a) >>= f = f(a)`\n- **Right Identity**: `m >>= return = m`\n- **Associativity**: `(m >>= f) >>= g = m >>= (λx. f(x) >>= g)`\n- **Catch Identity**: `catch(Right(a), h) = Right(a)`\n- **Catch Error**: `catch(Left(e), h) = h(e)`\n- **Catch Composition**: `catch(catch(m, h1), h2) = catch(m, λe. catch(h1(e), h2))`\n\n**In Framework**:\n- Used by `@catch:` modifier for error handling behaviors\n- Used by `@fallback:` modifier for recovery strategies\n- Integrates with `/chain` and `/rmp` commands\n- Preserves composition with existing operators (→, ||, >=>)\n\n---\n\n## Unified Modifiers\n\nAll commands support these modifiers. Place them before the task description.\n\n### @mode: - Execution Mode\n\n| Mode | Description | Effect |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| `@mode:active` | Default execution | Execute with auto-detection |\n| `@mode:iterative` | RMP loop | Iterate until @quality: met |\n| `@mode:dry-run` | Preview only | Show plan, no execution |\n| `@mode:spec` | Generate spec | Output YAML specification |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @mode:iterative \"build auth system\"`\n\n### @quality: - Quality Threshold\n\n| Format | Description | Range |\n|--------|-------------|-------|\n| `@quality:0.85` | Target threshold | 0.0 - 1.0 |\n| `@quality:85%` | Percentage form | 0% - 100% |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @quality:0.9 \"optimize algorithm\"`\n\n### @tier: - Complexity Tier\n\n| Tier | Tokens | Pattern | Strategy |\n|------|--------|---------|----------|\n| `@tier:L1` | 600-1200 | Single op | DIRECT |\n| `@tier:L2` | 1500-3000 | A → B | DIRECT |\n| `@tier:L3` | 2500-4500 | A → B → C | MULTI_APPROACH |\n| `@tier:L4` | 3000-6000 | A \\|\\| B \\|\\| C | MULTI_APPROACH |\n| `@tier:L5` | 5500-9000 | Hierarchical | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n| `@tier:L6` | 8000-12000 | Iterative | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n| `@tier:L7` | 12000-22000 | Ensemble | AUTONOMOUS_EVOLUTION |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @tier:L5 \"design microservices\"`\n\n### @budget: - Token Budget\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@budget:20000` | Total tokens |\n| `@budget:[5K,4K,6K]` | Per-agent allocation |\n| `@budget:auto` | Automatic calculation |\n\n**Example**: `/task-relay @budget:[5000,4000,6000] [R→D→I]`\n\n### @variance: - Budget Variance Threshold\n\n| Format | Description | Action |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@variance:15%` | Acceptable variance | WARN if exceeded |\n| `@variance:20%` | Default | HALT if exceeded |\n\n**Example**: `/hekat @budget:18K @variance:15% [R→D→I]`\n\n### @max_iterations: - Iteration Limit\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@max_iterations:5` | Maximum RMP iterations |\n| `@max_iterations:3` | Fewer iterations |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @quality:0.9 @max_iterations:3 \"task\"`\n\n### @catch: - Error Handling Behavior (Phase 3)\n\n| Format | Description | Result |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@catch:halt` | Stop chain on error (default) | Left(error) |\n| `@catch:log` | Log error, continue chain | Left(error) logged |\n| `@catch:retry:N` | Retry command N times | Right(result) or Left(error) |\n| `@catch:skip` | Skip failed command | Right(empty) |\n| `@catch:substitute:/alt` | Use alternative command | Right(alt_result) |\n\n**Example**: `/chain @catch:retry:3 [/api→/process] \"fetch data\"`\n\n### @fallback: - Error Recovery Strategy (Phase 3)\n\n| Format | Description | When Used |\n|--------|-------------|-----------|\n| `@fallback:return-best` | Return highest quality result | Iterative refinement |\n| `@fallback:return-last` | Return last successful result | Prefer recency |\n| `@fallback:use-default:[val]` | Use specific default | Known safe value |\n| `@fallback:empty` | Return empty/neutral | Minimal context |\n\n**Example**: `/rmp @fallback:return-best @quality:0.9 \"complex task\"`\n\n### @quality:visualize - Quality Flow Visualization (Phase 5)\n\n| Format | Description | Output |\n|--------|-------------|--------|\n| `@quality:visualize` | Show quality flow (default: bar chart) | Visual quality tracking |\n| `@quality:visualize:bar` | Bar chart format | ASCII bar chart |\n| `@quality:visualize:flow` | Flow diagram format | Arrows with quality values |\n| `@quality:visualize:detailed` | Detailed breakdown | Full quality metrics |\n| `@quality:visualize:compact` | Compact summary | Single-line summary |\n\n**Categorical Foundation**: Uses [0,1]-enriched category structure where `Hom_Q(A, B) = [0,1]` and quality tensor follows `q1 ⊗ q2 = min(q1, q2)`\n\n**Example**: `/chain @quality:visualize [/analyze→/design→/implement] \"build feature\"`\n\n### @template: - Template Components\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@template:{context:expert}` | Single component |\n| `@template:{context:X}+{mode:Y}+{format:Z}` | Combined |\n\n**Components**:\n- `{context:expert\\|teacher\\|reviewer\\|debugger}`\n- `{mode:direct\\|cot\\|multi\\|iterative}`\n- `{format:prose\\|structured\\|code\\|checklist}`\n\n**Example**: `/meta @template:{context:expert}+{mode:cot}+{format:code} \"implement\"`\n\n### @domain: - Force Domain Classification\n\n| Domain | Use Case |\n|--------|----------|\n| `@domain:ALGORITHM` | Algorithmic correctness |\n| `@domain:SECURITY` | Security review |\n| `@domain:API` | API design/review |\n| `@domain:DEBUG` | Debugging |\n| `@domain:TESTING` | Test generation |\n\n**Example**: `/meta @domain:SECURITY \"review auth code\"`\n\n### @skills: - Skill Discovery & Composition\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `@skills:discover(domain=X)` | Discover by domain |\n| `@skills:discover(relevance>0.7)` | Discover by quality |\n| `@skills:compose(A⊗B)` | Tensor composition |\n| `@skills:compose(A→B→C)` | Sequential |\n| `@skills:compose(A>=>B)` | Kleisli |\n| `@skills:skill1,skill2` | Explicit list |\n| `@skills:best(domain=X)` | Best for domain |\n\n**Example**: `/meta-command @skills:compose(api-testing⊗validation) \"create tests\"`\n\n---\n\n## Composition Operators\n\n### → (Sequence) - Kleisli Composition\n\n**Unicode**: U+2192\n**Meaning**: Output of A becomes input of B\n**Quality**: `quality(A → B) ≤ min(quality(A), quality(B))`\n\n```bash\n# Command syntax\n/chain [/debug→/review→/test] \"error in auth.py\"\n\n# Agent syntax\n[R→D→I→T] \"build feature\"\n\n# Skill syntax\n@skills:compose(research→design→implement)\n```\n\n### || (Parallel) - Concurrent Execution\n\n**Meaning**: Execute A, B, C concurrently, aggregate results\n**Quality**: `quality(A || B || C) = mean(quality(A), quality(B), quality(C))`\n\n```bash\n# Parallel commands\n/chain [/review-security || /review-performance] \"audit code\"\n\n# Parallel agents\n[R||D||A] \"evaluate options\"\n\n# Mixed\n[R→(D||F)→I] \"full-stack with parallel design\"\n```\n\n### ⊗ (Tensor) - Quality-Degrading Combination\n\n**Unicode**: U+2297\n**Meaning**: Combine capabilities, quality degrades to minimum\n**Quality**: `quality(A ⊗ B) = min(quality(A), quality(B))`\n\n```bash\n# Skill tensor\n@skills:compose(api-testing⊗jest-patterns⊗validation)\n\n# Agent tensor\n[debug-detective⊗test-engineer] \"fix and test\"\n```\n\n### >=> (Kleisli) - Monadic Refinement\n\n**Meaning**: Composition with quality-gated iteration at each stage\n**Quality**: `quality(A >=> B)` improves with each iteration\n\n```bash\n# RMP stages\n/rmp @quality:0.85 [analyze>=>design>=>implement] \"build feature\"\n\n# Each stage:\n# 1. Execute\n# 2. Assess quality\n# 3. If quality < threshold: refine\n# 4. Pass to next stage\n```\n\n---\n\n## Command Invocation Syntax\n\n### Standard Pattern\n\n```\n/<command> @modifier1:value @modifier2:value [composition] \"task description\"\n```\n\n### Examples\n\n```bash\n# Simple\n/meta \"implement rate limiter\"\n\n# With modifiers\n/meta @mode:iterative @quality:0.85 \"build API\"\n\n# With composition\n/chain [/debug→/fix→/test] \"TypeError in auth.py\"\n\n# Full syntax\n/hekat @mode:active @tier:L5 @budget:18K [R→D→(I||T)] \"build auth system\"\n\n# With skills\n/meta-command @skills:discover(domain=API) @mode:iterative \"create endpoint\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent Hotkeys (HEKAT Compatible)\n\n### Tier 1 - Single Agent\n\n| Key | Agent | Domain |\n|-----|-------|--------|\n| `[R]` | deep-researcher | Research |\n| `[D]` | api-architect | Design |\n| `[I]` | practical-programmer | Implementation |\n| `[T]` | test-engineer | Testing |\n| `[B]` | build-engineer | Build |\n| `[F]` | frontend-specialist | Frontend |\n| `[A]` | analyzer | Analysis |\n\n### Tier 2 - Ctrl Modifiers\n\n| Key | Effect |\n|-----|--------|\n| `[Ctrl+P]` | L4 Parallel mode |\n| `[Ctrl+H]` | L5 Hierarchical mode |\n| `[Ctrl+I]` | L6 Iterative mode |\n\n### Tier 3 - Agent Chains\n\n```bash\n[R→D→I]        # Research → Design → Implement\n[R→D→I→T]      # Full pipeline with testing\n[P:R||D||A]    # Parallel: Research, Design, Analyze\n[R→(D||F)→I]   # Mixed: Research, parallel Design/Frontend, Implement\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quality Assessment Structure\n\n### Multi-Dimensional Quality Vector\n\n| Dimension | Weight | Description |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| Correctness | 40% | Does it solve the problem? |\n| Clarity | 25% | Is it understandable? |\n| Completeness | 20% | Are edge cases handled? |\n| Efficiency | 15% | Is it well-designed? |\n\n### Aggregate Score\n\n```\naggregate = (0.40 × correctness) + (0.25 × clarity) +\n            (0.20 × completeness) + (0.15 × efficiency)\n```\n\n### Quality Thresholds\n\n| Score | Status | Action |\n|-------|--------|--------|\n| ≥0.9 | Excellent | Stop, success |\n| 0.8-0.9 | Good | Stop, success |\n| 0.7-0.8 | Acceptable | Continue if @mode:iterative |\n| 0.6-0.7 | Poor | Refine if iterations remain |\n| <0.6 | Failed | Abort or restructure |\n\n---\n\n## Checkpoint Format\n\nAll commands produce standardized checkpoints:\n\n```yaml\nCHECKPOINT_[type]_[n]:\n  command: /[command]\n  iteration: [n]\n  quality:\n    correctness: [0-1]\n    clarity: [0-1]\n    completeness: [0-1]\n    efficiency: [0-1]\n    aggregate: [0-1]\n  quality_delta: [+/- from previous]\n  budget:\n    used: [tokens]\n    remaining: [tokens]\n    variance: [%]\n  status: [CONTINUE | CONVERGED | MAX_ITERATIONS | HALT]\n  trend: [RAPID_IMPROVEMENT | STEADY_IMPROVEMENT | PLATEAU | DEGRADING]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Simple Task\n\n```bash\n/meta \"task\"\n```\n- Auto-detect domain, tier, template\n- Single-pass execution\n\n### Pattern 2: Quality-Gated Iteration\n\n```bash\n/rmp @quality:0.85 @max_iterations:5 \"task\"\n```\n- Iterate until quality threshold\n- Track quality improvement\n\n### Pattern 3: Multi-Stage Pipeline\n\n```bash\n/chain [/analyze→/design→/implement→/test] \"feature\"\n```\n- Sequential execution\n- Output → Input flow\n\n### Pattern 4: Parallel Exploration\n\n```bash\n/chain [/approach-a || /approach-b || /approach-c] \"evaluate options\"\n```\n- Concurrent execution\n- Aggregate results\n\n### Pattern 5: Hierarchical Orchestration\n\n```bash\n/hekat @tier:L5 [Lead→(Worker||Worker)→Synthesize] \"complex task\"\n```\n- Lead agent coordinates\n- Workers execute in parallel\n- Synthesizer combines results\n\n### Pattern 6: Skill-Driven Meta-Command\n\n```bash\n/meta-command @skills:discover(domain=API,relevance>0.7) \"create endpoint command\"\n```\n- Auto-discover relevant skills\n- Inject into command creation\n\n---\n\n## Mode Behaviors\n\n### @mode:active\n- Execute immediately\n- Auto-detect all parameters\n- Single-pass unless combined with @mode:iterative\n\n### @mode:iterative\n- Enable RMP loop\n- Iterate until @quality: threshold\n- Track quality across iterations\n\n### @mode:dry-run\n- Show execution plan\n- Do not execute\n- Exit after plan display\n\n### @mode:spec\n- Generate YAML specification\n- Do not execute\n- Exit after spec generation\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Budget Exceeded\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: HALT\nreason: \"Budget variance exceeded @variance: threshold\"\naction: \"Review agent outputs, adjust budget allocation\"\n```\n\n### Quality Plateau\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: NO_IMPROVEMENT\nreason: \"Quality improvement < 0.02 for 2 iterations\"\naction: \"Fixed-point reached, returning best result\"\n```\n\n### Max Iterations\n\n```yaml\nSTATUS: MAX_ITERATIONS\nreason: \"Reached @max_iterations: limit\"\naction: \"Return best result from iterations\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Self-Reference Protocol\n\nWhen executing any command or skill:\n\n1. **Check modifiers**: Parse all @modifier: values\n2. **Apply defaults**: Use defaults for unspecified modifiers\n3. **Validate syntax**: Ensure operators match specification\n4. **Execute**: Follow categorical laws\n5. **Checkpoint**: Output standardized checkpoint\n6. **Quality assess**: Evaluate using multi-dimensional vector\n7. **Decide**: CONTINUE, CONVERGE, or HALT based on rules\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference Quick Look\n\n### Core Categorical Commands (F, M, W, α)\n\n| Command | Categorical Role | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|------------------|---------------|\n| `/meta` | **Functor F**: Task → Prompt | @mode:, @tier:, @template:, @domain: |\n| `/rmp` | **Monad M**: Prompt →ⁿ Prompt | @quality:, @max_iterations:, @mode: |\n| `/context` | **Comonad W**: History → Context | @mode:, @focus:, @depth:, @transform: |\n| `/transform` | **Nat. Trans. α**: F ⇒ G | @from:, @to:, @verify:, @mode: |\n\n### Natural Transformation Operations (/transform)\n\n| Mode | Description | Type Signature |\n|------|-------------|----------------|\n| `@mode:transform` | Strategy switch (default) | α_A: F(A) → G(A) |\n| `@mode:compare` | Compare strategies | Show F vs G side-by-side |\n| `@mode:analyze` | Recommend optimal | Suggest best α |\n\n**Strategy Registry (Functors)**:\n- `zero-shot` (F_ZS): Direct prompt, quality ~0.65\n- `few-shot` (F_FS): Exemplar prompt, quality ~0.78\n- `chain-of-thought` (F_CoT): Reasoning prompt, quality ~0.85\n- `tree-of-thought` (F_ToT): Branching prompt, quality ~0.88\n- `meta-prompting` (F_Meta): Adaptive prompt, quality ~0.90\n\n**Aliases**:\n- `/cot` = `/transform @to:chain-of-thought`\n- `/tot` = `/transform @to:tree-of-thought`\n\n### Comonad Operations (/context)\n\n| Mode | Operation | Type Signature |\n|------|-----------|----------------|\n| `@mode:extract` | Focus on current | ε: W(A) → A |\n| `@mode:duplicate` | Meta-observation | δ: W(A) → W(W(A)) |\n| `@mode:extend` | Context-aware transform | (W(A) → B) → W(A) → W(B) |\n\n**Aliases**:\n- `/extract` = `/context @mode:extract`\n- `/focus` = `/context @mode:extract @depth:1`\n\n### Composition & Routing Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|---------|---------------|\n| `/chain` | Command composition | @mode:, @budget:, @quality:, @catch:, @fallback:, @quality:visualize |\n| `/route` | Dynamic routing | @domain: |\n| `/build-prompt` | Template assembly | @template: |\n\n### Domain Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose | Key Modifiers |\n|---------|---------|---------------|\n| `/review` | Domain-aware code review | @domain: |\n| `/debug` | Systematic debugging | @mode: |\n| `/hekat` | Agent orchestration DSL | @tier:, @budget:, @variance: |\n| `/meta-command` | Create new commands | @skills:, @mode: |\n| `/task-relay` | Multi-agent relay | @budget:, @pattern: |\n\n---\n\n## Skill Reference Quick Look\n\n| Skill | Purpose | Integration |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `categorical-meta-prompting` | Core F, M, W framework | /meta, /rmp, /context |\n| `categorical-structure-builder` | Implement any categorical structure | {prompt:categorical-structure} |\n| `recursive-meta-prompting` | RMP implementation patterns | @mode:iterative |\n| `dynamic-prompt-registry` | Prompt lookup/composition | @skills:, {prompt:} |\n| `quality-enriched-prompting` | [0,1]-enriched quality | @quality: |\n| `atomic-blocks` | Composable atomic blocks | /blocks, @block: |\n| `meta-self` | This reference | Self-reference |\n\n---\n\n## Atomic Blocks (Layer 3 Access)\n\nFor power users who need fine-grained control, the framework exposes atomic blocks that underlie all commands.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n```\nSkill: atomic-blocks\nCommand: /blocks [composition] \"task\"\n```\n\n### Available Blocks\n\n| Layer | Blocks | Purpose |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| Assessment | assess_difficulty, assess_domain, assess_quality, select_tier | Analyze and classify |\n| Transformation | select_strategy, build_template, apply_transform, execute_prompt | Transform to outputs |\n| Refinement | evaluate_convergence, extract_improvement, apply_refinement | Monad M iteration |\n| Composition | sequence (→), parallel (\\|\\|), kleisli (>=>), tensor (⊗) | Combine blocks |\n\n### Progressive Disclosure\n\n| Layer | Users | Access |\n|-------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | 90% | `/meta \"task\"` - blocks hidden |\n| 2 | 9% | `/meta @block:assess_domain:SECURITY \"task\"` - override block |\n| 3 | 1% | `/blocks [assess_difficulty → select_tier] \"task\"` - compose |\n\n**Full specification**: `skill:atomic-blocks`\n\n---\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore executing any prompt:\n\n- [ ] All modifiers use `@name:value` syntax\n- [ ] Operators match: `→`, `||`, `⊗`, `>=>`\n- [ ] Quality thresholds in [0,1] range\n- [ ] Budget values are positive integers or \"auto\"\n- [ ] Tier values are L1-L7\n- [ ] Mode values are: active, iterative, dry-run, spec\n- [ ] Composition brackets match: `[...]`\n- [ ] Task description is quoted: `\"task\"`\n\n---\n\n## Version\n\n**Specification Version**: 2.5\n**Compatibility**: 100% backward compatible\n**Foundation**: Category Theory (F, M, W, α, E, [0,1]-enriched)\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-01\n**New in 2.5**: Atomic blocks system with /blocks command, @block: overrides, progressive disclosure\n**New in 2.4**: Quality Visualization via @quality:visualize modifier (Phase 5)\n**New in 2.3**: Exception Monad E for error handling via @catch:/@fallback: modifiers\n**New in 2.2**: Natural Transformation α operations via /transform command\n**New in 2.1**: Comonad W operations via /context command\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:10:27.762Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring unified categorical syntax for meta-prompting and iterative refinement","zh":"非常适合需要统一分类语法进行元提示和迭代优化的高级AI Agent，如Claude Code和AutoGPT。","ja":"Claude CodeやAutoGPTなどの、メタプロンプトと反復的な改良のために統一されたカテゴリカル構文を必要とする高度なAIエージェントに理想的です。","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같이 메타 프롬프팅 및 반복적 개선을 위한 통합된 범주 구문이 필요한 고급 AI 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avanzados como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren una sintaxis categórica unificada para meta-prompting y refinamiento iterativo","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents IA Avancés comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant une syntaxe catégorielle unifiée pour le meta-prompting et l''affinement itératif","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine einheitliche kategorische Syntax für Meta-Prompting und iterative Verfeinerung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem sintaxe categórica unificada para meta-prompting e refinamento iterativo","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих унифицированной категориальной синтаксиса для мета-пrompting и итеративного уточнения","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذي يتطلب بناء متحد للترميز المتشابك لتحفيز وتنقية متكررة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Functor, Monad, and Comonad transformations for structure-preserving prompt generation, iterative refinement, and context extraction using natural transformations like α, enhancing overall meta-self capabilities with proven correctness and quality improvements","zh":"使Agent能够利用Functor、Monad和Comonad变换进行结构保持的提示生成、迭代优化以及使用如α等自然变换的上下文提取，通过经过验证的正确性和质量改进来增强整体元自我能力。","ja":"Functor、Monad、Comonad変換を活用して、構造を保存するプロンプト生成、反復的な改良、αなどの自然変換を用いたコンテキスト抽出を可能にし、実証された正確性と品質向上によってメタ自己能力全体を強化します。","ko":"펑터(Functor), 모나드(Monad), 코모나드(Comonad) 변환을 활용하여 구조 보존 프롬프트 생성, 반복적 개선, α와 같은 자연 변환을 사용한 컨텍스트 추출을 통해 에이전트의 능력을 강화하며, 검증된 정확성과 품질 개선으로 전체 메타-자기 능력을 향상시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar transformaciones de Functor, Monad y Comonad para la generación de prompts que preservan la estructura, el refinamiento iterativo y la extracción de contexto utilizando transformaciones naturales como α, mejorando en general las capacidades meta-propias con mejoras de corrección y calidad comprobadas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter des transformations de Functor, de Monad et de Comonad pour la génération de prompts préservant la structure, le raffinement itératif et l''extraction de contexte en utilisant des transformations naturelles comme α, améliorant ainsi les capacités meta-propres avec des améliorations de correction et de qualité prouvées","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Functor-, Monad- und Comonad-Transformationen für strukturpräservierende Promptgenerierung, iterative Verfeinerung und Kontextextraktion unter Verwendung natürlicher Transformationen wie α zu nutzen, wodurch die Meta-Selbstfähigkeiten im Allgemeinen mit nachgewiesenen Korrektheits- und Qualitätsverbesserungen verbessert werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a utilizarem transformações de Functor, Monad e Comonad para geração de prompts que preservam a estrutura, refinamento iterativo e extração de contexto usando transformações naturais como α, melhorando as capacidades de auto-metas comprovadas de correção e melhoria da qualidade","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать преобразования Functor, Monad и Comonad для генерации подсказок, сохраняющих структуру, итеративного уточнения и извлечения контекста с использованием естественных преобразований, таких как α, повышая возможности мета-самосовершенствования с доказанной корректностью и улучшением качества","ar":"يمكن للعميل الاستفادة من تحويلات Functor و Monad و Comonad لتوليد التحفيزات التي تحافظ على الهيكل والتنقية المتكررة واستخراج السياق باستخدام التحويلات الطبيعية مثل α، وتحسين القدرات الذاتية للمتاس مع تحسينات جودة وموثوقية مثبتة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating categorical meta-prompting for complex tasks","Generating iterative refinements for prompt optimization","Debugging meta-self inconsistencies using natural transformations"],"zh":["自动化复杂任务的分类元提示","生成用于提示优化的迭代改进","使用自然变换调试元自我不一致性"],"ja":["複雑なタスクのためのカテゴリカルメタプロンプトの自動化","プロンプト最適化のための反復的な改良の生成","自然変換を用いたメタ自己の不整合のデバッグ"],"ko":["복잡한 작업을 위한 범주형 메타 프롬프팅 자동화","프롬프트 최적화를 위한 반복적 개선 생성","자연 변환을 사용한 메타-자기 불일치 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar el meta-prompting categórico para tareas complejas","Generar refinamientos iterativos para la optimización de prompts","Depurar inconsistencias meta-propias utilizando transformaciones naturales"],"fr":["Automatiser le meta-prompting catégoriel pour les tâches complexes","Générer des affinements itératifs pour l''optimisation des prompts","Déboguer les incohérences meta-propres en utilisant des transformations naturelles"],"de":["Automatisieren des kategorischen Meta-Prompting für komplexe Aufgaben","Generieren von iterativen Verfeinerungen für die Optimierung von Prompts","Fehlerbehebung von Meta-Selbstinkonsistenzen unter Verwendung natürlicher Transformationen"],"pt":["Automatizar o meta-prompting categórico para tarefas complexas","Gerar refinamentos iterativos para otimização de prompts","Depurar inconsistências de meta-auto utilizando transformações naturais"],"ru":["Автоматизация категориального мета-пrompting для сложных задач","Генерация итеративных уточнений для оптимизации подсказок","Отладка несоответствий мета-самосовершенствования с использованием естественных преобразований"],"ar":["الاستفادة من التحفيز المتشابك للتسلسل الهرمي للمهام المعقدة","إنتاج التنقيحات المتكررة لتحسين التحفيزات","تصحيح ασ Zh للاستفادة من التحويلات الطبيعية لتصحيح الانسجام الذاتي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive understanding of categorical foundations","Limited to agents capable of processing and applying meta-prompting frameworks"],"zh":["需要全面理解分类基础","仅限于能够处理和应用元提示框架的Agent"],"ja":["カテゴリカルな基礎の包括的な理解が必要","メタプロンプトフレームワークを処理および適用できるエージェントに限定される"],"ko":["범주론적 기초에 대한 포괄적인 이해 필요","메타 프롬프팅 프레임워크를 처리하고 적용할 수 있는 에이전트로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión exhaustiva de los fundamentos categóricos","Limitado a agents capaces de procesar y aplicar marcos de meta-prompting"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension exhaustive des fondements catégoriels","Limité aux agents capables de traiter et d''appliquer des cadres de meta-prompting"],"de":["Erfordert ein umfassendes Verständnis der kategorischen Grundlagen","Begrenzt auf Agents, die in der Lage sind, Meta-Prompting-Frameworks zu verarbeiten und anzuwenden"],"pt":["Requer compreensão abrangente dos fundamentos categóricos","Limitado a agentes capazes de processar e aplicar estruturas de meta-prompting"],"ru":["Требует всестороннего понимания категориальных основ","Ограничен агентами, способными обрабатывать и применять фреймворки мета-пrompting"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا شاملاً لمبادئ التصنيف","محدود للعميل القادر على معالجة وتطبيق إطارات التحفيز المتشابك"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"1f98417c0054c7606924c734d6cdd8587a9fe3c042fd368b7c03bb0ec3947ebe","qualityScore":60}');
