指令を検証するためのコアルール、構造、内容、効率、ガバナンス、メンテナンスを提供する","ko":"구현 규칙은 AI 에이전트의 지시를 검증하기 위한 핵심 규칙, 구조, 내용, 효율, 治理, 유지 보수를 제공한다","es":"Reglas para validar instrucciones de Agentes de IA. Mejora la estructura, contenido y eficiencia de tus proyectos","fr":"Règles pour valider les instructions des Agents d''IA. Améliorez la structure, le contenu et l''efficacité de vos projets","de":"Regeln zur Validierung von Anweisungen für KI-Agenten. Verbessern Sie die Struktur, den Inhalt und die Effizienz Ihrer Projekte","pt":"Regras comprovadas para validar instruções de agentes de IA, melhorando a estrutura, conteúdo e eficiência dos projetos","ru":"Доказанные правила для проверки инструкций ИИ Агентов, улучшающие структуру, содержание и эффективность проектов","ar":"قواعد مدعومة بالدليل لتحقق تعليمات وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي، وتحسين الهيكل والمحتوى والكفاءة للمشاريع","en":"Evidence-backed rules for validating AI coding agent instructions. Core rules for structure, content, efficiency, governance, and maintenance."},"definition":{"en":"Evidence-backed rules for validating AI coding agent instructions. Core rules for structure, content, efficiency, governance, and maintenance."},"features":{"zh":["结构规则","内容验证","效率优化","治理和维护","代码审查"],"ja":["構造ルール","内容検証","効率最適化","ガバナンスとメンテナンス","コードレビュー"],"ko":["구조 규칙","내용 검증","효율 최적화"," 治理와 유지 보수","코드 리뷰"],"es":["Estructura de proyecto eficiente","Contenido de código validado","Reglas de gobernanza y mantenimiento","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como React y Node.js","Compatibilidad con CLI","Soporte para múltiples Agentes de IA"],"fr":["Structure de projet efficace","Contenu de code validé","Règles de gouvernance et de maintenance","Intégration avec des outils de développement tels que React et Node.js","Compatibilité avec CLI","Support pour plusieurs Agents d''IA"],"de":["Effiziente Projektstruktur","Validierter Code-Inhalt","Regeln für Governance und Wartung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js","Kompatibilität mit CLI","Unterstützung für mehrere KI-Agenten"],"pt":["Estrutura de codificação eficiente","Conteúdo de alta qualidade","Governança e manutenção de projetos","Regras para validação de instruções","Melhoria da eficiência dos projetos"],"ru":["Эффективная структура кодирования","Высококачественный контент","Управление и обслуживание проектов","Правила для проверки инструкций","Улучшение эффективности проектов"],"ar":["هيكل ترميز فعال","محتوى عالي الجودة","إدارة وصيانة المشاريع","قواعد للتحقق من التعليمات","تحسين كفاءة المشاريع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","实现规则","代码验证","效率优化","治理和维护","AI编码代理","代码审查","结构规则"],"ja":["AIエージェント","実装ルール","コード検証","効率最適化","ガバナンスとメンテナンス","AIエージェントの指令","コードレビュー","構造ルール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","구현 규칙","코드 검증","효율 최적화"," 治理와 유지 보수","AI 에이전트의 지시","코드 리뷰","구조 규칙"],"es":["cómo usar Agentes de IA","qué es un Agente de IA","Agentes de IA alternativos","Agentes de IA vs herramientas de desarrollo","instalar Agentes de IA","guía de configuración de Agentes de IA","desarrollo de proyectos con Agentes de IA","mejora de la eficiencia con Agentes de IA"],"fr":["comment utiliser les Agents d''IA","qu''est-ce qu''un Agent d''IA","Agents d''IA alternatifs","Agents d''IA vs outils de développement","installer les Agents d''IA","guide de configuration des Agents d''IA","développement de projets avec les Agents d''IA","amélioration de l''efficacité avec les Agents d''IA"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","KI-Agenten-Alternativen","KI-Agenten vs Entwicklungstools","KI-Agenten installieren","Konfigurationsanleitung für KI-Agenten","Projektentwicklung mit KI-Agenten","Effizienzsteigerung mit KI-Agenten"],"pt":["como usar agentes de IA","o que é agente de IA","alternativas para agentes de IA","agentes de IA vs outros ferramentas","instalação de agentes de IA","guia de configuração de agentes de IA"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агентов","что такое ИИ Агент","альтернативы для ИИ Агентов","ИИ Агенты vs другие инструменты","установка ИИ Агентов","руководство по настройке ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام الوكلاء الذكيين","ما هو وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات للوكلاء الذكيين","الوكلاء الذكيين مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت الوكلاء الذكيين","دليل إعداد الوكلاء الذكيين"]}},"owner":"reporails","repo":"rules","repoPath":"reporails/rules","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.896Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"implement-rule","description":"Implement checks, patterns, and fixtures for an existing rule skeleton","bodyPreview":"# /implement-rule\n\nImplement checks, regex patterns, and test fixtures for an existing rule that has a skeleton but empty `checks: []`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/implement-rule <coordinate> [--agent <name>] [--dry-run]\n```\n\n- `<coordinate>`: Rule coordinate (e.g., CORE:C:0001, CLAUDE:S:0001)\n- `--agent <name>`: Agent for template var resolution (default: `claude`)\n- `--dry-run`: Show what would be generated without writing files\n\n## Examples\n\n```\n/implement-rule CORE:S:0002\n/implement-rule CORE:M:0003 --a","body":"# /implement-rule\n\nImplement checks, regex patterns, and test fixtures for an existing rule that has a skeleton but empty `checks: []`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\n/implement-rule <coordinate> [--agent <name>] [--dry-run]\n```\n\n- `<coordinate>`: Rule coordinate (e.g., CORE:C:0001, CLAUDE:S:0001)\n- `--agent <name>`: Agent for template var resolution (default: `claude`)\n- `--dry-run`: Show what would be generated without writing files\n\n## Examples\n\n```\n/implement-rule CORE:S:0002\n/implement-rule CORE:M:0003 --agent codex\n/implement-rule CLAUDE:S:0001 --dry-run\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\nFollow: [@.shared/workflows/rule-implementation.md](../../../.shared/workflows/rule-implementation.md)\n\n### 1. Locate\n\nResolve rule directory from coordinate:\n1. Look up slug in `registry/coordinate-map.yml` (backbone key: `registry.coordinate_map`)\n2. Determine category from coordinate letter: S=structure, C=content, E=efficiency, M=maintenance, G=governance\n3. For core rules: `{categories.{category}}/{slug}/`\n4. For agent rules: `{agent_rules.{agent}}/{slug}/`\n\n### 2. Read\n\nParse `rule.md` frontmatter and body:\n- Extract: `id`, `type`, `level`, `targets`, `question`, `criteria`, Pass/Fail examples from body\n- **Abort if `checks:` is already non-empty** — rule is already implemented\n- Identify the **violation class**: what structural or content pattern makes an instruction file FAIL this rule? The Pass/Fail examples are illustrations, not specifications.\n\n### 3. Analyze — Pattern Design\n\nThis is the critical step. The goal is to design a check that catches the **class of violation**, not a regex that discriminates between two fixture files.\n\n#### How to use frontmatter fields\n\n| Field | Design role |\n|-------|------------|\n| `title` | Names the concern — what property should instruction files have? |\n| `question` | Defines the evaluation question — what are we asking about the file? |\n| `criteria` | Lists observable properties of a PASSING file — invert each to get violation indicators |\n| Pass example | ONE illustration of a good file — extract the structural pattern that makes it good |\n| Fail example | ONE illustration of a bad file — extract the structural pattern that makes it bad |\n\n**Think in terms of violation structure, not fixture discrimination.**\n\n#### Mechanical rules\n\n- Select check function(s) from the 10 available: `file_exists`, `directory_exists`, `directory_contains`, `git_tracked`, `frontmatter_key`, `file_count`, `line_count`, `byte_size`, `path_resolves`, `extract_imports`\n- Derive `args` from rule description (e.g., `max: 300` for `line_count`)\n- No regex patterns needed\n\n#### Deterministic rules — violation detection\n\nDesign a pattern that matches the **structural signature of the violation**:\n\n1. Read the Fail example. Ask: what STRUCTURAL pattern makes this file bad? Not \"what text does it contain?\" but \"what is the shape of the problem?\"\n2. Read the `criteria` (if present). Each criterion describes a PASSING property. Invert: what does a file look like when it LACKS this property?\n3. Design a regex that matches the structural signature, not a specific keyword.\n\n**Two violation types:**\n\n| Type | Approach | Example |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| **Presence of bad content** | Pattern matches the violation directly | Secrets: `(?i)(api[_-]?key\\|secret)\\s*[=:]\\s*[''\"]?[A-Za-z0-9]{8,}` |\n| **Absence of good content** | Pattern matches the structural gap left by the missing content | Missing description: `^#\\s+[^\\n]+\\n\\s*\\n##` (title followed immediately by section heading, no prose between) |\n\n**NEVER use presence-then-negate as the primary strategy.** A pattern with `negate: true` that looks for \"does good content exist?\" is fragile — any incidental keyword match satisfies it. Instead, find the structural shape of the violation itself.\n\n`negate: true` is acceptable ONLY when:\n- The violation is purely about absence AND\n- No structural signature exists (the bad file is structurally identical to the good file, just missing a keyword) AND\n- You''ve confirmed there is no structural pattern to detect\n\nFor core rules: use `{{instruction_files}}` in paths (not `**/*.md`).\n\n#### Semantic rules — candidate surfacing\n\nSemantic rules have two phases: deterministic pre-check → semantic evaluation.\n\n**Pre-check purpose**: Find text that EXHIBITS the violation pattern — content that needs human/LLM judgment to determine if it''s actually a violation.\n\n**Pre-check design**:\n1. Read the `question` field. What kind of content needs to be EVALUATED?\n2. Read the `criteria` field. What observable text patterns MIGHT indicate a violation but need context to confirm?\n3. Design a pattern that matches these ambiguous indicators — not content matching the rule''s topic, but content matching the violation''s surface appearance.\n\nExample: Rule \"no-linter-enforceable-style\"\n- BAD pre-check: `(?i)(style|format|indent)` — matches the rule''s topic, not violation indicators\n- GOOD pre-check: `(?i)(indent|tab|space|bracket|semicolon|line.length|80.char|120.char)` — matches specific linter-enforceable patterns\n\nTerminal semantic check uses `prompt` derived from rule''s `question`/`criteria` fields.\n\n### 4. Generate checks\n\nWrite `checks:` array in `rule.md` frontmatter:\n- IDs follow `{NAMESPACE}.{CATEGORY}.{SLOT}.{descriptive-name}` format (e.g., `CORE.S.0005.file-exists`)\n- Check types must not exceed rule type ceiling:\n  - `mechanical` rule → only `mechanical` checks\n  - `deterministic` rule → `mechanical` + `deterministic` checks\n  - `semantic` rule → any types, semantic must be last\n- Severity from rule context: `critical` for L1, `high`/`medium` for L2+\n\n### 5. Generate patterns\n\nFor deterministic/semantic rules, write regex patterns in `rule.yml`:\n- `id` matches the check ID from frontmatter\n- `languages: [generic]` for markdown targets\n- `paths.include` uses template vars (`{{instruction_files}}`)\n- Pattern captures the violation, not the desired state\n- Severity mapping: critical→ERROR, high/medium/low→WARNING\n\nFor mechanical-only rules: leave `rule.yml` as `rules: []`.\n\n### 6. Generate fixtures\n\nFixtures simulate REAL instruction files, not minimal test content.\n\n**Pass fixture** (`tests/pass/`):\n- A realistic instruction file (30-80 lines) that a real project might have\n- Contains the structural patterns that satisfy the rule\n- Include realistic sections, commands, and project context — not just the minimum to pass\n- File names match resolved template vars (e.g., `CLAUDE.md` for claude agent)\n\n**Fail fixture** (`tests/fail/`):\n- A realistic instruction file that exhibits the specific violation\n- The violation should be the ONLY difference from a reasonable file — don''t make the fail fixture obviously broken in multiple ways\n- Must trigger the pattern''s structural signature, not just be \"bad in general\"\n\n**Fixture quality check**: After generating fixtures, re-read them and ask:\n- Does the pass fixture look like a real CLAUDE.md from a real project?\n- Does the fail fixture look like a plausible mistake someone would make?\n- Would the pattern catch the fail fixture for the RIGHT reason (structural violation match), not an incidental one?\n\nRemove `.gitkeep` from directories that now have real fixture content.\n\n### 7. Verify\n\nRun the test harness (`/test-rules`):\n```bash\ndocker compose -f runtime/docker-compose.yml -f runtime/docker-compose.dev.yml run --rm test --rule <coordinate> --verbose\n```\n- All checks must pass for both pass and fail fixtures\n- If test fails: re-examine the violation class analysis (step 3), not just the regex. The pattern may be structurally wrong, not just syntactically wrong.\n\n## Reference\n\n- Schema: `schemas/rule.schema.yml` — check field definitions, mechanical check names, severity enum\n- Patterns: `docs/pattern-guide.md` — pattern syntax, generic mode, combining patterns\n- Runtime: `runtime/` — test runner, fixture format, mechanical check implementations\n- Agent config: `agents/{agent}/config.yml` — template var values per agent\n- Path resolution: `.shared/knowledge/backbone-resolution.md`\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Rule type | Modifies rule.md | Modifies rule.yml | Fixture content |\n|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| mechanical | checks with `check` + `args` | No change (`rules: []`) | Files/dirs matching check function expectations |\n| deterministic | checks with `pattern` + `message` | Regex patterns | Content triggering/not triggering pattern |\n| semantic | pre-checks + terminal `prompt` | Regex patterns for pre-checks | Content producing/not producing candidates |\n\n## Severity Mapping\n\n| rule.md severity | rule.yml severity |\n|------------------|-------------------|\n| critical | ERROR |\n| high | WARNING |\n| medium | WARNING |\n| low | WARNING |\n\n## Pattern Design Examples\n\n### Good: Structural violation detection\n\nRule: \"has-project-description\" — file must open with a project description.\n\n**Violation structure**: Title exists, but next non-blank line is a section heading (no description prose between).\n\n```yaml\npattern-regex: \"^#\\\\s+[^\\\\n]+\\\\n\\\\s*\\\\n##\"\nmessage: \"Title followed immediately by section heading — no project description\"\n```\n\nThis catches the SHAPE of the problem: `# Title\\n\\n## Section` with nothing between.\n\n### Bad: Minimal fixture discrimination\n\nSame rule, but designed to discriminate fixtures:\n\n```yaml\npattern-regex: \"\\\\A## \"\nmessage: \"File opens with H2 instead of project description\"\n```\n\nThis only catches files starting with `##` — misses the primary failure mode (title present, description absent).\n\n### Good: Absence via structural gap\n\nRule: \"has-commands\" — file must document executable commands.\n\n**Violation structure**: File has sections but none contain backtick-wrapped commands.\n\n```yaml\n# Combined pattern: file has 2+ sections but zero backtick commands\npatterns:\n  - pattern-regex: \"^## \"\n  - pattern-not-regex: \"`[a-z]+ .+`\"\n```\n\nThis requires both conditions: structured file (has sections) AND no commands. A file with no structure at all fails a different rule.\n\n### Bad: Presence check with negate\n\nSame rule, but as a negated presence check:\n\n```yaml\npattern-regex: \"`[a-z]+ .+`\"\nnegate: true  # fragile — any backtick content satisfies this\n```\n\nA file containing `` `see above` `` or `` `my-var` `` passes this check despite having no actual commands.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Pattern discriminates fixtures instead of catching violation class | Re-analyze: what is the STRUCTURAL SHAPE of the violation? |\n| Using `negate: true` as primary strategy | Find the structural gap pattern. Negate is last resort only. |\n| Pre-check matches rule topic instead of violation indicators | Pre-check should find text that NEEDS judgment, not text about the topic |\n| Fixture is minimal synthetic content | Write realistic 30-80 line instruction files |\n| Fail fixture is broken in multiple ways | One specific violation in an otherwise reasonable file |\n| Pattern matches desired state | Invert: pattern must match the violation |\n| Using `**/*.md` in paths | Use `{{instruction_files}}` template var |\n| Missing `cross_file: true` | Add when pattern operates across target set |\n| Semantic rule without pre-checks | Always add deterministic pre-check before semantic |\n| Fixture file named wrong | Must match resolved template var (e.g., `CLAUDE.md`) |\n| Leaving `.gitkeep` alongside real fixtures | Remove `.gitkeep` when adding content |"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:10:46.351Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Coding Agents needing structured rule implementation and validation.","zh":"适合需要结构化规则实现和验证的AI编码代理。","ja":"構造化ルールの実装と検証が必要なAIコーディングエージェントに最適。","ko":"구조화된 규칙을 구현하고 검증해야 하는 AI 코딩 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Codificación de IA que necesitan implementación y validación de reglas estructuradas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Codage IA nécessitant une mise en œuvre et une validation de règles structurées.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Coding-Agents, die eine strukturierte Regelimplementierung und -validierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Codificação de IA que necessitam de implementação de regras estruturadas e validação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодирования ИИ, которым необходима реализация структурированных правил и проверка.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البرمجيين للذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ قواعد منظم و التحقق منها."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement checks, regex patterns, and test fixtures for existing rules, enhancing code efficiency and governance through evidence-backed rules for structure, content, and maintenance, utilizing command-line interfaces and template variable resolution.","zh":"赋予代理实现检查、正则表达式模式和测试fixture用于现有规则，通过基于证据的规则增强代码效率和管理，利用命令行接口和模板变量解析。","ja":"エージェントに既存のルールに対するチェック、正規表現パターン、およびテストフィクスチャを実装する能力を付与し、コマンドラインインターフェースとテンプレート変数解決を利用して、構造、コンテンツ、メンテナンスの証拠に基づくルールを通じてコード効率とガバナンスを強化する。","ko":"에이전트가 기존 규칙에 대한 검사, 정규식 패턴 및 테스트.fixture를 구현할 수 있도록 하여, 명령줄 인터페이스와 템플릿 변수 해석을 사용하여 구조, 콘텐츠, 유지 보수에 대한 증거 기반 규칙을 통해 코드 효율성과 거버넌스를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar controles, patrones de regex y fixtures de prueba para reglas existentes, mejorando la eficiencia y el gobierno del código a través de reglas respaldadas por evidencia para estructura, contenido y mantenimiento, utilizando interfaces de línea de comandos y resolución de variables de plantilla.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des contrôles, des modèles de regex et des fixtures de test pour les règles existantes, améliorant l''efficacité et la gouvernance du code grâce à des règles étayées par des preuves pour la structure, le contenu et la maintenance, en utilisant des interfaces de ligne de commande et une résolution de variables de modèle.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Prüfungen, Regex-Muster und Testfixtures für bestehende Regeln zu implementieren, wodurch die Code-Effizienz und -Governance durch evidenzbasierte Regeln für Struktur, Inhalt und Wartung verbessert werden, unter Verwendung von Kommandozeilen-Schnittstellen und Template-Variablen-Auflösung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar verificações, padrões regex e testes para regras existentes, melhorando a eficiência e governança do código por meio de regras comprovadas por evidências para estrutura, conteúdo e manutenção, utilizando interfaces de linha de comando e resolução de variáveis de modelo.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность реализовать проверки, шаблоны regex и тестовые фикстуры для существующих правил, повышая эффективность и управление кодом посредством правил, подтвержденных доказательствами, для структуры, содержания и обслуживания, используя командные интерфейсы и разрешение переменных шаблона.","ar":"يتمتع الوكلاء بتنفيذ الفحوصات وأشكال regex والمرافق الاختبارية للقواعد الحالية، مما يعزز كفاءة الحوكمة والكود من خلال القواعد المثبتة بالأدلة للتركيب والمحتوى والصيانة، باستخدام واجهات سطر الأوامر وحل متغيرات القالب."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing regex patterns for input validation","Generating test fixtures for rule verification","Enhancing code structure with evidence-backed rules"],"zh":["为输入验证实施正则表达式模式","为规则验证生成测试fixture","使用证据支持的规则增强代码结构"],"ja":["入力検証のための正規表現パターンの実装","ルール検証のためのテストフィクスチャの生成","証拠に基づくルールを使用したコード構造の強化"],"ko":["입력 유효성 검사 위한 정규식 패턴 구현","규칙 검증을 위한 테스트(fixture) 생성","증거 기반 규칙을 사용한 코드 구조 강화"],"es":["Implementar patrones de regex para la validación de entrada","Generar fixtures de prueba para la verificación de reglas","Mejorar la estructura del código con reglas respaldadas por evidencia"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des modèles de regex pour la validation des entrées","Générer des fixtures de test pour la vérification des règles","Améliorer la structure du code avec des règles étayées par des preuves"],"de":["Implementierung von Regex-Mustern für die Eingabevalidierung","Generierung von Testfixtures für die Regelverifizierung","Verbesserung der Code-Struktur mit evidenzbasierten Regeln"],"pt":["Implementação de padrões regex para validação de entrada","Geração de testes para verificação de regras","Melhoria da estrutura do código com regras comprovadas por evidências"],"ru":["Реализация шаблонов regex для проверки ввода","Генерация тестовых фикстур для проверки правил","Улучшение структуры кода правилами, подтвержденными доказательствами"],"ar":["تنفيذ أنماط regex للتحقق من المدخلات","إنتاج المرافق الاختبارية للتحقق من القواعد","تحسين هيكل الكود بالقواعد المثبتة بالأدلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires rule coordinate and agent name","Dependent on template variable resolution agent","Limited to existing rule skeletons"],"zh":["需要规则坐标和代理名称","依赖于模板变量解析代理","仅限于现有规则骨架"],"ja":["ルール座標とエージェント名が必要","テンプレート変数解決エージェントに依存","既存のルールスケルトンに限定"],"ko":["규칙 좌표와 에이전트 이름이 필요","템플릿 변수 해석 에이전트에 의존","기존 규칙 스케ルトন에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere coordenada de regla y nombre de agente","Dependiente de la resolución de variables de plantilla del agente","Limitado a esqueletos de reglas existentes"],"fr":["Nécessite une coordonnée de règle et un nom d''agent","Dépend de la résolution des variables de modèle de l''agent","Limité aux squelettes de règles existants"],"de":["Benötigt Regenkoordinate und Agentenname","Abhängig von der Auflösung von Template-Variablen des Agents","Begrenzt auf bestehende Regelskelette"],"pt":["Exige coordenada de regra e nome do agente","Dependente da resolução de variáveis de modelo do agente","Limitado a esqueletos de regras existentes"],"ru":["Требует координаты правила и имени агента","Зависит от разрешения переменных шаблона агента","Ограничен существующими скелетами правил"],"ar":["يتطلب إحداثيات القاعدة واسم الوكيل","يعتمد على حل متغيرات القالب للوكيل","محدود بهياكل القواعد الحالية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"af40151dd8a53c51e154623c33f114ccabbc68ec40a0435e4cf9bd6708abf03f","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('AWolf81/memory-lane/memorylane', 'community', 'AWolf81', 'memory-lane', 'AWolf81/memory-lane', 'memorylane', 0, 0, 60, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.901Z', '2026-03-02T02:13:54.214Z', 'eb1f296f783857fd4eab00f38f702446bd3d48df2fe8e10c8d2c9ba166767d39', '{"id":"AWolf81/memory-lane/memorylane","name":"memorylane","description":{"zh":"MemoryLane 为 Claude Code 提供持久的项目记忆，通过本地知识提取和智能注入","ja":"MemoryLane は Claude Code に耐久性のあるプロジェクトメモリを提供し、ローカルで知識を抽出し、重要な情報のみを注入します","ko":"MemoryLane은 Claude Code에 지속적인 프로젝트 메모리를 제공하여 로컬에서 지식을 추출하고 중요한 정보만 주입합니다","es":"MemoryLane proporciona a Claude Code una memoria de proyecto duradera extrayendo conocimiento local y manteniendo solo lo importante","fr":"MemoryLane fournit à Claude Code une mémoire de projet durable en extrayant des connaissances locales et en conservant uniquement l''essentiel","de":"MemoryLane bietet Claude Code eine langlebige Projektmemorie, indem es lokale Kenntnisse extrahiert und nur das Wesentliche beibehält","pt":"O MemoryLane fornece memória de projeto duradoura para o Claude Code, extraindo conhecimento localmente e injetando apenas o necessário.","ru":"MemoryLane обеспечивает надежную память проекта для Claude Code, извлекая знания локально и.inject только необходимое.","ar":"يُمنح MemoryLane ذاكرة مشروع متينة لـ Claude Code، مستخرجاً المعرفة محليًا وإضافة فقط ما يلزم.","en":"MemoryLane gives Claude Code durable project memory by extracting knowledge locally and injecting only what matters. "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"MemoryLane AI智能工具 - 持久的项目记忆","ja":"MemoryLane AIエージェント - プロジェクトメモリを強化","ko":"MemoryLane AI 에이전트 - 프로젝트 메모리 강화","es":"Herramientas de AI: MemoryLane para proyectos duraderos","fr":"Outils d''IA : MemoryLane pour des projets durables","de":"KI-Tools: MemoryLane für langlebige Projekte","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: MemoryLane - Memória de Projeto Durable","r