de projets","Intégration avec Claude Code","Fonctionnalités durables pour les projets"],"de":["Extraktion lokaler Kenntnisse","Injektion wesentlicher Funktionen","Verbesserung der Projektmemorie","Integration mit Claude Code","Langlebige Funktionen für Projekte"],"pt":["Extração de conhecimento local","Injeção de informações relevantes","Melhoria da memória de projeto","Integração com Claude Code","Tecnologia de IA avançada"],"ru":["Локальное извлечение знаний","Инъекция релевантной информации","Улучшение памяти проекта","Интеграция с Claude Code","Продвинутая технология ИИ"],"ar":["استخراج معرفة محلية","إضافة معلومات ذات صلة","تحسين ذاكرة المشروع","التكامل مع Claude Code","تقنية ذكاء اصطناعي متقدمة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["MemoryLane AI工具","如何使用 MemoryLane","什么是 MemoryLane","MemoryLane 替代品","MemoryLane 与其他工具的比较","MemoryLane 安装","MemoryLane 设置指南","AI智能工具","项目记忆管理"],"ja":["MemoryLane AIエージェント","MemoryLane の使い方","MemoryLane とは","MemoryLane の代替","MemoryLane と他のツールの比較","MemoryLane のインストール","MemoryLane の設定ガイド","AI エージェント","プロジェクトメモリ管理"],"ko":["MemoryLane AI 에이전트","MemoryLane 사용 방법","MemoryLane이란","MemoryLane 대체","MemoryLane과 다른 도구 비교","MemoryLane 설치","MemoryLane 설정 가이드","AI 에이전트","프로젝트 메모리 관리"],"es":["cómo usar MemoryLane","qué es MemoryLane","alternativas a MemoryLane","MemoryLane vs Claude Code","instalación de MemoryLane","guía de configuración de MemoryLane","herramientas de AI para proyectos","mejora de la memoria de proyectos"],"fr":["comment utiliser MemoryLane","qu''est-ce que MemoryLane","alternatives à MemoryLane","MemoryLane vs Claude Code","installation de MemoryLane","guide de configuration de MemoryLane","outils d''IA pour les projets","amélioration de la mémoire de projets"],"de":["wie man MemoryLane verwendet","was ist MemoryLane","Alternativen zu MemoryLane","MemoryLane vs Claude Code","Installation von MemoryLane","Konfigurationsanleitung für MemoryLane","KI-Tools für Projekte","Verbesserung der Projektmemorie"],"pt":["como usar MemoryLane","o que é MemoryLane","ferramentas de IA para projetos","MemoryLane vs outras ferramentas","instalar MemoryLane","guia de configuração do MemoryLane"],"ru":["как использовать MemoryLane","что такое MemoryLane","инструменты ИИ для проектов","MemoryLane vs другие инструменты","установить MemoryLane","руководство по настройке MemoryLane"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام MemoryLane","ما هو MemoryLane","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمشاريع","MemoryLane مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت MemoryLane","دليل إعداد MemoryLane"]}},"owner":"AWolf81","repo":"memory-lane","repoPath":"AWolf81/memory-lane","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.901Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"memorylane","description":"Zero-config persistent memory for Claude with automatic cost savings. Use when you need to remember project context, reduce API token costs, track learned patterns, manage memories across sessions, or curate/clean up memories. Automatically compresses context 6x and saves 84% on API costs. Keywords: memory, remember, recall, context, cost savings, reduce tokens, learn, patterns, insights, curate, clean up memories, review memories.","bodyPreview":"# MemoryLane Skill\n\n## What This Skill Does\n\nMemoryLane provides persistent memory for Claude with proven 84.3% cost savings:\n\n- **Persistent Memory**: Remember information across sessions in 4 categories (patterns, insights, learnings, context)\n- **Context Compression**: 6.4x average compression ratio (20K → 3K tokens)\n- **Cost Tracking**: Real-time API cost savings monitoring\n- **Passive Learning**: Automatically learns from git commits and file changes\n- **Zero Configuration**: Works out of t","body":"# MemoryLane Skill\n\n## What This Skill Does\n\nMemoryLane provides persistent memory for Claude with proven 84.3% cost savings:\n\n- **Persistent Memory**: Remember information across sessions in 4 categories (patterns, insights, learnings, context)\n- **Context Compression**: 6.4x average compression ratio (20K → 3K tokens)\n- **Cost Tracking**: Real-time API cost savings monitoring\n- **Passive Learning**: Automatically learns from git commits and file changes\n- **Zero Configuration**: Works out of the box with smart defaults\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate MemoryLane when the user:\n- Asks to \"remember\" something about the project\n- Wants to know \"what you remember\" or \"what you know\"\n- Mentions \"API costs\", \"token usage\", or \"reduce costs\"\n- Asks about \"project patterns\" or \"insights\"\n- Wants to see \"learned\" information\n- Requests \"context compression\" or \"optimize context\"\n- Asks to \"curate memories\", \"clean up memories\", or \"review memory quality\"\n- Mentions memories seem low quality, self-referential, or not useful\n\n## Core Commands\n\n### Check Status\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py status\n```\nShows memory statistics, category breakdown, and cost savings.\n\n### Recall Memories\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py recall \"<query>\"\n```\nSearch memories by keyword. Example:\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py recall \"authentication\"\n```\n\n### View Insights\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py insights\n```\nDisplay learned project insights (high-value patterns).\n\n### View Cost Savings\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py costs\n```\nDetailed breakdown of token savings and cost reduction.\n\n### Configure Settings\n```bash\n# Get a setting\npython3 src/cli.py config get memory.max_context_tokens\n\n# Set a setting\npython3 src/cli.py config set memory.max_context_tokens 3000\n\n# List all settings\npython3 src/cli.py config list\n```\n\n### Export Memories as Markdown\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py export-markdown --category patterns --output context.md\n```\n\n### Backup/Restore\n```bash\n# Create backup\npython3 src/cli.py backup --output backup.json\n\n# Restore from backup\npython3 src/cli.py restore backup.json\n```\n\n### Reset Memories\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py reset --force\n```\n\n## Individual Memory Management\n\n### Get a Memory\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py memory get <id>\n```\nExample: `python3 src/cli.py memory get lear-009`\n\n### Delete a Memory\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py memory delete <id>\n```\nExample: `python3 src/cli.py memory delete lear-009`\n\n### Update a Memory\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py memory update <id> --content \"New content\"\n```\nExample: `python3 src/cli.py memory update patt-001 --content \"Chose Unix sockets for lower latency\"`\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Always use these commands instead of editing memories.json directly.\n\n## Batch Curation Commands\n\n### Check Curation Status\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py curate\n```\nShows if curation is needed based on memory count and age.\n\n### List Memories for Review\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py curate --list\n```\nShows all uncurated memories with their IDs and content.\n\n### Apply Curation Decisions\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py curate --apply ''<JSON>''\n```\nApply curation decisions. JSON format:\n```json\n{\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\"id\": \"patt-001\", \"action\": \"KEEP\"},\n    {\"id\": \"lear-002\", \"action\": \"DELETE\", \"reason\": \"off-topic\"},\n    {\"id\": \"insi-003\", \"action\": \"REWRITE\", \"new_content\": \"Improved content\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Proactive Memory Quality Check\n**IMPORTANT**: When you see MemoryLane context injected via `# Project Context (from MemoryLane)` in system messages, quickly scan for poor quality memories:\n\nSigns of poor quality memories that warrant curation:\n- Status summaries: \"Based on git status...\", \"Current status of...\"\n- Meta/self-referential: \"The curation should...\", \"The hook detected...\"\n- Debug fragments: \"Let me check...\", \"Looking at the debug log...\"\n- Incomplete: Sentences ending with \"...\" or starting mid-thought\n- Duplicates of CLAUDE.md content\n\n**If you detect 2+ poor quality memories in the injected context**, proactively ask:\n> \"I notice some of the injected memories appear to be low quality (status summaries, debug notes). Would you like me to clean these up?\"\n\nIf user confirms, proceed with LLM-assisted curation below.\n\n### LLM-Assisted Curation\nWhen the user requests curation OR confirms after you detect poor memories:\n\n1. List and evaluate all memories:\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py curate --list\n```\n\n2. Evaluate each memory for:\n   - **Usefulness**: Is this actionable knowledge or just meta/debug info?\n   - **Duplication**: Is this already covered by CLAUDE.md or another memory?\n   - **Quality**: Is it complete, clear, and well-formed?\n   - **Relevance**: Would this help with future development work?\n\n3. Apply decisions (DELETE/KEEP/REWRITE):\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py curate --apply ''<JSON decisions>''\n```\n\n**DELETE these types:**\n- Meta observations about the current session\n- Debug notes and action statements\n- Status summaries\n- Duplicates of CLAUDE.md content\n- Incomplete fragments\n\n**KEEP these types:**\n- Architectural decisions with rationale\n- Bug fixes with solutions\n- Actual project context (not about MemoryLane itself)\n- Configuration knowledge\n\nExample evaluation:\n- ❌ \"Based on git status, here''s the current status...\" → DELETE (status summary)\n- ❌ \"Let me check the debug log...\" → DELETE (debug action)\n- ❌ \"The Stop hook only triggers when...\" → DELETE if in CLAUDE.md\n- ✅ \"stdio:ignore hiding Python errors - fixed by capturing stderr\" → KEEP (bug fix)\n- ✅ \"Chose Unix sockets over HTTP for 10x lower latency\" → KEEP (decision)\n\n## Learning Commands\n\n### Initial Learning\n```bash\npython3 src/learner.py initial\n```\nPerform initial learning from git history (last 20 commits) and workspace structure.\n\n### Scan Workspace\n```bash\npython3 src/learner.py scan\n```\nScan and index all Python/JS/TS files in the workspace.\n\n### Analyze Git History\n```bash\npython3 src/learner.py git\n```\nExtract patterns from recent git commits.\n\n### Continuous Learning (Background)\n```bash\npython3 src/learner.py watch\n```\nWatch for file changes and git commits continuously (runs until stopped).\n\n## Server Commands\n\n### Start Sidecar Server\n```bash\npython3 src/server.py start\n```\nStart background server with Unix socket IPC (for low-latency memory operations).\n\n### Check Server Status\n```bash\npython3 src/server.py status\n```\n\n### Stop Server\n```bash\npython3 src/server.py stop\n```\n\n## Testing Commands\n\n### Run All Tests\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n### Validate Cost Savings\n```bash\npytest tests/test_cost_savings.py -v -s\n```\nRuns comprehensive cost validation tests (shows 84.3% savings proof).\n\n### Test Memory Store\n```bash\npytest tests/test_memory_store.py -v\n```\n\n## Usage Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Remember Important Information\nWhen the user says: \"Remember that this project uses PostgreSQL with SSL mode required\"\n\n```bash\n# (You would typically use the Python API, but for CLI:)\npython3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, ''src'')\nfrom memory_store import MemoryStore\nstore = MemoryStore(''.memorylane/memories.json'')\nstore.add_memory(''context'', ''Project uses PostgreSQL with SSL mode required'', ''manual'', 0.9)\nprint(''✓ Remembered'')\n\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Recall Project Knowledge\nWhen the user asks: \"What do you know about our database setup?\"\n\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py recall \"database\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Show Cost Savings\nWhen the user asks: \"How much money has MemoryLane saved me?\"\n\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py costs\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Learn from Project History\nWhen starting work on a project:\n\n```bash\npython3 src/learner.py initial\npython3 src/cli.py insights\n```\n\n## Integration with Workflows\n\n### Daily Development Workflow\n```bash\n# Morning: Start server and check status\npython3 src/server.py start\npython3 src/cli.py status\n\n# During work: MemoryLane learns passively\n# (no action needed - watches git commits and file changes)\n\n# Evening: Check what was learned\npython3 src/cli.py insights\npython3 src/cli.py costs\n```\n\n### Project Onboarding Workflow\n```bash\n# Step 1: Initial learning\npython3 src/learner.py initial\n\n# Step 2: Review learned patterns\npython3 src/cli.py recall \"primary language\"\npython3 src/cli.py insights\n\n# Step 3: Export context for sharing\npython3 src/cli.py export-markdown --output project-context.md\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\nKey settings in `.memorylane/config.json`:\n\n- `memory.max_context_tokens`: Target token count for compression (default: 2000)\n- `memory.compression_ratio_target`: Target compression ratio (default: 7.0x)\n- `context_rot.model_context_tokens`: Advertised model window for context rot guard (default: 200000)\n- `context_rot.safe_fraction`: Fraction of model window allowed for prompt + injected context (default: 0.5)\n- `context_rot.reserve_tokens`: Buffer reserved for assistant response (default: 1200)\n- `learning.watch_file_changes`: Enable file watching (default: true)\n- `learning.watch_git_commits`: Learn from commits (default: true)\n- `privacy.exclude_patterns`: Files to ignore (default: *.env, secrets/, etc.)\n\n## Performance Metrics\n\nValidated through comprehensive testing:\n\n- **Cost Savings**: 84.3% (baseline $17.25/week → $2.70/week)\n- **Compression Ratio**: 6.4x average (2.3M tokens → 360K tokens)\n- **Retrieval Latency**: <100ms (target, server not benchmarked yet)\n- **Memory Quality**: Relevance scoring with automatic pruning\n\n## Important Notes\n\n1. **Privacy**: All data stored locally in `.memorylane/` directory\n2. **No Dependencies**: Pure Python 3.8+ (no external packages needed for production)\n3. **Automatic Exclusions**: Respects `.env`, `secrets/`, and other sensitive patterns\n4. **Backup Before Reset**: Always creates backup before destructive operations\n5. **Server Optional**: CLI works standalone; server adds performance for frequent operations\n\n## Example Conversation Flow\n\n**User**: \"Remember that our API uses JWT tokens with 24-hour expiration\"\n\n**You**: Let me store that in MemoryLane''s context.\n```bash\npython3 -c \"...\"  # Add to memory\n```\n✓ Remembered in context category with 0.9 relevance.\n\n**User**: \"What do you know about our authentication?\"\n\n**You**: Let me recall what I know about authentication.\n```bash\npython3 src/cli.py recall \"authentication\"\n```\nFound 2 memories:\n1. [context] API uses JWT tokens with 24-hour expiration ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n2. [patterns] Project uses authentication middleware ⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nBased on what I''ve learned, your project uses JWT tokens for authentication with 24-hour expiration...\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**Server won''t start**: Check if already running with `python3 src/server.py status`\n\n**No memories found**: Run initial learning with `python3 src/learner.py initial`\n\n**Cost tracking shows $0**: Metrics file not initialized yet (will populate after server usage)\n\n**Tests failing**: Install dev dependencies with `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:13:54.214Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Claude Code Agents needing persistent project memory and cost optimization through context compression and passive learning.","zh":"非常适合需要持久项目内存和通过上下文压缩和被动学习实现成本优化的 Claude Code Agents。","ja":"Claude Code エージェントが持続的なプロジェクトメモリとコンテキスト圧縮およびパッシブ学習によるコスト最適化を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"지속적인 프로젝트 메모리와 컨텍스트 압축 및 수동 학습을 통해 비용 최적화를 필요한 Claude Code 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Claude Code que necesitan memoria de proyecto persistente y optimización de costos a través de la compresión de contexto y el aprendizaje pasivo.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Claude Code nécessitant une mémoire de projet persistante et une optimisation des coûts grâce à la compression de contexte et à l''apprentissage passif.","de":"Perfekt für Claude Code-Agents, die ein persistierendes Projektgedächtnis und eine Kostenoptymierung durch Kontextkomprimierung und passives Lernen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Código Claude que necessitam de memória de projeto persistente e otimização de custos por meio da compressão de contexto e aprendizado passivo.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Claude Code, которым необходима постоянная память проекта и оптимизация затрат за счет сжатия контекста и пассивного обучения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل كلود كود الذي يحتاج إلى ذاكرة مشروع مستدامة وتحسين التكلفة من خلال ضغط السياق والتعلم السلبي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to retain information across sessions with 84.3% cost savings, utilizing context compression with a 6.4x average compression ratio and real-time API cost savings monitoring through protocols like git commits and file changes.","zh":"赋予代理在会话之间保留信息的能力，平均节省成本 84.3%，利用上下文压缩平均压缩比 6.4 倍，并通过 git 提交和文件更改等协议实时监控 API 成本节省。","ja":"エージェントがセッション間で情報を保持できるようにし、平均して 84.3% のコストを削減し、コンテキスト圧縮の平均圧縮比 6.4 倍を利用し、git コミットやファイルの変更などのプロトコルを使用してリアルタイムで API コストの節約を監視します。","ko":"에이전트가 세션 간에 정보를 유지할 수 있도록 하며, 평균 84.3%의 비용을節約하고, 컨텍스트 압축의 평균 압축 비율 6.4배를 利用하며, git 커밋 및 파일 변경 등 프로토콜을 통해 실시간으로 API 비용 절감을 監視합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes retener información entre sesiones con un ahorro de costos del 84,3%, utilizando la compresión de contexto con una relación de compresión promedio de 6,4x y un monitoreo de ahorros de costos de API en tiempo real a través de protocolos como confirmaciones de git y cambios de archivo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de conserver les informations entre les sessions avec une économie de coûts de 84,3%, en utilisant la compression de contexte avec un ratio de compression moyen de 6,4x et un suivi en temps réel des économies de coûts d''API via des protocoles tels que les validations git et les modifications de fichiers.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Informationen zwischen Sitzungen beizubehalten, mit einer Kostenersparnis von 84,3%, unter Nutzung der Kontextkomprimierung mit einem durchschnittlichen Komprimierungsverhältnis von 6,4x und Echtzeit-Überwachung der API-Kostenersparnis durch Protokolle wie git-Commits und Dateiänderungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reter informações entre sessões com economia de custos de 84,3%, utilizando a compressão de contexto com uma taxa de compressão média de 6,4x e monitoramento de economia de custos de API em tempo real por meio de protocolos como commits git e alterações de arquivos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью сохранять информацию между сессиями с экономией затрат в 84,3%, используя сжатие контекста со средним коэффициентом сжатия 6,4x и мониторинг экономии затрат API в режиме реального времени через протоколы như коммиты git и изменения файлов.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من الاحتفاظ بالمعلومات عبر الجلسات مع توفير التكاليف بنسبة 84.3٪ ، باستخدام ضغط السياق بنسبة ضغط متوسطة تبلغ 6.4x ومراقبة توفير تكاليف واجهة برمجة التطبيقات في الوقت الفعلي من خلال بروتوكولات مثل التعهدات git وتغييرات الملفات."},"useCases":{"en":["Retaining project context across sessions","Automatically learning from git commits and file changes","Monitoring API cost savings in real-time","Compressing context by an average of 6.4x"],"zh":["保留会话间的项目上下文","自动从 git 提交和文件更改中学习","实时监控 API 成本节省","平均 6.4 倍的上下文压缩"],"ja":["セッション間のプロジェクトコンテキストを保持する","git コミットやファイルの変更から自動的に学習する","API コストの節約をリアルタイムで監視する","平均 6.4 倍のコンテキスト圧縮"],"ko":["세션 간의 프로젝트 컨텍스트 유지","git 커밋 및 파일 변경에서 자동으로 학습","실시간으로 API 비용 절감 監視","平均 6.4배의 컨텍스트 압축"],"es":["Retener el contexto del proyecto entre sesiones","Aprender automáticamente de confirmaciones de git y cambios de archivo","Monitorear los ahorros de costos de API en tiempo real","Comprimir el contexto con una relación de compresión promedio de 6,4x"],"fr":["Conserver le contexte du projet entre les sessions","Apprendre automatiquement à partir de validations git et de modifications de fichiers","Surveiller les économies de coûts d''API en temps réel","Compresser le contexte avec un ratio de compression moyen de 6,4x"],"de":["Projekt-Kontext zwischen Sitzungen beibehalten","Automatisch aus git-Commits und Dateiänderungen lernen","API-Kostenersparnis in Echtzeit überwachen","Kontext mit einem durchschnittlichen Komprimierungsverhältnis von 6,4x komprimieren"],"pt":["Manter o contexto do projeto entre sessões","Aprender automaticamente com commits git e alterações de arquivos","Monitorar a economia de custos de API em tempo real","Comprimir o contexto com uma média de 6,4x"],"ru":["Сохранять контекст проекта между сессиями","Автоматически учиться из коммитов git и изменений файлов","Мониторить экономию затрат API в режиме реального времени","Сжимать контекст в среднем в 6,4 раза"],"ar":["الحفاظ على سياق المشروع عبر الجلسات","التعلم تلقائيًا من التعهدات git وتغييرات الملفات","مراقبة توفير تكاليف واجهة برمجة التطبيقات في الوقت الفعلي","ضغط السياق بمتوسط ​​6.4x"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with Claude Code","Limited to 4 categories of memory (patterns, insights, learnings, context)"],"zh":["需要与 Claude Code 集成","仅限 4 类内存（模式、洞察、学习、上下文）"],"ja":["Claude Code との統合が必要","メモリは 4 つのカテゴリ（パターン、洞察、学習、コンテキスト）に限定"],"ko":["Claude Code와의 통합이 필요","메모리는 4가지 카테고리(패턴, 통찰, 학습, 컨텍스트)로 제한"],"es":["Requiere integración con Claude Code","Limitado a 4 categorías de memoria (patrones, perspectivas, conocimientos, contexto)"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Claude Code","Limité à 4 catégories de mémoire (modèles, perspectives, connaissances, contexte)"],"de":["Benötigt Integration mit Claude Code","Begrenzt auf 4 Kategorien des Gedächtnisses (Muster, Einblicke, Lernergebnisse, Kontext)"],"pt":["Requer integração com o Claude Code","Limitado a 4 categorias de memória (padrões, insights, aprendizados, contexto)"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Claude Code","Ограничен до 4 категорий памяти (образцы, идеи, знания, контекст)"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع كلود كود","محدود بـ 4 فئات من الذاكرة (الأنماط، والرؤى، والتعلم، والسياق)"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"eb1f296f783857fd4eab00f38f702446bd3d48df2fe8e10c8d2c9ba166767d39","qualityScore":60}');
