"Transformación de notas caóticas en tareas acciónables","Compatibilidad con múltiples metas de vida","Construido con Next.js, Supabase y Claude AI","Productividad mejorada con IA","Tareas organizadas y prioritarias"],"fr":["Transformation de notes chaotiques en tâches actionnables","Compatibilité avec plusieurs objectifs de vie","Construit avec Next.js, Supabase et Claude AI","Productivité améliorée avec l''IA","Tâches organisées et prioritaires"],"de":["Umwandlung chaotischer Notizen in handhabbare Aufgaben","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Lebenszielen","Erstellt mit Next.js, Supabase und Claude AI","Erhöhte Produktivität durch KI","Aufgaben organisiert und priorisiert"],"pt":["Construído com Next.js","Integração com Supabase","Tecnologia de IA da Claude","Organização de notas em tarefas","Suporte a múltiplos objetivos de vida"],"ru":["Построен на Next.js","Интеграция с Supabase","Технология ИИ от Claude","Организация заметок в действия","Поддержка нескольких целей жизни"],"ar":["مبني على Next.js","التكامل مع Supabase","تكنولوجيا الذكاء الاصطناعي من Claude","تنظيم الملاحظات في مهام","دعم أهداف الحياة المتعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能助手","Issue-Resolution","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI","如何使用AI智能助手","什么是AI智能助手","Issue-Resolution安装","Issue-Resolution设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Issue-Resolution","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントとは","Issue-Resolutionのインストール","Issue-Resolutionの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Issue-Resolution","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트란","Issue-Resolution 설치","Issue-Resolution 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de resolución de problemas con IA","cómo utilizar herramientas de productividad con IA","alternativas a herramientas de resolución de problemas","guía de instalación de herramientas de resolución de problemas","configuración de herramientas de resolución de problemas","qué es un agente de resolución de problemas con IA","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI"],"fr":["outils de résolution de problèmes avec IA","comment utiliser des outils de productivité avec IA","alternatives aux outils de résolution de problèmes","guide d''installation des outils de résolution de problèmes","configuration des outils de résolution de problèmes","qu''est-ce qu''un outil de résolution de problèmes avec IA","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI"],"de":["KI-gestützte Problemlösungstools","wie man KI-gestützte Produktivitätstools verwendet","Alternativen zu KI-gestützten Problemlösungstools","Installationsanleitung für KI-gestützte Problemlösungstools","Konfiguration von KI-gestützten Problemlösungstools","was ist ein KI-gestütztes Problemlösungstool","Next.js","Supabase","Claude AI"],"pt":["como usar Issue-Resolution","o que é Issue-Resolution","Issue-Resolution alternativa","Issue-Resolution vs Trello","instalar Issue-Resolution","guia de configuração do Issue-Resolution"],"ru":["как использовать Issue-Resolution","что такое Issue-Resolution","альтернатива Issue-Resolution","Issue-Resolution vs Trello","установить Issue-Resolution","руководство по настройке Issue-Resolution"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام حل المشكلات","ما هو حل المشكلات","بديل حل المشكلات","حل المشكلات مقابل Trello","تثبيت حل المشكلات","دليل إعداد حل المشكلات"]}},"owner":"mthangtr","repo":"groaly","repoPath":"mthangtr/groaly","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.903Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"issue-resolution","description":"Systematically diagnose and fix bugs through triage, reproduction, root cause analysis, and verified fixes. Use when resolving bugs, errors, failing tests, or investigating unexpected behavior.","bodyPreview":"# Issue Resolution Pipeline\n\nSystematically resolve issues through iterative diagnosis and verified fixes.\n\n## Pipeline Overview\n\n```\nINPUT → Triage → Reproduction → Root Cause Analysis → Impact → Fix → Verify\n              ◄──────────────►◄────────────────────►\n                    (Iterative loops allowed)\n```\n\n| Phase                  | Purpose                            | Output              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| 0. Triage","body":"# Issue Resolution Pipeline\n\nSystematically resolve issues through iterative diagnosis and verified fixes.\n\n## Pipeline Overview\n\n```\nINPUT → Triage → Reproduction → Root Cause Analysis → Impact → Fix → Verify\n              ◄──────────────►◄────────────────────►\n                    (Iterative loops allowed)\n```\n\n| Phase                  | Purpose                            | Output              |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| 0. Triage              | Normalize input, classify severity | Issue Brief         |\n| 1. Reproduction        | Prove the bug, trace code path     | Repro Report + Test |\n| 2. Root Cause Analysis | Find WHY, not just WHERE           | RCA Report          |\n| 3. Impact Assessment   | Blast radius, regression risk      | Impact Report       |\n| 4. Fix Decomposition   | Break into beads                   | .beads/\\*.md        |\n| 5. Verification        | Prove fix works, no regressions    | Passing tests       |\n\n## Phase 0: Triage\n\nNormalize different input types to a structured Issue Brief.\n\n### Input Types\n\n| Type                  | Triage Strategy                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| **Vague report**      | Clarify → Explore → Reproduce         |\n| **Error/Stack trace** | Parse trace → Locate code → Reproduce |\n| **Failing test**      | Run test → Extract assertion → Trace  |\n\n### Vague Report Triage\n\n```\nUser: \"Login is broken\"\n         │\n         ▼\nAsk clarification questions:\n• What error do you see?\n• When did it start working / stop working?\n• What steps trigger it?\n• Specific user/browser/environment?\n         │\n         ▼ (if user can''t clarify)\nExplore:\n• mcp__gkg__search_codebase_definitions: Find auth/login related code\n• git log: Recent changes in area\n• Check logs if available\n```\n\n### Error/Stack Trace Triage\n\n```\nParse the stack trace:\n• Extract file:line locations\n• mcp__gkg__get_definition on functions in trace\n• Read surrounding context\n         │\n         ▼\nIdentify reproduction conditions:\n• What input caused this?\n• Can we write a test?\n```\n\n### Failing Test Triage\n\n```\nRun test in isolation:\n• bun test <file> --filter \"<test name>\"\n• Read test file for setup/assertions\n• Check git log: was it passing before?\n         │\n         ▼\nTrace implementation:\n• What code does test exercise?\n• mcp__gkg__get_references on tested function\n• Recent changes to implementation?\n```\n\n### Severity Classification\n\nDetermines reproduction requirements:\n\n| Severity                            | Reproduction Required  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| **CRITICAL** (production, security) | Failing test REQUIRED  |\n| **REGRESSION** (was working)        | Failing test REQUIRED  |\n| **RACE CONDITION** (timing)         | Failing test REQUIRED  |\n| **LOGIC BUG**                       | Failing test PREFERRED |\n| **UI/VISUAL**                       | Manual + screenshot OK |\n| **PERFORMANCE**                     | Benchmark/profile OK   |\n| **QUICK FIX** (obvious cause)       | Manual repro OK        |\n\n### Issue Brief Template\n\nSave to `history/issues/<id>/brief.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Issue Brief: <Short Title>\n\n**Severity**: CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW\n**Type**: Regression / Edge case / Race condition / UI / Performance / Other\n**Repro Required**: Failing test / Manual OK\n\n## Symptom\n\n<What is happening>\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n<What should happen>\n\n## Reproduction\n\n<Steps, test command, or code path>\n\n## Evidence\n\n<Error message, stack trace, test output>\n\n## Affected Area\n\n<Files, modules, features involved>\n\n## Timeline\n\n<When started, recent changes if known>\n```\n\n## Phase 1: Reproduction\n\nProve the bug exists and trace the code path.\n\n### If Failing Test Required\n\n```bash\n# Create test file\n# packages/<area>/src/__tests__/<feature>.regression.test.ts\n\n# Test should:\n# 1. Set up conditions that trigger bug\n# 2. Assert expected behavior (currently fails)\n# 3. Be deterministic\n```\n\n### Reproduction Checklist\n\n- [ ] Bug is reproducible on demand\n- [ ] Exact error/behavior captured\n- [ ] Minimal reproduction (simplest case that fails)\n- [ ] Code path identified (stack trace or tracing)\n\n### Code Path Tracing\n\n```\nmcp__gkg__get_definition     → Find where error originates\nmcp__gkg__get_references     → Find callers\ngit blame <file>       → Who changed it, when\ngit log -p <file>      → What changed recently\n```\n\n### Repro Report Template\n\nSave to `history/issues/<id>/repro.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Reproduction Report: <Issue Title>\n\n## Reproduction Method\n\n☐ Failing test: `<test file and name>`\n☐ Manual: <steps>\n\n## Error/Behavior Captured\n\n<Exact error message, stack trace>\n\n## Code Path\n\n1. Entry: `<file>:<line>` - <function>\n2. Calls: `<file>:<line>` - <function>\n3. Fails at: `<file>:<line>` - <reason>\n\n## Recent Changes (if relevant)\n\n- <commit>: <summary>\n```\n\n## Phase 2: Root Cause Analysis\n\nFind WHY the bug happens, not just WHERE.\n\n### RCA Framework\n\n```\nSTEP 1: Generate hypotheses (3-5)\n         │\n         ▼\nSTEP 2: Gather evidence for/against each\n         │\n         ▼\nSTEP 3: Eliminate hypotheses\n         │\n         ▼\nSTEP 4: Confirm root cause\n```\n\n### Bug Type → RCA Strategy\n\n| Bug Type            | Strategy                  | Key Tools                       |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Regression**      | Find breaking change      | `git bisect`, `git blame`       |\n| **Edge case**       | Analyze boundary inputs   | Type inspection, boundary tests |\n| **Race condition**  | Trace async flow          | Timing logs, async analysis     |\n| **Data corruption** | Trace state changes       | Data flow analysis              |\n| **External dep**    | Check version/API changes | Changelogs, API docs            |\n\n### Oracle for RCA\n\n**Hypothesis Generation:**\n\n```\noracle(\n  task: \"Generate root cause hypotheses\",\n  context: \"\"\"\n    Symptom: <error>\n    Code path: <trace>\n    Recent changes: <git log>\n\n    Generate 3-5 hypotheses ranked by likelihood.\n    For each, what evidence would support/refute it?\n  \"\"\",\n  files: [\"<affected files>\"]\n)\n```\n\n**Hypothesis Validation:**\n\n```\noracle(\n  task: \"Validate root cause hypothesis\",\n  context: \"\"\"\n    Hypothesis: <proposed cause>\n    Evidence: <gathered evidence>\n\n    1. Does evidence support or refute?\n    2. Explain causal chain: cause → symptom\n    3. What would confirm this?\n  \"\"\",\n  files: [\"<relevant files>\"]\n)\n```\n\n### Iteration: RCA → Reproduction Loop\n\nIf hypothesis needs more evidence:\n\n```\nIN RCA: \"Need timing logs to confirm race condition\"\n    │\n    ▼\nBACK TO REPRO:\n• Add instrumentation\n• Run with specific conditions\n• Capture new evidence\n    │\n    ▼\nRETURN TO RCA with new evidence\n```\n\n### RCA Report Template\n\nSave to `history/issues/<id>/rca.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Root Cause Analysis: <Issue Title>\n\n## Iteration: <N>\n\n## Hypotheses Considered\n\n### Hypothesis A: <Description>\n\n- **Likelihood**: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW\n- **Supporting evidence**: ...\n- **Refuting evidence**: ...\n- **Verdict**: ✓ CONFIRMED / ✗ ELIMINATED\n\n### Hypothesis B: ...\n\n## Root Cause (Confirmed)\n\n**Cause**: <Clear statement>\n\n**Causal chain**:\n\n1. <Step> leads to\n2. <Step> leads to\n3. <Symptom>\n\n## Why This Happened\n\n<Underlying reason - missing validation, wrong assumption, etc.>\n\n## Fix Approach\n\n**Immediate**: <What to change>\n**Preventive**: <How to prevent similar bugs>\n```\n\n## Phase 3: Impact Assessment\n\nBefore fixing, understand blast radius.\n\n### Impact Analysis\n\n```\nmcp__gkg__get_references <affected function>\n    → Who else calls this?\n\nGrep for related patterns\n    → Similar code that might have same bug?\n\nReview test coverage\n    → What tests cover this area?\n```\n\n### Regression Risk\n\n| Factor              | Risk Level |\n| ------------------- | ---------- |\n| High usage function | HIGH       |\n| Shared utility      | HIGH       |\n| Public API change   | HIGH       |\n| Internal helper     | LOW        |\n| Isolated module     | LOW        |\n\n### Spike for Complex Fixes\n\nIf fix approach is uncertain:\n\n```bash\nbd create \"Spike: Validate fix approach for <issue>\" -t task -p 0\n```\n\nExecute via MULTI_AGENT_WORKFLOW, write to `.spikes/<issue-id>/`.\n\n### Impact Report Template\n\nSave to `history/issues/<id>/impact.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Impact Assessment: <Issue Title>\n\n## Blast Radius\n\n### Direct Impact\n\n- <File/function directly changed>\n\n### Callers Affected\n\n- <List from mcp__gkg__get_references>\n\n### Related Code\n\n- <Similar patterns that may need same fix>\n\n## Regression Risk\n\n**Level**: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW\n**Reason**: <Why this risk level>\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n- Existing tests: <list>\n- Tests to add: <list>\n\n## Fix Validation\n\n☐ Spike completed (if needed): `.spikes/<id>/`\n☐ Fix approach validated\n```\n\n## Phase 4: Fix Decomposition\n\nBreak fix into beads.\n\n### Simple Fix (Single Bead)\n\n```bash\nbd create \"Fix: <issue title>\" -t bug -p <priority>\n```\n\nBead includes:\n\n- Root cause reference\n- Fix implementation\n- Test (failing → passing)\n- Docs update (if behavior change)\n\n### Complex Fix (Multiple Beads)\n\n```bash\nbd create \"Epic: Fix <issue>\" -t epic -p <priority>\nbd create \"Add regression test for <issue>\" -t task --blocks <epic>\nbd create \"Fix <component A>\" -t bug --blocks <epic> --deps <test>\nbd create \"Fix <component B>\" -t bug --blocks <epic> --deps <test>\nbd create \"Update docs for <behavior change>\" -t task --blocks <epic> --deps <fix-a>,<fix-b>\n```\n\n### Fix Bead Template\n\n```markdown\n# Fix: <Issue Title>\n\n**Type**: bug\n**Priority**: <0-4>\n**Fixes**: <issue reference>\n\n## Root Cause\n\n<From RCA report>\n\n## Fix Implementation\n\n<What to change and why>\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `<file>`: <change description>\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Regression test passes\n- [ ] Original symptom no longer reproducible\n- [ ] No new test failures\n- [ ] `bun run check-types` passes\n- [ ] `bun run build` passes\n```\n\n## Phase 5: Verification\n\nProve fix works and nothing else broke.\n\n### Verification Checklist\n\n```bash\n# 1. Regression test passes\nbun test <regression-test-file>\n\n# 2. Original symptom gone\n<manual verification or test>\n\n# 3. No new failures\nbun run test\n\n# 4. Types and build\nbun run check-types\nbun run build\n```\n\n### Iteration: Verify → RCA Loop\n\nIf fix doesn''t work:\n\n```\nTest still fails after fix\n    │\n    ▼\nRoot cause was wrong or incomplete\n    │\n    ▼\nBACK TO RCA:\n• Eliminate current hypothesis\n• Generate new hypotheses\n• Update RCA Report with iteration\n```\n\n### Verify → Impact Loop\n\nIf fix causes regressions:\n\n```\nNew test failures after fix\n    │\n    ▼\nFix has unintended side effects\n    │\n    ▼\nBACK TO IMPACT:\n• Reassess blast radius\n• Consider alternative fix approach\n```\n\n## Loop Limits\n\nPrevent infinite iteration:\n\n| Loop         | Soft Limit | Hard Limit | At Hard Limit               |\n| ------------ | ---------- | ---------- | --------------------------- |\n| RCA → Repro  | 2          | 4          | Escalate / pair debug       |\n| RCA → Triage | 1          | 2          | Re-evaluate original report |\n| Verify → RCA | 2          | 3          | Oracle deep review          |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Tool Selection\n\n| Need                  | Tool                            |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Parse stack trace     | Read + mcp**gkg**get_definition |\n| Find callers          | mcp**gkg**get_references        |\n| Recent changes        | git log, git blame              |\n| Binary search commits | git bisect                      |\n| Reasoning about cause | oracle                          |\n| Validate fix approach | Spike via MULTI_AGENT_WORKFLOW  |\n\n### Common Mistakes\n\n- **Fixing symptom, not cause** → Leads to recurrence\n- **Skipping reproduction** → Can''t verify fix\n- **No regression test** → Bug returns later\n- **Ignoring impact** → Fix breaks other things\n- **Not iterating** → Wrong diagnosis persists\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:16:36.606Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Diagnostic Agents needing structured issue resolution pipelines with iterative diagnosis and verified fixes.","zh":"非常适合需要具有迭代诊断和已验证修复的结构化问题解决流程的诊断Agent。","ja":"反復的な診断と検証済み修正を備えた構造化された問題解決パイプラインを必要とする診断エージェントに最適です。","ko":"반복적인 진단과 검증된 수정을 갖춘 구조화된 문제 해결 파이프라인이 필요한 진단 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Diagnóstico que necesitan pipelines estructurados de resolución de incidencias con diagnóstico iterativo y correcciones verificadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Diagnostic nécessitant des pipelines structurés de résolution de problèmes avec diagnostic itératif et correctifs vérifiés.","de":"Perfekt für Diagnose-Agents, die strukturierte Pipelines zur Problembehebung mit iterativer Diagnose und verifizierten Korrekturen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Diagnóstico que precisam de pipelines de resolução de problemas estruturados com diagnóstico iterativo e soluções verificadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для диагностических агентов, требующих структурированных конвейеров решения проблем с итеративной диагностикой и проверенными исправлениями.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التشخيصيين الذين يحتاجون إلى трубكات حل المشكلات المهيكلة مع التشخيص التكراري والتصحيحات المفوضة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically resolve issues using Next.js, Supabase, and Claude AI, providing a comprehensive framework for triage, reproduction, root cause analysis, impact assessment, and fix verification via iterative loops.","zh":"赋能Agent使用Next.js、Supabase和Claude AI系统地解决问题，通过迭代循环为分诊、复现、根本原因分析、影响评估和修复验证提供一个全面的框架。","ja":"Next.js、Supabase、Claude AIを使用して問題を体系的に解決するエージェントを強化し、トリアージ、再現、根本原因分析、影響評価、および反復ループによる修正検証のための包括的なフレームワークを提供します。","ko":"Next.js, Supabase 및 Claude AI를 사용하여 문제를 체계적으로 해결하는 에이전트를 강화하며, 반복 루프를 통한 트라이아지, 재현, 근본 원인 분석, 영향 평가 및 수정 검증을 위한 포괄적인 프레임워크를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes resolver problemas sistemáticamente utilizando Next.js, Supabase y Claude AI, proporcionando un marco integral para triaje, reproducción, análisis de causa raíz, evaluación de impacto y verificación de correcciones mediante bucles iterativos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de résoudre systématiquement les problèmes en utilisant Next.js, Supabase et Claude AI, en fournissant un cadre complet pour le tri, la reproduction, l''analyse de la cause racine, l''évaluation de l''impact et la vérification des correctifs via des boucles itératives.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Probleme systematisch mit Next.js, Supabase und Claude AI zu lösen, und bietet einen umfassenden Rahmen für Triaging, Reproduktion, Root-Cause-Analyse, Auswirkungsbewertung und Korrekturverifizierung durch iterative Schleifen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a resolver problemas de forma sistemática usando Next.js, Supabase e Claude AI, fornecendo uma estrutura abrangente para triagem, reprodução, análise de causa raiz, avaliação de impacto e verificação de soluções via loops iterativos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически решать проблемы с помощью Next.js, Supabase и Claude AI, предоставляя комплексную основу для триажа, воспроизведения, анализа коренной причины, оценки воздействия и верификации исправлений через итерационные циклы.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على حل المشكلات بشكل منهجي باستخدام Next.js و Supabase و Claude AI، مما يوفر إطارًا شاملاً لترشيح، وإعادة الإنتاج، وتحليل السبب الجذري، وتقييم التأثير، وتصديق الإصلاحات من خلال الحلقات التكرارية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating issue triage and reproduction for faster resolution","Generating actionable tasks from chaotic notes across multiple life goals","Debugging complex issues through root cause analysis and verified fixes"],"zh":["自动化问题分诊和复现以实现更快解决","从跨多个生活目标的混乱笔记中生成可操作任务","通过根本原因分析和已验证修复来调试复杂问题"],"ja":["より迅速な解決のための問題のトリアージと再現の自動化","複数のライフゴールにわたる混沌としたノートから実践可能なタスクを生成","根本原因分析と検証済み修正による複雑な問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["더 빠른 해결을 위한 문제 트라이아지 및 재현 자동화","다중 생목표에 걸친 혼란스러운 노트에서 실행 가능한 작업 생성","근본 원인 분석과 검증된 수정을 통한 복잡한 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización del triaje y reproducción de incidencias para una resolución más rápida","Generación de tareas accionables a partir de notas caóticas en múltiples objetivos de vida","Depuración de problemas complejos mediante análisis de causa raíz y correcciones verificadas"],"fr":["Automatisation du tri et de la reproduction des problèmes pour une résolution plus rapide","Génération de tâches actionnables à partir de notes chaotiques couvrant de multiples objectifs de vie","Débogage de problèmes complexes via l''analyse de la cause racine et des correctifs vérifiés"],"de":["Automatisierung des Triagings und der Reproduktion von Problemen für schnellere Lösungen","Generierung umsetzbarer Aufgaben aus chaotischen Notizen über mehrere Lebensziele hinweg","Debuggen komplexer Probleme durch Root-Cause-Analyse und verifizierte Korrekturen"],"pt":["Automatizar a triagem e reprodução de problemas para uma resolução mais rápida","Gerar tarefas executáveis a partir de notas caóticas em vários objetivos de vida","Depurar problemas complexos por meio da análise da causa raiz e soluções verificadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать триаж и воспроизведение проблем для более быстрого решения","Генерировать действенные задачи из хаотичных заметок по нескольким целям жизни","Отлаживать сложные проблемы посредством анализа коренной причины и проверенных исправлений"],"ar":["أتمتة ترشيح وإعادة الإنتاج للمشكلات من أجل حل أسرع","توليد مهام قابلة للتنفيذ من ملاحظات فوضوية عبر أهداف الحياة المتعددة","تصحيح المشكلات المعقدة من خلال تحليل السبب الجذري والإصلاحات المفوضة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with Next.js and Supabase","Dependent on Claude AI for advanced diagnostic capabilities","Iterative loops may require additional computational resources"],"zh":["需要与Next.js和Supabase集成","依赖Claude AI来获得高级诊断能力","迭代循环可能需要额外的计算资源"],"ja":["Next.jsおよびSupabaseとの統合が必要","高度な診断機能のためにClaude AIに依存","反復ループには追加の計算リソースが必要な場合がある"],"ko":["Next.js 및 Supabase와의 통합 필요","고급 진단 기능을 위해 Claude AI에 의존","반복 루프에 추가 계산 리소스가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere integración con Next.js y Supabase","Depende de Claude AI para capacidades de diagnóstico avanzadas","Los bucles iterativos pueden requerir recursos computacionales adicionales"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Next.js et Supabase","Dépend de Claude AI pour les capacités de diagnostic avancées","Les boucles itératives peuvent nécessiter des ressources informatiques supplémentaires"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit Next.js und Supabase","Abhängig von Claude AI für erweiterte Diagnosefähigkeiten","Iterative Schleifen können zusätzliche Rechenressourcen erfordern"],"pt":["Requer integração com Next.js e Supabase","Depende de Claude AI para capacidades de diagnóstico avançadas","Os loops iterativos podem exigir recursos computacionais adicionais"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Next.js и Supabase","Зависит от Claude AI для расширенных возможностей диагностики","Итерационные циклы могут требовать дополнительных вычислительных ресурсов"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع Next.js و Supabase","يعتمد على Claude AI للقدرات التشخيصية المتقدمة","الحلقات التكرارية قد تتطلب موارد حاسوبية إضافية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"14297f6531dd397ffab169c75a71c1274a7b012f4b7188116a5eb3ead50b4c52","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('LeighAtkins/OpenPaint/Writing Hookify Rules', 'community', 'LeighAtkins', 'OpenPaint', 'LeighAtkins/OpenPaint', 'Writing Hookify Rules', 0, 0, 60, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.904Z', '2026-03-02T02:17:07.569Z', 'cf7a6a0b92092f44c6532bd9af7189748a9c3b4d044005418230b08cc99ac55c', '{"id":"LeighAtkins/OpenPaint/Writing Hookify Rules","name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":{"zh":"Writing Hookify规则是AI智能工具，用于在照片上绘制图表","ja":"Hookifyルールの作成は、写真上に図を描くためのAIエージェントです","ko":"Hookify 규칙 작성은 사진에 다이어그램을 그리는 AI 에이전트입니다","es":"Este es un herramienta de pintura que puede ser utilizada para dibujar diagramas sobre fotos","fr":"Ceci est un outil de peinture qui peut être utilisé pour dessiner des diagrammes sur des photos","de":"Dies ist ein Malwerkzeug, das verwendet werden kann, um Diagramme über Fotos zu zeichnen","pt":"O Hookify é uma ferramenta de desenho que permite criar diagramas em cima de fotos","ru":"Hookify - это инструмент для рисования, который позволяет создавать диаграммы на фотографиях","ar":"Hookify هو أداة رسومات تمكنك من إنشاء مخططات على الصور","en":"This is a paint tool that can be used to draw diagrams on top of photos."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能工具：Writing Hookify 规则","ja":"AIエージェント：Hookify ルールの作成","ko":"AI 에이전트: Hookify 규칙 작성","es":"Escribir Reglas de Hookify para Agentes de Inteligencia A...","fr":"Écrire des règles de Hookify pour les agents de l''IA","de":"Schreiben von Hookify-Regeln für KI-Agenten","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Regras Hookify para Desenho","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Правила Hookify для Рисования","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: قواعد Hookify للرسم","en":"Writing Hookify Rules"},"description":{"zh":"Writing Hookify规则是AI智能工具，用于在照片上绘制图表","ja":"Hookifyルールの作成は、写真上に図を描くためのAIエージェントです","ko":"Hookify 규칙 작성은 사진에 다이어그램을 그리는 AI 에이전트입니다","es":"Este es un herramienta de pintura que puede ser utilizada para dibujar diagramas sobre fotos","fr":"Ceci est un outil de peinture qui peut être utilisé pour dessiner des diagrammes sur des photos","de":"Dies ist ein Malwerkzeug, das verwendet werden kann, um Diagramme über Fotos zu zeichnen","pt":"O Hookify é uma ferramenta de desenho que permite criar diagramas em cima de fotos","ru":"Hookify - это инструмент для рисования, который позволяет создавать диаграммы на фотографиях","ar":"Hookify هو أداة رسومات تمكنك من إنشاء مخططات على الصور","en":"This is a paint tool that can be used to draw diagrams on top of photos."},"definition":{"en":"This is a paint tool that can be used to draw diagrams on top of photos."},"features":{"zh":["基于AI的图表绘制","支持多种照片格式","简单易用的界面","高精度的图表识别","实时预览和编辑"],"ja":["AIベースの図の作成","複数の写真形式をサポート","シンプルで使いやすいインターフェース","高精度の図の認識","リアルタイムプレビューと編集"],"ko":["AI 기반 다이어그램 그리기","여러 사진 형식 지원","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운 인터페이스","고정밀도 다이어그램 인식","실시간 미리보기 및 편집"],"es":["Escribir reglas de Hookify para crear agentes de inteligencia artificial","Interactuar con diagramas y fotos","Crear agentes de inteligencia artificial que puedan aprender y mejorar","Utilizar un lenguaje de programación para definir las reglas de Hookify","Crear agentes de inteligencia artificial que puedan interactuar con otros agentes"],"fr":["Écrire des règles de Hookify pour créer des agents de l''IA","Interagir avec des diagrammes et des photos","Créer des agents de l''IA qui peuvent apprendre et améliorer","Utiliser un langage de programmation pour définir les règles de Hookify","Créer des agents de l''IA qui peuvent interagir avec d''autres agents"],"de":["Schreiben von Hookify-Regeln für die Erstellung von KI-Agenten","Interagieren mit Diagrammen und Fotos","Erstellen von KI-Agenten, die lernen und verbessern können","Verwenden eines Programmierungsprachens, um die Regeln von Hookify zu definieren","Erstellen von KI-Agenten, die mit anderen Agenten interagieren können"],"pt":["Desenho de diagramas em cima de fotos","Ferramenta de pintura avançada","Compatibilidade com múltiplos formatos de imagem","Interface de usuário intuitiva","Suporte a ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["Рисование диаграмм на фотографиях","Продвинутый инструмент для рисования","Совместимость с несколькими форматами изображений","Интуитивный интерфейс пользователя","Поддержка ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["رسم المخططات على الصور","أداة رسومات متقدمة","التوافق مع عدة صيغ للصور","واجهة مستخدم سهلة الاستخدام","دعم أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","Writing Hookify规则","图表绘制","照片编辑","AI图表识别","Hookify规则教程","AI工具下载","图表绘制软件"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Hookifyルールの作成","図の作成","写真編集","AI図の認識","Hookifyルールのチュートリアル","AIツールのダウンロード","図の作成ソフトウェア"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Hookify 규칙 작성","다이어그램 그리기","사진 편집","AI 다이어그램 인식","Hookify 규칙 튜토리얼","AI 도구 설치","다이어그램 그리기 소프트웨어"],"es":["Escribir reglas de Hookify","Crear agentes de inteligencia artificial","Interactuar con diagramas y fotos","Aprender a escribir reglas de Hookify","Escribir reglas de Hookify para crear agentes de inteligencia artificial","Escribir reglas de Hookify para crear agentes de inteligencia artificial que puedan aprender y mejorar"],"fr":["Écrire des règles de Hookify","Créer des agents de l''IA","Interagir avec des diagrammes et des photos","Apprendre à écrire des règles de Hookify","Écrire des règles de Hookify pour créer des agents de l''IA","Écrire des règles de Hookify pour créer des agents de l''IA qui peuvent apprendre et améliorer"],"de":["Schreiben von Hookify-Regeln","Erstellen von KI-Agenten","Interagieren mit Diagrammen und Fotos","Lernen Sie, wie man Hookify-Regeln schreibt","Schreiben von Hookify-Regeln für die Erstellung von KI-Agenten","Schreiben von Hookify-Regeln für die Erstellung von KI-Agenten, die lernen und verbessern können"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","regras Hookify","desenho de diagramas","ferramenta de pintura","como usar Hookify","alternativas ao Hookify","guia de instalação do Hookify"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","правила Hookify","рисование диаграмм","инструмент для рисования","как использовать Hookify","альтернативы Hookify","руководство по установке Hookify"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","قواعد Hookify","رسم المخططات","أداة رسومات","كيفية استخدام Hookify","بديلات Hookify","دليل تثبيت Hookify"]}},"owner":"LeighAtkins","repo":"OpenPaint","repoPath":"LeighAtkins/OpenPaint","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.904Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to create a hookify rule, write a hook rule, configure hookify, add a hookify rule, or needs guidance on hookify rule syntax and patterns.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggest","body":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggestions, etc.\n```\n\n### Frontmatter Fields\n\n**name** (required): Unique identifier for the rule\n- Use kebab-case: `warn-dangerous-rm`, `block-console-log`\n- Be descriptive and action-oriented\n- Start with verb: warn, prevent, block, require, check\n\n**enabled** (required): Boolean to activate/deactivate\n- `true`: Rule is active\n- `false`: Rule is disabled (won''t trigger)\n- Can toggle without deleting rule\n\n**event** (required): Which hook event to trigger on\n- `bash`: Bash tool commands\n- `file`: Edit, Write, MultiEdit tools\n- `stop`: When agent wants to stop\n- `prompt`: When user submits a prompt\n- `all`: All events\n\n**action** (optional): What to do when rule matches\n- `warn`: Show message but allow operation (default)\n- `block`: Prevent operation (PreToolUse) or stop session (Stop events)\n- If omitted, defaults to `warn`\n\n**pattern** (simple format): Regex pattern to match\n- Used for simple single-condition rules\n- Matches against command (bash) or new_text (file)\n- Python regex syntax\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\nevent: bash\npattern: rm\\s+-rf\n```\n\n### Advanced Format (Multiple Conditions)\n\nFor complex rules with multiple conditions:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: warn-env-file-edits\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.env$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: API_KEY\n---\n\nYou''re adding an API key to a .env file. Ensure this file is in .gitignore!\n```\n\n**Condition fields:**\n- `field`: Which field to check\n  - For bash: `command`\n  - For file: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- `operator`: How to match\n  - `regex_match`: Regex pattern matching\n  - `contains`: Substring check\n  - `equals`: Exact match\n  - `not_contains`: Substring must NOT be present\n  - `starts_with`: Prefix check\n  - `ends_with`: Suffix check\n- `pattern`: Pattern or string to match\n\n**All conditions must match for rule to trigger.**\n\n## Message Body\n\nThe markdown content after frontmatter is shown to Claude when the rule triggers.\n\n**Good messages:**\n- Explain what was detected\n- Explain why it''s problematic\n- Suggest alternatives or best practices\n- Use formatting for clarity (bold, lists, etc.)\n\n**Example:**\n```markdown\n⚠️ **Console.log detected!**\n\nYou''re adding console.log to production code.\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Debug logs shouldn''t ship to production\n- Console.log can expose sensitive data\n- Impacts browser performance\n\n**Alternatives:**\n- Use a proper logging library\n- Remove before committing\n- Use conditional debug builds\n```\n\n## Event Type Guide\n\n### bash Events\n\nMatch Bash command patterns:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: bash\npattern: sudo\\s+|rm\\s+-rf|chmod\\s+777\n---\n\nDangerous command detected!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Dangerous commands: `rm\\s+-rf`, `dd\\s+if=`, `mkfs`\n- Privilege escalation: `sudo\\s+`, `su\\s+`\n- Permission issues: `chmod\\s+777`, `chown\\s+root`\n\n### file Events\n\nMatch Edit/Write/MultiEdit operations:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\npattern: console\\.log\\(|eval\\(|innerHTML\\s*=\n---\n\nPotentially problematic code pattern detected!\n```\n\n**Match on different fields:**\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.tsx?$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: console\\.log\\(\n---\n\nConsole.log in TypeScript file!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Debug code: `console\\.log\\(`, `debugger`, `print\\(`\n- Security risks: `eval\\(`, `innerHTML\\s*=`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- Sensitive files: `\\.env$`, `credentials`, `\\.pem$`\n- Generated files: `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`\n\n### stop Events\n\nMatch when agent wants to stop (completion checks):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: stop\npattern: .*\n---\n\nBefore stopping, verify:\n- [ ] Tests were run\n- [ ] Build succeeded\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n```\n\n**Use for:**\n- Reminders about required steps\n- Completion checklists\n- Process enforcement\n\n### prompt Events\n\nMatch user prompt content (advanced):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: prompt\nconditions:\n  - field: user_prompt\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: deploy to production\n---\n\nProduction deployment checklist:\n- [ ] Tests passing?\n- [ ] Reviewed by team?\n- [ ] Monitoring ready?\n```\n\n## Pattern Writing Tips\n\n### Regex Basics\n\n**Literal characters:** Most characters match themselves\n- `rm` matches \"rm\"\n- `console.log` matches \"console.log\"\n\n**Special characters need escaping:**\n- `.` (any char) → `\\.` (literal dot)\n- `(` `)` → `\\(` `\\)` (literal parens)\n- `[` `]` → `\\[` `\\]` (literal brackets)\n\n**Common metacharacters:**\n- `\\s` - whitespace (space, tab, newline)\n- `\\d` - digit (0-9)\n- `\\w` - word character (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, _)\n- `.` - any character\n- `+` - one or more\n- `*` - zero or more\n- `?` - zero or one\n- `|` - OR\n\n**Examples:**\n```\nrm\\s+-rf         Matches: rm -rf, rm  -rf\nconsole\\.log\\(   Matches: console.log(\n(eval|exec)\\(    Matches: eval( or exec(\nchmod\\s+777      Matches: chmod 777, chmod  777\nAPI_KEY\\s*=      Matches: API_KEY=, API_KEY =\n```\n\n### Testing Patterns\n\nTest regex patterns before using:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"import re; print(re.search(r''your_pattern'', ''test text''))\"\n```\n\nOr use online regex testers (regex101.com with Python flavor).\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Too broad:**\n```yaml\npattern: log    # Matches \"log\", \"login\", \"dialog\", \"catalog\"\n```\nBetter: `console\\.log\\(|logger\\.`\n\n**Too specific:**\n```yaml\npattern: rm -rf /tmp  # Only matches exact path\n```\nBetter: `rm\\s+-rf`\n\n**Escaping issues:**\n- YAML quoted strings: `\"pattern\"` requires double backslashes `\\\\s`\n- YAML unquoted: `pattern: \\s` works as-is\n- **Recommendation**: Use unquoted patterns in YAML\n\n## File Organization\n\n**Location:** All rules in `.claude/` directory\n**Naming:** `.claude/hookify.{descriptive-name}.local.md`\n**Gitignore:** Add `.claude/*.local.md` to `.gitignore`\n\n**Good names:**\n- `hookify.dangerous-rm.local.md`\n- `hookify.console-log.local.md`\n- `hookify.require-tests.local.md`\n- `hookify.sensitive-files.local.md`\n\n**Bad names:**\n- `hookify.rule1.local.md` (not descriptive)\n- `hookify.md` (missing .local)\n- `danger.local.md` (missing hookify prefix)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Creating a Rule\n\n1. Identify unwanted behavior\n2. Determine which tool is involved (Bash, Edit, etc.)\n3. Choose event type (bash, file, stop, etc.)\n4. Write regex pattern\n5. Create `.claude/hookify.{name}.local.md` file in project root\n6. Test immediately - rules are read dynamically on next tool use\n\n### Refining a Rule\n\n1. Edit the `.local.md` file\n2. Adjust pattern or message\n3. Test immediately - changes take effect on next tool use\n\n### Disabling a Rule\n\n**Temporary:** Set `enabled: false` in frontmatter\n**Permanent:** Delete the `.local.md` file\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/examples/` for complete examples:\n- `dangerous-rm.local.md` - Block dangerous rm commands\n- `console-log-warning.local.md` - Warn about console.log\n- `sensitive-files-warning.local.md` - Warn about editing .env files\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n**Minimum viable rule:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: bash\npattern: dangerous_command\n---\n\nWarning message here\n```\n\n**Rule with conditions:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.ts$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: any\n---\n\nWarning message\n```\n\n**Event types:**\n- `bash` - Bash commands\n- `file` - File edits\n- `stop` - Completion checks\n- `prompt` - User input\n- `all` - All events\n\n**Field options:**\n- Bash: `command`\n- File: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- Prompt: `user_prompt`\n\n**Operators:**\n- `regex_match`, `contains`, `equals`, `not_contains`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:17:07.569Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced Language Agents needing customized event handling and pattern matching capabilities.","zh":"适合需要自定义事件处理和模式匹配能力的高级语言代理。","ja":"高度な言語エージェントがカスタマイズされたイベント処理とパターンマッチング機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 언어 에이전트가 사용자 정의 이벤트 처리 및 패턴 매칭 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que necesitan un manejo de eventos personalizado y capacidades de coincidencia de patrones.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage Avancés ayant besoin d''une gestion d''événements personnalisée et de capacités de correspondance de modèles.","de":"Perfekt für Advanced Language Agents, die ein benutzerdefiniertes Ereignishandling und Musterabgleichfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que necessitam de tratamento de eventos personalizados e capacidades de correspondência de padrões.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Продвинутых Языковых Агентов, требующих настраиваемой обработки событий и возможностей сопоставления с образцом.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء اللغوية المتقدمة التي تحتاج إلى التعامل مع الأحداث المخصصة وقدرات مطابقة الأنماط."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define event-driven responses using YAML frontmatter and regex patterns in markdown files, supporting bash, file, stop, prompt, or all events, and enables the display of custom messages with markdown formatting.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用 YAML 前置内容和 markdown 文件中的正则表达式模式的事件驱动响应的能力，支持 bash、文件、停止、提示或所有事件，并允许使用 markdown 格式显示自定义消息。","ja":"YAML フロントマターと Markdown ファイル内の正規表現パターンを使用してイベント駆動のレスポンスを定義するエージェントの能力を与え、bash、ファイル、停止、プロンプト、またはすべてのイベントをサポートし、Markdown フォーマットでカスタム メッセージを表示できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 YAML 프론티어와 마크다운 파일 내의 정규식 패턴을 사용하여 이벤트 주도 응답을 정의할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며 bash, 파일, 중지, 프롬프트 또는 모든 이벤트를 지원하며 마크다운 형식으로 사용자 정의 메시지를 표시할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir respuestas basadas en eventos utilizando YAML frontmatter y patrones regex en archivos markdown, que admiten eventos bash, archivo, detener, prompt o todos los eventos, y permite la visualización de mensajes personalizados con formato markdown.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des réponses basées sur les événements en utilisant YAML frontmatter et des modèles regex dans des fichiers markdown, prenant en charge les événements bash, fichier, arrêter, invite ou tous les événements, et permet d''afficher des messages personnalisés avec une mise en forme markdown.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, ereignisgesteuerte Antworten unter Verwendung von YAML-Frontmatter und Regex-Mustern in Markdown-Dateien zu definieren, die bash-, Datei-, Stop-, Prompt- oder alle Ereignisse unterstützen, und ermöglicht die Anzeige von benutzerdefinierten Nachrichten mit Markdown-Formatierung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definir respostas orientadas a eventos usando YAML frontmatter e padrões regex em arquivos markdown, suportando eventos bash, arquivo, parar, prompt ou todos os eventos, e permite a exibição de mensagens personalizadas com formatação markdown.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность определять событийно-ориентированные ответы с использованием YAML frontmatter и шаблонов regex в файлах markdown, поддерживая события bash, файл, остановка, приглашение или все события, и позволяет отображать пользовательские сообщения с форматированием markdown.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تعريف استجابات مدفوعة بالأحداث باستخدام YAML frontmatter ونماذج regex في ملفات markdown، مع دعم أحداث bash وملف وايقاف وتسجيل الدخول أو جميع الأحداث، ويمكّن عرض رسائل مخصصة بتنسيق markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining custom event handlers for Claude","Creating pattern-based responses for specific user inputs","Generating markdown-formatted messages for agent interactions"],"zh":["为 Claude 定义自定义事件处理程序","为特定用户输入创建基于模式的响应","为代理交互生成带有 markdown 格式的消息"],"ja":["Claude のカスタム イベント ハンドラーを定義する","特定のユーザー入力に対してパターン ベースのレスポンスを作成する","エージェントのやり取り用に Markdown フォーマットのメッセージを生成する"],"ko":["Claude의 사용자 정의 이벤트 핸들러를 정의","특정 사용자 입력에 대한 패턴 기반 응답 생성","에이전트 상호 작용을 위한 마크다운 형식의 메시지 생성"],"es":["Definir controladores de eventos personalizados para Claude","Crear respuestas basadas en patrones para entradas de usuario específicas","Generar mensajes con formato markdown para interacciones de agentes"],"fr":["Définir des gestionnaires d''événements personnalisés pour Claude","Créer des réponses basées sur des modèles pour des entrées utilisateur spécifiques","Générer des messages avec une mise en forme markdown pour les interactions d''agents"],"de":["Definieren benutzerdefinierter Ereignishandler für Claude","Erstellen musterbasierter Antworten für spezifische Benutzereingaben","Generieren von Nachrichten mit Markdown-Formatierung für Agenteninteraktionen"],"pt":["Definindo manipuladores de eventos personalizados para Claude","Criando respostas baseadas em padrões para entradas de usuário específicas","Gerando mensagens formatadas em markdown para interações de agente"],"ru":["Определение пользовательских обработчиков событий для Claude","Создание ответов на основе шаблонов для конкретных входных данных пользователя","Генерация сообщений, отформатированных в markdown, для взаимодействия агента"],"ar":["تعريف معالجات أحداث مخصصة ل Claude","إنشاء استجابات قائمة على الأنماط لمدخلات المستخدم الخاصة","توليد رسائل بتنسيق markdown لتفاعلات الوكيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires storage of rules in .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md files","Dependent on YAML frontmatter and markdown file format","Regex pattern matching capabilities may require additional expertise"],"zh":["需要将规则存储在 .claude/hookify.{规则名称}.local.md 文件中","依赖于 YAML 前置内容和 markdown 文件格式","正则表达式模式匹配功能可能需要额外的专业知识"],"ja":["ルールを .claude/hookify.{ルール名}.local.md ファイルに保存する必要がある","YAML フロントマターと Markdown ファイル形式に依存する","正規表現パターン マッチング機能には追加の専門知識が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["규칙을 .claude/hookify.{규칙 이름}.local.md 파일에 저장해야 함","YAML 프론티어와 마크다운 파일 형식에 의존","정규식 패턴 매칭 기능은 추가 전문 지식이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere el almacenamiento de reglas en archivos .claude/hookify.{nombre-de-regla}.local.md","Dependiente del formato de frontmatter YAML y de archivo markdown","Las capacidades de coincidencia de patrones regex pueden requerir experiencia adicional"],"fr":["Nécessite le stockage des règles dans des fichiers .claude/hookify.{nom-de-règle}.local.md","Dépendant du format de frontmatter YAML et de fichier markdown","Les capacités de correspondance de modèles regex peuvent nécessiter une expertise supplémentaire"],"de":["Erfordert die Speicherung von Regeln in Dateien .claude/hookify.{regelname}.local.md","Abhängig vom YAML-Frontmatter- und Markdown-Dateiformat","Die Regex-Musterabgleichfähigkeiten können zusätzliche Expertise erfordern"],"pt":["Requer armazenamento de regras em arquivos .claude/hookify.{nome-da-regra}.local.md","Dependente do formato de arquivo YAML frontmatter e markdown","As capacidades de correspondência de padrão regex podem exigir conhecimento adicional"],"ru":["Требует хранения правил в файлах .claude/hookify.{имя-правила}.local.md","Зависит от формата файла YAML frontmatter и markdown","Возможности сопоставления с образцом regex могут требовать дополнительного опыта"],"ar":["يتطلب تخزين القواعد في ملفات .claude/hookify.{اسم-القاعدة}.local.md","يعتمد على تنسيق ملف YAML frontmatter و markdown","قد تتطلب إمكانيات مطابقة النمط regex خبرة إضافية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"cf7a6a0b92092f44c6532bd9af7189748a9c3b4d044005418230b08cc99ac55c","qualityScore":60}');
