-review","ar":"عاملات الذكاء الاصطناعي dyad:multi-pr-review","en":"dyad:multi-pr-review"},"description":{"zh":"dyad是一个本地、开源的AI应用构建工具，支持多人代码审查，适用于高级用户","ja":"dyadはローカル、オープンソースのAIアプリビルダーで、マルチプルコードレビュー機能を備えています","ko":"dyad는 로컬, 오픈소스 AI 앱 빌더로 멀티 프로그래머 코드 리뷰 기능을 제공합니다","es":"dyad:multi-pr-review es una aplicación de código abierto para constructores de aplicaciones AI locales para usuarios avanzados, similar a Replit o Bolt","fr":"dyad:multi-pr-review est une application open-source pour les constructeurs d''applications AI locaux pour les utilisateurs avancés, similaire à Replit ou Bolt","de":"dyad:multi-pr-review ist eine Open-Source-Anwendung für lokale AI-App-Entwickler für Power-User, ähnlich wie Replit oder Bolt","pt":"O dyad:multi-pr-review é uma ferramenta de código aberto para construir aplicativos AI locais para usuários avançados, alternativa ao Replit e Bolt","ru":"dyad:multi-pr-review - это открытый ИИ инструмент для создания локальных приложений для продвинутых пользователей, альтернатива Replit и Bolt","ar":"dyad:multi-pr-review هو أداة مفتوحة المصدر لبناء تطبيقات الذكاء الاصطناعي المحلية لمستخدمي الطرف الثالث، بديل ل Replit و Bolt","en":"Local, open-source AI app builder for power users ✨ v0 / Lovable / Replit / Bolt alternative 🌟 Star if you like it!"},"definition":{"en":"Local, open-source AI app builder for power users ✨ v0 / Lovable / Replit / Bolt alternative 🌟 Star if you like it!"},"features":{"zh":["本地、开源的AI应用构建工具","支持多人代码审查","适用于高级用户","提供代码审查功能","Lovable、Replit、Bolt替代品"],"ja":["ローカル、オープンソースのAIアプリビルダー","マルチプルコードレビュー機能","パワーユーザー向け","コードレビュー機能あり","Lovable、Replit、Boltの代替"],"ko":["로컬, 오픈소스 AI 앱 빌더","멀티 프로그래머 코드 리뷰 기능","파워 유저를 위한 기능","코드 리뷰 기능 제공","Lovable, Replit, Bolt의 대안"],"es":["Código abierto","Aplicación local","Similar a Replit o Bolt","Para usuarios avanzados","Construcción de aplicaciones AI","Alternativa a otras herramientas de AI"],"fr":["Open-source","Application locale","Similaire à Replit ou Bolt","Pour les utilisateurs avancés","Conception d''applications AI","Alternative à d''autres outils d''IA"],"de":["Open-Source","Lokale Anwendung","Ähnlich wie Replit oder Bolt","Für Power-User","Erstellung von AI-Anwendungen","Alternative zu anderen KI-Tools"],"pt":["Código aberto","Construção de aplicativos AI locais","Alternativa ao Replit e Bolt","Ferramenta para usuários avançados","Suporte a múltiplos protocolos"],"ru":["Открытый код","Создание локальных приложений ИИ","Альтернатива Replit и Bolt","Инструмент для продвинутых пользователей","Поддержка нескольких протоколов"],"ar":["كود مفتوح","بناء تطبيقات الذكاء الاصطناعي المحلية","بديل ل Replit و Bolt","أداة لمستخدمي الطرف الثالث","دعم بروتوكولات متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","代码审查","AI应用构建","dyad教程","Lovable替代品","Replit替代品","Bolt替代品","如何使用dyad","dyad安装"],"ja":["AIエージェント","コードレビュー","AIアプリビルダー","dyadチュートリアル","Lovableの代替","Replitの代替","Boltの代替","dyadの使い方","dyadのインストール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","코드 리뷰","AI 앱 빌더","dyad 사용법","Lovable의 대안","Replit의 대안","Bolt의 대안","dyad 설치 가이드","dyad 설정 방법"],"es":["herramientas de AI","dyad multi-pr-review","alternativa a Replit","cómo usar dyad","qué es dyad","instalación de dyad","guía de configuración de dyad","dyad vs Replit","dyad vs Bolt"],"fr":["outils d''IA","dyad multi-pr-review","alternative à Replit","comment utiliser dyad","qu''est-ce que dyad","installation de dyad","guide de configuration de dyad","dyad vs Replit","dyad vs Bolt"],"de":["KI-Tools","dyad multi-pr-review","Alternative zu Replit","wie man dyad verwendet","was ist dyad","Installation von dyad","Konfigurationsanleitung für dyad","dyad vs Replit","dyad vs Bolt"],"pt":["como usar dyad:multi-pr-review","o que é dyad:multi-pr-review","dyad:multi-pr-review alternativa","dyad:multi-pr-review vs Replit","instalar dyad:multi-pr-review","guia de configuração dyad:multi-pr-review"],"ru":["как использовать dyad:multi-pr-review","что такое dyad:multi-pr-review","dyad:multi-pr-review альтернатива","dyad:multi-pr-review vs Replit","установить dyad:multi-pr-review","руководство по настройке dyad:multi-pr-review"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام dyad:multi-pr-review","ما هو dyad:multi-pr-review","dyad:multi-pr-review بديل","dyad:multi-pr-review مقابل Replit","تثبيت dyad:multi-pr-review","دليل إعداد dyad:multi-pr-review"]}},"owner":"dyad-sh","repo":"dyad","repoPath":"dyad-sh/dyad","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.916Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dyad:multi-pr-review","description":"Multi-agent code review system that spawns three independent Claude sub-agents to review PR diffs. Each agent receives files in different randomized order to reduce ordering bias. One agent focuses specifically on code health and maintainability. Issues are validated using reasoned analysis rather than simple vote counting. Reports merge verdict (YES / NOT SURE / NO). Automatically deduplicates against existing PR comments. Always posts a summary (even if no new issues), with low priority issues in a collapsible section.","bodyPreview":"# Multi-Agent PR Review\n\nThis skill spawns three independent sub-agents to review code changes from different perspectives, then validates and aggregates their findings through reasoned analysis.\n\n## Overview\n\n1. Fetch PR diff and existing comments\n2. Spawn 3 sub-agents with specialized personas using the Task tool\n   - Each agent receives files in a different randomized order to reduce ordering bias\n   - **Correctness Expert**: Bugs, edge cases, control flow, security, error handling\n   - **Cod","body":"# Multi-Agent PR Review\n\nThis skill spawns three independent sub-agents to review code changes from different perspectives, then validates and aggregates their findings through reasoned analysis.\n\n## Overview\n\n1. Fetch PR diff and existing comments\n2. Spawn 3 sub-agents with specialized personas using the Task tool\n   - Each agent receives files in a different randomized order to reduce ordering bias\n   - **Correctness Expert**: Bugs, edge cases, control flow, security, error handling\n   - **Code Health Expert**: Dead code, duplication, complexity, meaningful comments, abstractions\n   - **UX Wizard**: User experience, consistency, accessibility, error states, delight\n3. Each agent reviews and classifies issues (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW severity)\n4. Validate issues using reasoned analysis (not just vote counting)\n5. Determine merge verdict based on confirmed issues\n6. Filter out issues already commented on (deduplication)\n7. Post findings: summary with verdict + inline comments for HIGH/MEDIUM issues\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Determine PR Number and Repo\n\nParse the PR number and repo from the user''s input. If not provided, try to infer from the current git context:\n\n```bash\n# Get current repo\ngh repo view --json nameWithOwner -q ''.nameWithOwner''\n\n# If user provides a PR URL, extract the number\n# If user just says \"review this PR\", check for current branch PR\ngh pr view --json number -q ''.number''\n```\n\n### Step 2: Fetch PR Diff and Context\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Always save files to the current working directory (e.g. `./pr_diff.patch`), never to `/tmp/` or other directories outside the repo. In CI, only the repo working directory is accessible.\n\n```bash\n# Save the diff to current working directory (NOT /tmp/)\ngh pr diff <PR_NUMBER> --repo <OWNER/REPO> > ./pr_diff.patch\n\n# Get PR metadata\ngh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --repo <OWNER/REPO> --json title,body,files,headRefOid\n\n# Fetch existing comments to avoid duplicates\ngh api repos/<OWNER/REPO>/pulls/<PR_NUMBER>/comments --paginate\ngh api repos/<OWNER/REPO>/issues/<PR_NUMBER>/comments --paginate\n```\n\nSave the diff content and existing comments for use in the review.\n\n### Step 3: Spawn Review Agents in Parallel\n\nUse the `Task` tool to spawn 3 sub-agents **in parallel** (all in a single message with multiple Task tool calls). Each agent should be a `general-purpose` subagent.\n\n**File Ordering**: Before spawning, create 3 different orderings of the changed files (randomize/shuffle the order). Each agent gets the files in a different order to reduce ordering bias (reviewers tend to focus more on files they see first).\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Each agent''s prompt must include:\n\n1. Their role description (from the corresponding file in `references/`)\n2. The full PR diff content (inline, NOT a file path - agents cannot read files from the parent''s context)\n3. The list of existing PR comments (so they can avoid flagging already-commented issues)\n4. Instructions to output findings as structured JSON\n\n#### Agent Prompt Template\n\nFor each agent, the prompt should follow this structure:\n\n````\nYou are a code reviewer with this specialization:\n\n<role>\n[Contents of references/<role>.md - e.g., correctness-reviewer.md]\n</role>\n\nYou are reviewing PR #<NUMBER> in <REPO>: \"<PR TITLE>\"\n\n<pr_description>\n[PR body/description]\n</pr_description>\n\nHere is the diff to review (files presented in a specific order for this review):\n\n<diff>\n[Full diff content - with files in THIS agent''s randomized order]\n</diff>\n\nHere are existing PR comments (do NOT flag issues already commented on):\n\n<existing_comments>\n[Existing comment data as JSON]\n</existing_comments>\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read your role description carefully and review the diff from your expert perspective.\n2. For each issue you find, classify it as HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW severity using the guidelines in your role description.\n3. Output your findings as a JSON array with this schema:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"path/to/file.ts\",\n    \"line_start\": 42,\n    \"line_end\": 45,\n    \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n    \"category\": \"category-name\",\n    \"title\": \"Brief title\",\n    \"description\": \"Clear description of the issue and its impact\",\n    \"suggestion\": \"How to fix (optional)\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nSeverity levels:\n- HIGH: Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, crashes, broken functionality, UX blockers\n- MEDIUM: Logic errors, edge cases, performance issues, sloppy code that hurts maintainability, UX issues that degrade the experience\n- LOW: Minor style issues, nitpicks, minor polish improvements\n\nBe thorough but focused. Only flag real issues, not nitpicks disguised as higher severity issues.\n\nIMPORTANT: Cross-reference infrastructure changes (DB migrations, new tables/columns, API endpoints, config entries) against actual usage in the diff. If a migration creates a table but no code in the PR reads from or writes to it, that''s dead infrastructure and should be flagged.\n\nOutput ONLY the JSON array, no other text.\n````\n\n### Step 4: Collect and Parse Results\n\nWait for all 3 agents to complete. Parse the JSON array from each agent''s response.\n\n### Step 5: Validate Issues with Reasoned Analysis\n\n**Do NOT use simple consensus voting (e.g., \"2+ agents agree\").** Instead, perform reasoned validation:\n\nFor each unique issue found (group similar issues by file + approximate line range):\n\n1. **Evaluate validity**: Is this a real issue or a false positive? Consider:\n   - Does the code actually have this problem?\n   - Is the reviewer misunderstanding the code''s purpose?\n   - Is this issue already handled elsewhere in the codebase?\n\n2. **Evaluate severity**: Is the severity rating correct? Consider:\n   - What''s the actual user/system impact?\n   - Is this being over- or under-rated?\n\n3. **Make a decision**:\n   - **CONFIRMED**: Issue is valid and severity is appropriate\n   - **CONFIRMED (adjusted)**: Issue is valid but severity should be changed\n   - **DROPPED**: Issue is a false positive, explain why\n\nTrack dropped issues with reasoning for the summary comment.\n\n### Step 6: Determine Merge Verdict\n\nBased on the confirmed issues, determine the verdict:\n\n- **:white_check_mark: YES - Ready to merge**: No HIGH issues, at most minor MEDIUM issues that are judgment calls\n- **:thinking: NOT SURE - Potential issues**: Has MEDIUM issues that should probably be addressed, but none are clear blockers\n- **:no_entry: NO - Do NOT merge**: Has HIGH severity issues or multiple serious MEDIUM issues that NEED to be fixed\n\n### Step 7: Deduplicate Against Existing Comments\n\nBefore posting, filter out issues that match existing PR comments:\n\n- Same file path\n- Same or nearby line number (within 3 lines)\n- Similar keywords in the issue title appear in the existing comment body\n\n### Step 8: Post GitHub Comments\n\n#### Summary Comment\n\nPost a summary comment on the PR using `gh pr comment`:\n\n```markdown\n## :mag: Dyadbot Code Review Summary\n\n**Verdict: [VERDICT EMOJI + TEXT]**\n\nReviewed by 3 independent agents: Correctness Expert, Code Health Expert, UX Wizard.\n\n### Issues Summary\n\n| Severity               | File                  | Issue                  |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| :red_circle: HIGH      | `src/auth.ts:45`      | SQL injection in login |\n| :yellow_circle: MEDIUM | `src/ui/modal.tsx:12` | Missing loading state  |\n\n<details>\n<summary>:green_circle: Low Priority Notes (X items)</summary>\n\n- **Minor naming inconsistency** - `src/helpers.ts:23`\n- **Could add hover state** - `src/button.tsx:15`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>:no_entry_sign: Dropped False Positives (X items)</summary>\n\n- **~~Potential race condition~~** - Dropped: State is only accessed synchronously in this context\n- **~~Missing null check~~** - Dropped: Value is guaranteed non-null by the caller''s validation\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n_Generated by Dyadbot multi-agent code review_\n```\n\n**Always post a summary**, even if no issues are found. In that case:\n\n```markdown\n## :mag: Dyadbot Code Review Summary\n\n**Verdict: :white_check_mark: YES - Ready to merge**\n\n:white_check_mark: No issues found by multi-agent review.\n\n---\n\n_Generated by Dyadbot multi-agent code review_\n```\n\n#### Inline Comments\n\nFor each HIGH and MEDIUM issue, post an inline review comment at the relevant line using `gh api`:\n\n```bash\n# Post a review with inline comments\ngh api repos/<OWNER/REPO>/pulls/<PR_NUMBER>/reviews \\\n  -X POST \\\n  --input payload.json\n```\n\nWhere payload.json contains:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"commit_id\": \"<HEAD_SHA from PR metadata>\",\n  \"body\": \"Multi-agent review: X issue(s) found\",\n  \"event\": \"COMMENT\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/auth.ts\",\n      \"line\": 45,\n      \"body\": \"**:red_circle: HIGH** | security\\n\\n**SQL injection in login**\\n\\nDescription of the issue...\\n\\n:bulb: **Suggestion:** Use parameterized queries\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Severity Guidelines\n\nAcross all reviewers:\n\n- **HIGH**: Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, crashes, broken functionality, race conditions, UX blockers\n- **MEDIUM**: Logic errors, unhandled edge cases, performance issues, sloppy code that hurts maintainability, poor error messages, missing loading/empty states, accessibility gaps\n- **LOW**: Minor style issues, naming nitpicks, optional polish improvements\n\n**Philosophy**: Sloppy code that hurts maintainability is MEDIUM, not LOW. We care about code health.\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\nreferences/\n  correctness-reviewer.md  - Role description for the correctness expert\n  code-health-reviewer.md  - Role description for the code health expert\n  ux-reviewer.md           - Role description for the UX wizard\n  issue_schema.md          - JSON schema for issue output\n```\n\n## Configuration Notes\n\n- **No Python scripts needed**: This skill executes entirely through Claude Code tools\n- **No ANTHROPIC_API_KEY needed**: Sub-agents spawned via Task tool have automatic access\n- **GITHUB_TOKEN required**: For PR access and commenting (usually already configured)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:25:35.474Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing multi-perspective analysis and validation of code changes.","zh":"适合需要多角度分析和验证代码更改的代码审查代理","ja":"コードの変更を多角的分析および検証するコードレビュー代理に最適","ko":"코드 변경의 다각도 분석 및 검증이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan un análisis y validación de cambios de código desde múltiples perspectivas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Révision de Code nécessitant une analyse et une validation des modifications de code à partir de plusieurs perspectives.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die eine Analyse und Validierung von Code-Änderungen aus mehreren Perspektiven benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise e validação de alterações de código de múltiplas perspectivas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов проверки кода, требующих многостороннего анализа и проверки изменений кода.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة الكود الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل وتحقق التغييرات في الكود من منظور متعددة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform comprehensive PR reviews by spawning independent sub-agents with specialized personas, such as Correctness Experts, to analyze code diffs and validate findings through reasoned analysis, utilizing Task tools and reducing ordering bias.","zh":"赋予代理通过生成具有专业人格的独立子代理（如正确性专家）来执行全面PR审查的能力，分析代码差异并通过推理分析验证发现，利用Task工具并减少排序偏见","ja":"コード差分の分析や発見の検証を通じて、タスクツールを利用し、順序バイアスを減らすことで、正確性の専門家などの特化したペルソナを持つ独立したサブエージェントを生成し、包括的なPRレビューを実行するエージェントの能力を付与","ko":"에이전트에게 독립적인 하위 에이전트를 생성하여 코드 차이 분석 및发现의 검증을 수행하고, Task 도구를 사용하고, 정렬 편향을 줄이는 것을 통해 포괄적인 PR 리뷰를 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar revisiones de PR comprehensivas mediante la creación de subagentes independientes con personas especializadas, como Expertos en Corrección, para analizar diffs de código y validar hallazgos a través de un análisis razonado, utilizando herramientas de Task y reduciendo el sesgo de ordenación.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des examens de PR complets en créant des sous-agents indépendants avec des personas spécialisées, comme des Experts en Correction, pour analyser les diffs de code et valider les résultats via une analyse raisonnée, en utilisant des outils Task et en réduisant les biais d''ordre.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende PR-Überprüfungen durchzuführen, indem unabhängige Subagenten mit spezialisierten Persönlichkeiten, wie Korrektheitsexperten, erstellt werden, um Code-Diffs zu analysieren und Ergebnisse durch eine begründete Analyse zu validieren, unter Verwendung von Task-Tools und Verringerung von Ordnungsvoreingenommenheit.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar revisões abrangentes de PR, criando sub-agentes independentes com personas especializadas, como Especialistas em Correção, para analisar diferenças de código e validar descobertas por meio de análise fundamentada, utilizando ferramentas de Tarefa e reduzindo vies de ordenação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить комплексные проверки PR, создавая независимых субагентов с специализированными персонами, такими как Эксперты по Правильности, для анализа различий кода и проверки результатов посредством обоснованного анализа, используя инструменты Задачи и уменьшая предвзятость упорядочения.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إجراء مراجعات شاملة للـ PR من خلال إنشاء وكلاء فرعيين مستقلين مع شخصيات متخصصة، مثل أصحاب الخبرة في الدقة، لتحليل اختلافات الكود و التحقق من النتائج من خلال تحليل مدروس، باستخدام أدوات المهمة و تقليل انحياز الترتيب."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for bug detection and security audits","Validating code changes through multi-agent analysis and aggregation of findings","Debugging complex code issues by leveraging diverse perspectives from sub-agents"],"zh":["自动化代码审查以检测错误和安全审计","通过多代理分析和发现聚合来验证代码更改","利用多样化的子代理视角来调试复杂的代码问题"],"ja":["バグ検出とセキュリティ監査のためのコードレビューの自動化","コード変更の検証をマルチエージェント分析および発見の集約により実施","サブエージェントからの多様な視点を活用して複雑なコードの問題をデバッグ"],"ko":["버그 탐지 및 보안 감사를 위한 코드 리뷰 자동화","코드 변경 검증을 다중 에이전트 분석 및 발견 집약을 통해 수행","하위 에이전트의 다양화된 관점을 활용하여 복잡한 코드 문제를 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para la detección de errores y auditorías de seguridad","Validación de cambios de código a través de un análisis y agregación de resultados de múltiples agentes","Depuración de problemas de código complejos aprovechando diferentes perspectivas de subagentes"],"fr":["Automatisation des examens de code pour la détection des bogues et les audits de sécurité","Validation des modifications de code via une analyse et une agrégation de résultats de plusieurs agents","Débogage de problèmes de code complexes en exploitant des perspectives diverses de sous-agents"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews zur Fehlererkennung und Sicherheitsaudits","Validierung von Code-Änderungen durch Analyse und Aggregation von Ergebnissen mehrerer Agenten","Fehlerbehebung komplexer Codeprobleme durch Nutzung verschiedener Perspektiven von Subagenten"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para detecção de bugs e auditorias de segurança","Validar alterações de código por meio de análise e agregação de descobertas de múltiplos agentes","Depurar problemas de código complexos aproveitando perspectivas diversificadas de sub-agentes"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода для обнаружения ошибок и аудита безопасности","Проверить изменения кода посредством анализа и агрегации результатов от нескольких агентов","Отладить сложные проблемы кода, используя разнообразные перспективы субагентов"],"ar":["توفير مراجعات الكود آليًا للكشف عن الأخطاء ومراجعة الأمن","التحقق من التغييرات في الكود من خلال التحليل ودمج النتائج من وكلاء متعددين","تصحيح مشاكل الكود المعقدة من خلال الاستفادة من المنظورات المتنوعة للوكلاء التابعين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Task tool integration","Limited to code review use cases","Dependent on quality and specialization of spawned sub-agents"],"zh":["需要Task工具集成","仅限代码审查用例","依赖于生成的子代理的质量和专业化"],"ja":["タスクツールの統合が必要","コードレビュー用途のみ","生成されたサブエージェントの品質と特化度に依存"],"ko":["Task 도구 통합 필요","코드 리뷰 사용 사례에만 제한","생성된 하위 에이전트의 품질 및 전문성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere integración de herramientas de Task","Limitado a casos de uso de revisión de código","Dependiente de la calidad y especialización de los subagentes creados"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration d''outils Task","Limité aux cas d''usage de révision de code","Dépend de la qualité et de la spécialisation des sous-agents créés"],"de":["Benötigt eine Integration von Task-Tools","Begrenzt auf Code-Review-Anwendungsfälle","Abhängig von der Qualität und Spezialisierung der erstellten Subagenten"],"pt":["Requer integração com ferramenta de Tarefa","Limitado a casos de uso de revisão de código","Dependente da qualidade e especialização dos sub-agentes criados"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с инструментом Задачи","Ограничен случаи использования проверки кода","Зависит от качества и специализации созданных субагентов"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع أداة المهمة","محدود لحالات استخدام مراجعة الكود","يعتمد على جودة وتخصص الوكلاء التابعين المولدين"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"0573b2e9c7042a2cb78f0f7a5dd2068b0f6c0690698ebf6aab2ff1cd9ccc1a5f","qualityScore":60}');
