rrold/finder","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.952Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bmad-planner","description":"|","version":"5.1.0","bodyPreview":"# BMAD Planner\n\n## Purpose\n\nBusiness Model, Architecture, and Design documentation created in main\nrepository before feature development begins.\n\n**Now available as an interactive callable Python script** - saves ~2,000-2,700 tokens per feature compared to manual reproduction.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Current directory: main repository (not worktree)\n- Current branch: `contrib/<gh-user>`\n- Phase: Planning (Phase 1)\n\n## Interactive Callable Tool\n\nBMAD is now an **interactive callable tool** that runs a","body":"# BMAD Planner\n\n## Purpose\n\nBusiness Model, Architecture, and Design documentation created in main\nrepository before feature development begins.\n\n**Now available as an interactive callable Python script** - saves ~2,000-2,700 tokens per feature compared to manual reproduction.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Current directory: main repository (not worktree)\n- Current branch: `contrib/<gh-user>`\n- Phase: Planning (Phase 1)\n\n## Interactive Callable Tool\n\nBMAD is now an **interactive callable tool** that runs as a Python script in the main repository.\n\n### Invocation\n\n**Command:**\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py \\\n  <slug> <gh_user>\n```\n\n**Arguments:**\n- `slug`: Feature slug (e.g., my-feature)\n- `gh_user`: GitHub username\n- `--no-commit`: Optional flag to skip git commit (for testing)\n\n**Example:**\n```bash\n# In main repo on contrib branch\npython .claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py \\\n  my-feature stharrold\n```\n\n### Interactive Session Flow\n\n**Session output:**\n```\nWorking in main repository...\nBranch: contrib/stharrold\n\n======================================================================\nBMAD Interactive Planning Tool\n======================================================================\n\nCreating planning documents for: my-feature\nGitHub user: stharrold\nOutput directory: planning/my-feature\n\n======================================================================\n🧠 BMAD Analyst Persona - Requirements Gathering\n======================================================================\n\nI''ll help create the requirements document through interactive Q&A.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhat problem does this feature solve?\n> Add German vocabulary search by part of speech\n\nWho are the primary users of this feature?\n> German language learners\n\n[... continues with 5-10 questions ...]\n\n✓ Requirements gathering complete!\n\n======================================================================\n🏗️ BMAD Architect Persona - Technical Architecture Design\n======================================================================\n\nBased on the requirements, I''ll design the technical architecture.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTechnology Stack:\n\nWeb framework (if applicable)?\n  1) FastAPI\n  2) Flask\n  3) Django\n  4) None\n  [default: None]\n> 4\n\n[... continues with 5-8 questions ...]\n\n✓ Architecture design complete!\n\n======================================================================\n📋 BMAD PM Persona - Epic Breakdown\n======================================================================\n\nAnalyzing requirements and architecture to create epic breakdown...\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n✓ Identified 3 epics:\n  - E-001: Data Layer Foundation (Priority: P0, Medium complexity)\n  - E-002: Core Business Logic (Priority: P0, High complexity)\n  - E-003: Testing & Quality Assurance (Priority: P1, Medium complexity)\n\n✓ Epic breakdown complete!\n\n======================================================================\nGenerating Planning Documents\n======================================================================\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/CLAUDE.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/README.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/ARCHIVED/CLAUDE.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/ARCHIVED/README.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/requirements.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/architecture.md\n  ✓ Created planning/my-feature/epics.md\n\nCommitting planning documents...\n✓ Committed planning documents for my-feature\n\n======================================================================\n✓ BMAD Planning Documents Created Successfully!\n======================================================================\n\nFiles created in planning/my-feature:\n  - requirements.md (Business requirements and acceptance criteria)\n  - architecture.md (Technical architecture and design)\n  - epics.md (Epic breakdown and planning)\n  - CLAUDE.md (Context for Claude Code)\n  - README.md (Human-readable overview)\n  - ARCHIVED/ (Directory for deprecated planning docs)\n\nNext steps:\n  1. Review planning documents in planning/my-feature\n  2. Create feature worktree\n  3. SpecKit will auto-detect and use these planning documents\n  4. Token savings: ~1,700-2,700 tokens by reusing planning context\n```\n\n**What happens:**\n1. Script validates location (main repo, contrib branch)\n2. Conducts 🧠 Analyst Q&A (5-10 questions)\n3. Generates requirements.md from template + Q&A responses\n4. Conducts 🏗️ Architect Q&A (5-8 questions)\n5. Generates architecture.md from template + Q&A responses\n6. Automatically analyzes requirements + architecture (📋 PM)\n7. Generates epics.md with epic breakdown\n8. Creates compliant planning/<slug>/ directory structure\n9. Commits changes to contrib branch\n\n**Token Efficiency:**\n\n| Approach | Token Usage | Savings |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Before (manual):** Claude Code reproduces BMAD each time | ~2,500 tokens | - |\n| **After (callable tool):** Claude Code calls script | ~200 tokens | ~2,300 tokens (92%) |\n\n### Script Architecture\n\n**Location:** `.claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py`\n\n**Key functions:**\n- `detect_context()` - Verify main repo, contrib branch\n- `interactive_qa_analyst()` - 🧠 Requirements Q&A\n- `interactive_qa_architect()` - 🏗️ Architecture Q&A\n- `generate_epic_breakdown()` - 📋 Auto-generate epics\n- `process_*_template()` - Replace placeholders, inject Q&A responses\n- `create_directory_structure()` - CLAUDE.md, README.md, ARCHIVED/\n- `commit_planning_docs()` - Git commit\n\n## Document Templates\n\nTemplates are located in `templates/`:\n- `requirements.md.template` - Business requirements and acceptance criteria (170 lines)\n- `architecture.md.template` - System architecture and design decisions (418 lines)\n- `epics.md.template` - Epic breakdown with priorities and dependencies (245 lines)\n\n## Interactive Planning Approach\n\nBMAD uses a three-persona method to gather comprehensive planning information through interactive Q&A sessions with the user.\n\n### 🧠 Persona 1: BMAD Analyst (Requirements)\n\n**Role:** Business Analyst creating Product Requirements Document\n\n**Process:**\n1. Ask user about problem statement and business context\n2. Identify target users and stakeholders\n3. Define success criteria and measurable outcomes\n4. Gather functional and non-functional requirements\n5. Document user stories with scenarios\n6. Identify risks and constraints\n\n**Interactive Q&A Example:**\n```\nI''ll help create the requirements document using the BMAD Analyst persona.\n\nWhat problem does this feature solve?\n> [User describes the problem]\n\nWho are the primary users of this feature?\n> [User identifies user types]\n\nHow will we measure success for this feature?\n> [User defines success metrics]\n\nWhat are the must-have capabilities? (functional requirements)\n> [User lists key capabilities]\n\nAny performance, security, or scalability requirements? (non-functional)\n> [User specifies NFRs]\n```\n\n**Generates:** `planning/<feature>/requirements.md` using comprehensive template\n\n### 🏗️ Persona 2: BMAD Architect (Architecture)\n\n**Role:** Technical Architect designing system architecture\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read requirements.md for business context\n2. Ask user about technology preferences and constraints\n3. Design system components and data models\n4. Define API contracts and integration points\n5. Specify security, error handling, testing strategies\n6. Document deployment and observability approach\n\n**Interactive Q&A Example:**\n```\nBased on the requirements, I''ll design the technical architecture.\n\nTechnology preferences?\n- Web framework: FastAPI / Flask / Django?\n> [User chooses framework]\n\nDatabase requirements?\n- Development: SQLite\n- Production: PostgreSQL / MySQL?\n> [User chooses database]\n\nPerformance targets?\n- Response time: < 200ms?\n- Concurrent users: How many?\n> [User specifies targets]\n\nContainer strategy?\n- Using Podman (default for this project)\n- Multi-container setup needed?\n> [User confirms approach]\n```\n\n**Generates:** `planning/<feature>/architecture.md` using comprehensive template\n\n### 📋 Persona 3: BMAD PM (Epic Breakdown)\n\n**Role:** Project Manager breaking down work into epics\n\n**Process:**\n1. Read requirements.md + architecture.md for full context\n2. Identify major work streams (epics)\n3. Define scope, complexity, and dependencies for each epic\n4. Prioritize epics (P0/P1/P2)\n5. Create implementation timeline\n6. Estimate effort and identify risks\n\n**Analysis:**\n```\nAnalyzing requirements and architecture to create epic breakdown...\n\nIdentified 3 major epics:\n1. E-001: Data Layer (Foundation) - P0, High complexity\n2. E-002: API Layer (Core functionality) - P0, Medium complexity\n3. E-003: Testing & Quality - P1, Medium complexity\n\nDependencies detected:\n  E-001 → E-002 (API needs data layer)\n  E-002 → E-003 (tests need API)\n\nCreating epic breakdown document...\n```\n\n**Generates:** `planning/<feature>/epics.md` with epic definitions, priorities, timeline\n\n## How to Invoke BMAD\n\nWhen workflow-orchestrator loads bmad-planner during Phase 1, it calls the create_planning.py script.\n\n**Workflow Orchestrator Code:**\n```python\n# In workflow orchestrator - Phase 1.1\nif current_phase == 1 and current_step == ''1.1'':\n    import subprocess\n\n    result = subprocess.run([\n        ''python'',\n        ''.claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py'',\n        slug,       # my-feature\n        gh_user,    # stharrold\n    ], check=True)\n\n    # Script handles:\n    # - 🧠 Analyst Q&A with user\n    # - 🏗️ Architect Q&A with user\n    # - 📋 PM epic breakdown (automatic)\n    # - requirements.md, architecture.md, epics.md generation\n    # - Directory structure creation\n    # - Git commit\n\n    print(f\"✓ BMAD planning created in planning/{slug}/\")\n    print(\"  Next: Create feature worktree (Phase 2)\")\n```\n\n**User Experience:**\n```\nPhase 1: BMAD Planning Session\n\nWorkflow calls:\n  python .claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py my-feature stharrold\n\nScript conducts interactive session:\n  🧠 BMAD Analyst: Requirements gathering [5-10 questions]\n  🏗️ BMAD Architect: Architecture design [5-8 questions]\n  📋 BMAD PM: Epic breakdown [automatic analysis]\n\n✓ Generated: planning/my-feature/requirements.md\n✓ Generated: planning/my-feature/architecture.md\n✓ Generated: planning/my-feature/epics.md\n✓ Committed to contrib branch\n\n✓ BMAD planning complete!\n  Next: Create feature worktree (Phase 2 will use these docs)\n  Token savings: ~2,300 tokens vs manual approach\n```\n\n## Integration with Workflow\n\nThe workflow-orchestrator calls the create_planning.py script during Phase 1:\n\n```python\n# In workflow orchestrator\nif current_phase == 1 and current_step == ''1.1'':\n    import subprocess\n\n    result = subprocess.run([\n        ''python'',\n        ''.claude/skills/bmad-planner/scripts/create_planning.py'',\n        slug,\n        gh_user,\n    ], check=True)\n\n    print(f\"✓ BMAD planning created: planning/{slug}/\")\n```\n\n## Output Files\n\nBMAD generates three planning documents that become input context for SpecKit:\n\n```\nplanning/<feature-name>/\n├── requirements.md    # Business requirements (170 lines from template)\n│   ├─ Problem statement, stakeholders\n│   ├─ Functional requirements (FR-001, FR-002...)\n│   ├─ Non-functional requirements (performance, security...)\n│   ├─ User stories with scenarios\n│   └─ Risks, assumptions, success criteria\n│\n├── architecture.md    # Technical architecture (418 lines from template)\n│   ├─ System overview, components\n│   ├─ Technology stack with justifications\n│   ├─ Data models, API endpoints\n│   ├─ Container architecture (Containerfile, podman-compose.yml)\n│   ├─ Security, error handling, testing strategies\n│   └─ Deployment, observability, disaster recovery\n│\n├── epics.md          # Epic breakdown (245 lines from template)\n│   ├─ Epic definitions (scope, complexity, priority)\n│   ├─ Dependencies and critical path\n│   ├─ Implementation timeline\n│   └─ Resource requirements and risks\n│\n├── CLAUDE.md         # Context for this planning directory\n├── README.md         # Human-readable overview\n└── ARCHIVED/         # Deprecated planning documents\n```\n\n**These files become input context for SpecKit in Phase 2.**\n\n## Integration with SpecKit\n\nBMAD documents are used as context when creating SpecKit specifications:\n\n### Data Flow: BMAD → SpecKit\n\n**Phase 1 (Main Repo, contrib branch):**\n```\nBMAD Interactive Session\n  ↓\nplanning/<feature>/\n├── requirements.md\n├── architecture.md\n└── epics.md\n```\n\n**Create Worktree:**\n```bash\n# Worktree creation preserves link to main repo\ngit worktree add ../repo_feature_<slug> feature/<timestamp>_<slug>\n```\n\n**Phase 2 (Worktree):**\n```\nSpecKit reads from main repo:\n../planning/<feature>/requirements.md → Business context\n../planning/<feature>/architecture.md → Technical design\n../planning/<feature>/epics.md        → Epic priorities\n\nSpecKit generates (informed by BMAD):\nspecs/<feature>/spec.md  ← Detailed specification\nspecs/<feature>/plan.md  ← Implementation tasks\n```\n\n### Why This Connection Matters\n\n**Consistency:**\n- Technology choices in spec.md match architecture.md stack\n- spec.md acceptance criteria cover requirements.md success criteria\n- plan.md tasks align with epics.md breakdown\n\n**Completeness:**\n- All functional requirements from requirements.md appear in spec.md\n- Non-functional requirements (performance, security) included\n- Epic dependencies reflected in plan.md task ordering\n\n**Traceability:**\n- spec.md sections reference FR-001, FR-002... from requirements.md\n- plan.md tasks map to E-001, E-002... from epics.md\n- Architecture decisions from architecture.md justify implementation choices\n\n**Less Rework:**\n- Planning clarifies requirements before coding\n- Design decisions made explicit\n- Reduces ambiguity and prevents scope creep\n\n## Integration with Workflow\n\nThe workflow-orchestrator calls this skill during Phase 1:\n\n```python\n# In workflow orchestrator\nif current_phase == 1 and current_step == ''1.1'':\n    load_skill(''bmad-planner'')\n    create_planning_docs(feature_name, gh_user)\n    commit_changes(''docs: add BMAD planning for '' + feature_name)\n```\n\n## Template Placeholders\n\nBoth templates use these placeholders:\n- `{{TITLE}}` - Feature name (title case)\n- `{{DATE}}` - Creation date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- `{{GH_USER}}` - GitHub username\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Requirements first**: Define business needs before technical design\n- **Acceptance criteria**: Make success measurable\n- **Architecture clarity**: Explain design decisions and trade-offs\n- **Technology justification**: Document why specific tools/frameworks chosen\n- **Non-functional requirements**: Don''t forget performance, security, scalability\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:44:34.509Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing automated Business Model, Architecture, and Design planning capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化业务模型、架构和设计规划能力的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが自動化されたビジネスモデル、アーキテクチャ、および設計計画の機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 비즈니스 모델, 아키텍처, 디자인 계획 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan capacidades de planificación automatizada de Modelo de Negocio, Arquitectura y Diseño.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de capacités de planification automatisée de modèle commercial, d''architecture et de conception.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die automatisierte Geschäftsmodell-, Architektur- und Designplanungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de capacidades de planejamento automatizadas de Modelo de Negócios, Arquitetura e Design.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы автоматические возможности планирования бизнес-модели, архитектуры и дизайна.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات التخطيط الآلي لطراز العمل والهيكلة والتصميم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive documentation using interactive callable Python scripts, saving ~2,000-2,700 tokens per feature and supporting Phase 1 planning with features like web searches.","zh":"赋予代理创建使用交互式可调用Python脚本的综合文档的能力，每个功能可节省~2,000-2,700个令牌，并支持Phase 1规划，具有web搜索等功能。","ja":"エージェントがインタラクティブなcallable Pythonスクリプトを使用して包括的なドキュメントを作成できるようにし、各機能で~2,000-2,700トークンを節約し、Phase 1の計画をサポートし、Web検索などの機能を備えています。","ko":"에이전트가 상호 작용 가능한 callable Python 스크립트를 사용하여 포괄적인 문서를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 각 기능당 ~2,000-2,700토큰을 절약하고, Phase 1 계획을 지원하며, 웹 검색 등의 기능을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear documentación integral utilizando scripts de Python interactivos llamables, ahorrando ~2,000-2,700 tokens por función y admitiendo la planificación de la Fase 1 con características como búsquedas web.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer une documentation complète à l''aide de scripts Python interactifs appelables, économisant ~2,000-2,700 jetons par fonction et prenant en charge la planification de la Phase 1 avec des fonctionnalités telles que les recherches web.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende Dokumentationen mithilfe interaktiver aufrufbarer Python-Skripte zu erstellen, wodurch ~2,000-2,700 Token pro Funktion eingespart werden und die Planung der Phase 1 mit Funktionen wie Websuchen unterstützt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar documentação abrangente usando scripts Python interativos chamáveis, economizando ~2.000-2.700 tokens por recurso e apoiando o planejamento da Fase 1 com recursos como pesquisas na web.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать комплексную документацию с помощью интерактивных вызываемых скриптов Python, экономя ~2 000-2 700 токенов на функцию и поддерживая планирование Фазы 1 с функциями, такими как веб-поиск.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء توثيق شامِل باستخدام سكريبتات Python التفاعلية القابلة للاتصال، وتوفير ~2،000-2،700 رمز لكل ميزة ودعم التخطيط للفаза 1 بميزات مثل عمليات البحث على الويب."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating BMAD documentation creation","Generating feature development plans","Conducting web searches for feature research"],"zh":["自动化BMAD文档创建","生成功能开发计划","进行功能研究的web搜索"],"ja":["BMADドキュメントの自動化","機能開発計画の生成","機能の調査のためのWeb検索"],"ko":["BMAD 문서 자동 생성","기능 개발 계획 생성","기능 연구를 위한 웹 검색"],"es":["Creación automática de documentación de BMAD","Generación de planes de desarrollo de funciones","Realización de búsquedas web para investigaciones de funciones"],"fr":["Création automatique de documentation BMAD","Génération de plans de développement de fonctions","Réalisations de recherches web pour la recherche de fonctions"],"de":["Automatisierte Erstellung von BMAD-Dokumentation","Generierung von Funktionsentwicklungsplänen","Durchführung von Websuchen für Funktionsrecherchen"],"pt":["Criação automatizada de documentação BMAD","Geração de planos de desenvolvimento de recursos","Realização de pesquisas na web para pesquisa de recursos"],"ru":["Автоматизированная создание документации BMAD","Генерация планов разработки функций","Проведение веб-поисков для исследования функций"],"ar":["إنشاء توثيق آلي لبرنامج BMAD","توليد خطط لتطوير الميزات","إجراء عمليات بحث على الويب لأبحاث الميزات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires main repository access","Limited to contrib/<gh-user> branch","Python script compatibility required"],"zh":["需要主存储库访问权限","仅限于contrib/<gh-user>分支","需要Python脚本兼容性"],"ja":["メインリポジトリへのアクセスが必要","contrib/<gh-user>ブランチに限定される","Pythonスクリプトの互換性が必要"],"ko":["메인 저장소 접근 권한 필요","contrib/<gh-user> 브랜치로 제한","Python 스크립트 호환성 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio principal","Limitado a la rama contrib/<gh-user>","Se requiere compatibilidad de script de Python"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel principal","Limité à la branche contrib/<gh-user>","La compatibilité du script Python est requise"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf das Hauptrepository","Begrenzt auf den contrib/<gh-user>-Zweig","Python-Skript-Kompatibilität ist erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório principal","Limitado à branch contrib/<gh-user>","Compatibilidade com script Python requerida"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к основному репозиторию","Ограничен для ветки contrib/<gh-user>","Требуется совместимость со скриптом Python"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى المستودع الرئيسي","محدود للفرع contrib/<gh-user>","متطلبات متوافقة مع سكريبت Python"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"a5ffb1f00ca6c2cdb8fbc3b2d0afd8dfd6901fcd8cec5787c2ba715d23c1f168","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('synaptiai/agent-capability-standard/detect', 'community', 'synaptiai', 'agent-capability-standard', 'synaptiai/agent-capability-standard', 'detect', 0, 0, 60, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.974Z', '2026-03-02T02:55:00.282Z', '79e9ee741307f32b7dd612e5babc2e830ced1c3b0da9e20153729fb60944f3f9', '{"id":"synaptiai/agent-capability-standard/detect","name":"detect","description":{"zh":"Agent Capability Standard是一个开源的AI智能代理能力规范，定义了36个原子能力和9个认知层","ja":"Agent Capability Standardは、AIエージェントの能力を定義するためのオープンな仕様です","ko":"에이전트 能力 표준은 AI 에이전트의 능력을 정의하는 오픈 소스仕様입니다","es":"Detect es un agente de IA que sigue el estándar de capacidades componibles para agentes de IA, con 36 capacidades atómicas y resolución de conflictos de confianza","fr":"Detect est un outil d''IA qui suit la norme de capacités standardisées pour les agents d''IA, avec 36 capacités atomiques et une résolution de conflits de confiance","de":"Detect ist ein KI-Agent, der den Standard für komponierbare Fähigkeiten von KI-Agents folgt, mit 36 atomaren Fähigkeiten und vertrauensbasierter Konfliktlösung","pt":"A habilidade de detecção é uma capacidade fundamental dos agentes de IA, permitindo que eles detectem e respondam a eventos e mudanças no ambiente","ru":"Возможность обнаружения является фундаментальной способностью ИИ агентов, позволяющей им обнаруживать и реагировать на события и изменения в окружающей среде","ar":"مهارة الكشف هي قدرة أساسية لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح لهم بالكشف والاستجابة للأحداث والتغييرات في البيئة","en":"Agent Capability Standard is an open specification for composable AI agent capabilities. It defines 36 atomic capabilities across 9 cognitive layers, a type-safe workflow DSL, and grounded world modeling with trust-aware conflict resolution. Built on the Grounded Agency philosophy, it makes agent..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理检测","ja":"AIエージェントの検出","ko":"AI 에이전트 감지","es":"Detect: Agente de IA para capacidades estándar","fr":"Detect: Outil d''IA pour capacités standardisées","de":"Detect: KI-Agent für Standardfähigkeiten","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Detect - Agentes de IA Avançados","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Detect - Расширенные Возможности","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Detect - وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي ا...","en":"detect"},"description":{"zh":"Agent Capability Standard是一个开源的AI智能代理能力规范，定义了36个原子能力和9个认知层","ja":"Agent Capability Standardは、AIエージェントの能力を定義するためのオープンな仕様です","ko":"에이전트 能力 표준은 AI 에이전트의 능력을 정의하는 오픈 소스仕様입니다","es":"Detect es un agente de IA que sigue el estándar de capacidades componibles para agentes de IA, con 36 capacidades atómicas y resolución de conflictos de conf...","fr":"Detect est un outil d''IA qui suit la norme de capacités standardisées pour les agents d''IA, avec 36 capacités atomiques et une résolution de conflits de conf...","de":"Detect ist ein KI-Agent, der den Standard für komponierbare Fähigkeiten von KI-Agents folgt, mit 36 atomaren Fähigkeiten und vertrauensbasierter Konfliktlösung","pt":"A habilidade de detecção é uma capacidade fundamental dos agentes de IA, permitindo que eles detectem e respondam a eventos e mudanças no ambiente","ru":"Возможность обнаружения является фундаментальной способностью ИИ агентов, позволяющей им обнаруживать и реагировать на события и изменения в окружающей среде","ar":"مهارة الكشف هي قدرة أساسية لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح لهم بالكشف والاستجابة للأحداث والتغييرات في البيئة","en":"Agent Capability Standard is an open specification for composable AI agent capabilities. It defines 36 atomic capabilities across 9 cognitive layers, a type-..."},"definition":{"en":"Agent Capability Standard is an open specification for composable AI agent capabilities. It defines 36 atomic capabilities across 9 cognitive layers, a type-safe workflow DSL, and grounded world modeling with trust-aware conflict resolution. Built on the Grounded Agency philosophy, it makes agent reliability structural—not optional."},"features":{"zh":["36个原子能力","9个认知层","类型安全的工作流DSL","基于Grounded Agency哲学"],"ja":["36個の原子能力","9個の認知層","タイプセーフのワークフローDSL","Grounded Agency哲学に基づく"],"ko":["36개의 원자 능력","9개의 인지 계층","타입 안전 워크플로 DSL","그라운드 에이전시 철학을 기반으로"],"es":["36 capacidades atómicas","Resolución de conflictos de confianza","Filosofía de agencia basada en la realidad","Modelado de mundo basado en la realidad","Lenguaje de flujo de trabajo de tipo seguro"],"fr":["36 capacités atomiques","Résolution de conflits de confiance","Philosophie d''agent basée sur la réalité","Modélisation de monde basée sur la réalité","Langage de flux de travail de type sécurisé"],"de":["36 atomare Fähigkeiten","Vertrauensbasierte Konfliktlösung","Philosophie der Agenten basierend auf der Realität","Realitätsbasiertes Weltmodell","Sicheres Arbeitsablauf-DSL"],"pt":["Detecção de eventos e mudanças no ambiente","Resposta automatizada a eventos e mudanças","Integração com sistemas de IA avançados","Melhoria da confiabilidade e eficiência dos sistemas de IA","Suporte a múltiplos ambientes e plataformas"],"ru":["Обнаружение событий и изменений в окружающей среде","Автоматическая реакция на события и изменения","Интеграция с расширенными системами ИИ","Повышение надежности и эффективности систем ИИ","Поддержка нескольких окружающих сред и платформ"],"ar":["الكشف عن الأحداث والتغييرات في البيئة","الاستجابة الآلية للأحداث والتغييرات","التكامل مع أنظمة الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة","تحسين موثوقية وكفاءة أنظمة الذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم بيئات و منصات متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Agent Capability Standard","如何使用AI智能代理","AI智能代理的优势","AI智能代理检测工具","AI智能代理安装指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Agent Capability Standard","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントのメリット","AIエージェント検出ツール","AIエージェントのセットアップガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","에이전트 能力 표준","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트의 장점","AI 에이전트 감지 도구","AI 에이전트 설치 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar detect","qué es un agente de IA","detect vs otros agentes de IA","guía de instalación de detect","configuración de detect","agentes de IA para desarrollo","herramientas de IA para programadores","detect para resolución de conflictos"],"fr":["comment utiliser detect","qu''est-ce qu''un outil d''IA","detect vs autres outils d''IA","guide d''installation de detect","configuration de detect","outils d''IA pour développement","outils d''IA pour les programmeurs","detect pour la résolution de conflits"],"de":["wie man detect verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","detect vs andere KI-Agents","installationsanleitung für detect","konfiguration von detect","KI-Tools für Entwicklung","KI-Tools für Entwickler","detect für Konfliktlösung"],"pt":["como usar agentes de IA","o que é detecção de agentes de IA","agentes de IA avançados","ferramentas de IA para detecção","instalação de agentes de IA","guia de configuração de agentes de IA","alternativas para agentes de IA","comparação de agentes de IA"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ агенты","что такое обнаружение ИИ агентов","расширенные ИИ агенты","инструменты ИИ для обнаружения","установка ИИ агентов","руководство по настройке ИИ агентов","альтернативы ИИ агентам","сравнение ИИ агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي مهارة الكشف عن وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للكشف","تثبيت وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","دليل إعداد وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","مقارنة لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"synaptiai","repo":"agent-capability-standard","repoPath":"synaptiai/agent-capability-standard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.974Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"detect","description":"Determine whether a specific pattern, entity, or condition exists in the given data. Use when searching for patterns, checking existence, validating presence, or finding signals.","bodyPreview":"## Intent\n\nScan data sources to determine whether a specified pattern, entity, or condition is present. Detection is binary (present/absent) with associated signal strength.\n\n**Success criteria:**\n- Clear boolean determination of presence/absence\n- At least one evidence anchor for positive detections\n- False positive risk assessment provided\n- Confidence score justified by evidence quality\n\n**Compatible schemas:**\n- `schemas/output_schema.yaml`\n\n## Inputs\n\n| Parameter | Required | Type | Descrip","body":"## Intent\n\nScan data sources to determine whether a specified pattern, entity, or condition is present. Detection is binary (present/absent) with associated signal strength.\n\n**Success criteria:**\n- Clear boolean determination of presence/absence\n- At least one evidence anchor for positive detections\n- False positive risk assessment provided\n- Confidence score justified by evidence quality\n\n**Compatible schemas:**\n- `schemas/output_schema.yaml`\n\n## Inputs\n\n| Parameter | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `target` | Yes | string\\|object | The data source to scan (file path, URL, or structured data) |\n| `pattern` | Yes | string\\|regex | The pattern, entity type, or condition to detect |\n| `threshold` | No | object | Detection sensitivity settings (e.g., min_matches, confidence_floor) |\n| `scope` | No | string | Limit search to specific regions (e.g., \"functions\", \"imports\", \"comments\") |\n\n## Procedure\n\n1) **Define detection criteria**: Clarify exactly what constitutes a positive detection\n   - Convert vague patterns to concrete search terms or regex\n   - Establish minimum evidence threshold for positive detection\n\n2) **Scan target systematically**: Search the target data for matching signals\n   - Use Grep for text patterns with appropriate flags (-i for case-insensitive, etc.)\n   - Use Read for structural inspection when pattern requires context\n   - Record location (file:line) for each potential match\n\n3) **Evaluate signal strength**: For each match, assess how strongly it indicates true presence\n   - Strong: exact match with clear context\n   - Medium: partial match or ambiguous context\n   - Weak: possible match requiring human verification\n\n4) **Assess false positive risk**: Determine likelihood that detections are spurious\n   - High risk: generic patterns, noisy data, few matches\n   - Low risk: specific patterns, clean data, multiple corroborating signals\n\n5) **Ground claims**: Attach evidence anchors to all detection signals\n   - Format: `file:line` for file-based targets\n   - Include snippet of matched content for verification\n\n6) **Format output**: Structure results according to the output contract below\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn a structured object:\n\n```yaml\ndetected: boolean  # True if pattern/entity was found\ntarget_type: string  # What was being detected (e.g., \"security vulnerability\", \"deprecated API\")\nsignals:\n  - signal: string  # Description of what was found\n    strength: low | medium | high  # Signal strength\n    location: string  # file:line or path where found\nfalse_positive_risk: low | medium | high  # Likelihood of spurious detection\nconfidence: number  # 0.0-1.0 based on evidence quality\nevidence_anchors: array[string]  # File:line references\nassumptions: array[string]  # Explicit assumptions made\nnext_actions: array[string]  # 0-3 suggested follow-ups if uncertain\n```\n\n### Field Definitions\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `detected` | boolean | True if the target pattern/entity was found |\n| `target_type` | string | Category of what was searched for |\n| `signals` | array | List of individual detection signals with strength |\n| `false_positive_risk` | enum | Assessment of detection reliability |\n| `confidence` | number | 0.0-1.0 based on evidence completeness |\n| `evidence_anchors` | array[string] | File:line references or tool outputs |\n| `assumptions` | array[string] | Explicitly stated assumptions |\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Detect SQL Injection Vulnerability\n\n**Input:**\n```yaml\ntarget: src/api/user_controller.py\npattern: \"SQL injection pattern\"\nthreshold:\n  min_matches: 1\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```yaml\ndetected: true\ntarget_type: \"SQL injection vulnerability\"\nsignals:\n  - signal: \"String concatenation in SQL query with user input\"\n    strength: high\n    location: \"src/api/user_controller.py:47\"\n  - signal: \"Raw SQL execution without parameterization\"\n    strength: medium\n    location: \"src/api/user_controller.py:52\"\nfalse_positive_risk: low\nconfidence: 0.85\nevidence_anchors:\n  - \"src/api/user_controller.py:47\"\n  - \"src/api/user_controller.py:52\"\nassumptions:\n  - \"User input flows from request.params to query variable\"\n  - \"No input sanitization in calling function\"\nnext_actions:\n  - \"Verify data flow from user input to SQL query\"\n  - \"Check for parameterized query alternatives in codebase\"\n```\n\n**Evidence pattern:** Grep for SQL keywords combined with string formatting patterns, then Read to verify context.\n\n---\n\n### Example 2: Detect Deprecated API Usage\n\n**Input:**\n```yaml\ntarget: src/\npattern: \"componentWillMount|componentWillReceiveProps\"\nscope: \"*.jsx,*.tsx\"\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```yaml\ndetected: true\ntarget_type: \"deprecated React lifecycle method\"\nsignals:\n  - signal: \"componentWillMount usage\"\n    strength: high\n    location: \"src/components/Dashboard.jsx:23\"\nfalse_positive_risk: low\nconfidence: 0.95\nevidence_anchors:\n  - \"src/components/Dashboard.jsx:23\"\nassumptions:\n  - \"Project uses React 16.3+ where these methods are deprecated\"\nnext_actions:\n  - \"Migrate to componentDidMount or useEffect hook\"\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- [ ] Output contains `detected` boolean matching signal presence\n- [ ] At least one evidence anchor exists for positive detections\n- [ ] Confidence score correlates with number and strength of signals\n- [ ] All referenced file:line locations are valid and accessible\n- [ ] False positive risk assessment is justified\n\n**Verification tools:** Read (to verify file:line references exist)\n\n## Safety Constraints\n\n- `mutation`: false\n- `requires_checkpoint`: false\n- `requires_approval`: false\n- `risk`: low\n\n**Capability-specific rules:**\n- Do not access paths outside the specified target scope\n- Do not modify any files during detection\n- Stop and request clarification if detection criteria are ambiguous\n- Report uncertainty rather than guessing when signals are weak\n\n## Composition Patterns\n\n**Commonly follows:**\n- `inspect` - Detection often follows initial observation of a system\n- `search` - Detection may refine broad search results\n\n**Commonly precedes:**\n- `identify` - Positive detection often leads to classification of what was found\n- `estimate-risk` - Detection of anomalies feeds into risk assessment\n- `plan` - Detected issues may trigger remediation planning\n\n**Anti-patterns:**\n- Never use detect for complex entity classification (use `identify` instead)\n- Avoid detect for quantitative assessment (use `estimate` instead)\n\n**Workflow references:**\n- See `reference/composition_patterns.md#risk-assessment` for detection in risk workflows\n- See `reference/composition_patterns.md#observe-model-act` for detection in agentic loops\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:55:00.282Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Analysis Agents needing precise pattern detection capabilities with binary presence/absence determination and associated signal strength","zh":"适合需要精确模式检测能力的高级分析代理，具有二元存在/不存在确定性和相关信号强度","ja":"高度な分析エージェントが正確なパターン検出機能を必要とする場合に適しています。二元の存在/不存在の決定と関連する信号強度を備えています","ko":"정확한 패턴 감지 기능과 이진 존재/존재하지 않음 결정 및 관련信号 강도가 필요한 고급 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis Avanzados que necesitan capacidades de detección de patrones precisas con determinación de presencia/ausencia binaria y fuerza de señal de respuesta asociada","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse avancée nécessitant des capacités de détection de modèles précises avec détermination de présence/absence binaire et force de signal associée","de":"Ideal für erweiterte Analyseagenten, die präzise Mustererkennungsfähigkeiten mit binärer Anwesenheits-/Abwesenheitsbestimmung und zugehöriger Signalstärke benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise Avançada que necessitam de capacidades de detecção de padrões precisas com determinação de presença/ausência binária e força de sinal associada","ru":"Идеально для Продвинутых Аналитических Агентов, которым необходимы точные возможности обнаружения закономерностей с бинарным определением присутствия/отсутствия и связанной силой сигнала","ar":"مثالي لوكيلات التحليل المتقدم الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات كشف الأنماط الدقيقة مع تحديد الحضور/الغياب الثنائي والقوة الإشارة المرتبطة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to scan data sources for specified patterns or entities, providing clear boolean determinations, evidence anchors, and confidence scores justified by evidence quality, all while assessing false positive risk through trust-aware conflict resolution and grounded world modeling","zh":"赋予代理扫描数据源以查找指定模式或实体的能力，提供明确的布尔值判断、证据锚点和证据质量证明的信心评分，同时通过信任感知冲突解决和基于世界模型评估假阳性风险","ja":"エージェントにデータソースをスキャンして指定されたパターンまたはエンティティを検出する機能を付与し、明確なブール値の判断、証拠アンカー、証拠品質によって裏付けられた信頼スコアを提供し、信頼感覚のあるコンフリクト解決とグラウンデッドワールドモデリングを通じて偽陽性リスクを評価する","ko":"에이전트에게 데이터 소스를 스캔하여 지정된 패턴 또는 엔티티를 검색할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 명확한 불리언 판단, 증거 앵커 및 증거 품질에 의한 신뢰 점수를 제공하고, 신뢰 감지_conflict 해결 및 기반_세계 모델링을 통해 가짜 양성 위험을 평가한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes para escanear fuentes de datos en busca de patrones o entidades especificados, proporcionando determinaciones booleanas claras, anclajes de evidencia y puntuaciones de confianza justificadas por la calidad de la evidencia, todo mientras se evalúa el riesgo de falsos positivos a través de la resolución de conflictos consciente de la confianza y la modelización del mundo basada en hechos","fr":"Permet aux agents de scanner les sources de données pour les modèles ou les entités spécifiés, fournissant des déterminations booléennes claires, des ancrages d''évidence et des scores de confiance justifiés par la qualité de l''évidence, le tout en évaluant le risque de faux positifs grâce à la résolution de conflits consciente de la confiance et à la modélisation du monde basée sur les faits","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Datenquellen nach bestimmten Mustern oder Entitäten zu scannen, wodurch klare boolesche Bestimmungen, Beweisanker und Vertrauenswerte bereitgestellt werden, die durch die Qualität der Beweise gerechtfertigt sind, während das Risiko von Falschpositiven durch vertrauensbewusste Konfliktlösung und faktengestützte Weltmodellierung bewertet wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escanear fontes de dados para padrões ou entidades especificadas, fornecendo determinações booleanas claras, âncoras de evidência e pontuações de confiança justificadas pela qualidade da evidência, avaliando ao mesmo tempo o risco de falsos positivos por meio da resolução de conflitos consciente da confiança e modelagem de mundo baseada","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью сканировать источники данных для заданных закономерностей или сущностей, предоставляя четкие булевы определения, якоря доказательств и показатели уверенности, обоснованные качеством доказательств, и в то же время оценивая риск ложных срабатываний через доверчивое разрешение конфликтов и моделирование реального мира","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من فحص مصادر البيانات لاكتشاف الأنماط أو الكيانات المحددة، وتقديم تحديدات منطقية واضحة ومسامير الأدلة ودرجات الثقة المبررة بجودة الدليل، مع تقييم خطر الإيجابيات الكاذبة من خلال حل النزاعات المتأصل في الثقة والتنميط العالمي المبني على الأساس"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating entity detection in large datasets","Generating alerts based on pattern presence with confidence scores","Debugging false positives through risk assessment and evidence analysis"],"zh":["在大型数据集中自动执行实体检测","基于模式存在生成警报，并提供信心评分","通过风险评估和证据分析调试假阳性"],"ja":["大規模データセットでのエンティティ検出の自動化","パターンの存在に基づいてアラートを生成し、信頼スコアを提供する","リスク評価と証拠分析を通じて偽陽性をデバッグする"],"ko":["대규모 데이터セット에서 엔티티 감지를 자동화","패턴 존재에 따라 경고를 생성하고 신뢰 점수를 제공","위험 평가 및 증거 분석을 통해 가짜 양성을 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la detección de entidades en grandes conjuntos de datos","Generación de alertas basadas en la presencia de patrones con puntuaciones de confianza","Depuración de falsos positivos a través de la evaluación de riesgos y el análisis de evidencia"],"fr":["Automatisation de la détection d''entités dans de grands ensembles de données","Génération d''alertes basées sur la présence de modèles avec des scores de confiance","Débogage de faux positifs via l''évaluation des risques et l''analyse d''évidence"],"de":["Automatisierung der Entitätenerkennung in großen Datenmengen","Erzeugung von Alarmen basierend auf der Anwesenheit von Mustern mit Vertrauenswerten","Fehlersuche von Falschpositiven durch Risikobewertung und Beweisanalyse"],"pt":["Automatizar a detecção de entidades em grandes conjuntos de dados","Gerar alertas com base na presença de padrões com pontuações de confiança","Depurar falsos positivos por meio da avaliação de risco e análise de evidências"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обнаружение сущностей в больших наборах данных","Генерировать оповещения на основе наличия закономерностей с показателями уверенности","Отладить ложные срабатывания посредством оценки риска и анализа доказательств"],"ar":["أتمتة كشف الكيانات في مجموعات البيانات الكبيرة","توليد تنبيهات بناءً على وجود الأنماط مع درجات الثقة","تصحيح الأيجابيات الكاذبة من خلال تقييم المخاطر وتحليل الأدلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive content analysis","Binary detection only (present/absent)","Dependent on quality of evidence for confidence score justification"],"zh":["需要全面内容分析","仅二元检测（存在/不存在）","依赖于证据质量来证明信心评分"],"ja":["包括的コンテンツ分析が必要","二元検出のみ（存在/不存在）","証拠の品質に依存して信頼スコアを裏付け"],"ko":["포괄적인 콘텐츠 분석이 필요","이진 감지のみ（존재/존재하지 않음）","증거의 품질에 의존하여 신뢰 점수를 입증"],"es":["Requiere un análisis de contenido integral","Detección binaria solo (presente/ausente)","Dependiente de la calidad de la evidencia para la justificación de la puntuación de confianza"],"fr":["Nécessite une analyse de contenu complète","Détection binaire uniquement (présent/absent)","Dépendante de la qualité de l''évidence pour la justification du score de confiance"],"de":["Erfordert eine umfassende Inhaltsanalyse","Binäre Erkennung nur (vorhanden/nicht vorhanden)","Abhängig von der Qualität der Beweise für die Rechtfertigung des Vertrauenswerts"],"pt":["Exige análise abrangente de conteúdo","Deteção binária apenas (presente/ausente)","Dependente da qualidade da evidência para justificar a pontuação de confiança"],"ru":["Требует всестороннего анализа содержания","Бинарное обнаружение только (присутствует/отсутствует)","Зависит от качества доказательств для обоснования показателя уверенности"],"ar":["يتطلب تحليلًا شاملاً للمحتوى","كشف ثنائي فقط (حاضر/غائب)","يعتمد على جودة الدليل لتبرير درجة الثقة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"79e9ee741307f32b7dd612e5babc2e830ced1c3b0da9e20153729fb60944f3f9","qualityScore":60}');
