pyard-testing","guía de configuración de shipyard-testing"],"fr":["comment utiliser shipyard-testing","quoi est shipyard-testing","outils d''IA pour les projets","alternatives à shipyard-testing","shipyard-testing vs d''autres outils","installation de shipyard-testing","guide de configuration de shipyard-testing"],"de":["wie man shipyard-testing verwendet","was ist shipyard-testing","KI-Tools für Projekte","Alternativen zu shipyard-testing","shipyard-testing vs andere Tools","Installation von shipyard-testing","Konfigurationsanleitung für shipyard-testing"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","teste de estaleiro","ciclo de vida de projetos","disciplina e qualidade","agentes paralelos","como usar teste de estaleiro","teste de estaleiro vs outros plugins"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","верфь-тестирование","жизненный цикл проектов","дисциплина и качество","параллельные агенты","как использовать верфь-тестирование","верфь-тестирование vs другие плагины"],"ar":["أدوات ذكية","اختبار الساحة البحرية","دورة حياة المشاريع","الانضباط والجودة","عملاء موازيين","كيفية استخدام اختبار الساحة البحرية","اختبار الساحة البحرية مقابل مكونات إضافية أخرى"]}},"owner":"lgbarn","repo":"shipyard","repoPath":"lgbarn/shipyard","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.975Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"shipyard-testing","description":"Use when writing tests, structuring test suites, choosing test boundaries, or debugging test quality issues like flakiness, over-mocking, or brittle tests","bodyPreview":"<!-- TOKEN BUDGET: 400 lines / ~1200 tokens -->\n\n# Writing Effective Tests\n\n<activation>\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n\n- Writing or modifying test files (`*.test.*`, `*.spec.*`, `*_test.go`, `test_*.py`)\n- Setting up test infrastructure or test utilities\n- Debugging flaky, brittle, or slow tests\n- Deciding between unit, integration, and E2E tests\n- Choosing when and how to use mocks, stubs, or fakes\n\n## Natural Language Triggers\n- \"add tests\", \"test coverage\", \"testing strategy\", \"write tests f","body":"<!-- TOKEN BUDGET: 400 lines / ~1200 tokens -->\n\n# Writing Effective Tests\n\n<activation>\n\n## When This Skill Activates\n\n- Writing or modifying test files (`*.test.*`, `*.spec.*`, `*_test.go`, `test_*.py`)\n- Setting up test infrastructure or test utilities\n- Debugging flaky, brittle, or slow tests\n- Deciding between unit, integration, and E2E tests\n- Choosing when and how to use mocks, stubs, or fakes\n\n## Natural Language Triggers\n- \"add tests\", \"test coverage\", \"testing strategy\", \"write tests for\", \"how should I test\"\n\n</activation>\n\n## Overview\n\nTest behaviors through public APIs. Verify state, not interactions.\n\n**Core principle:** If refactoring breaks your tests but not your users, your tests are wrong.\n\n**Relationship to TDD:** The `shipyard:shipyard-tdd` skill covers WHEN to write tests (test-first, red-green-refactor). This skill covers HOW to write tests that are effective, maintainable, and trustworthy.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nTEST BEHAVIORS, NOT IMPLEMENTATIONS\n```\n\nA test should break only when the system''s observable behavior changes -- never because of refactoring, renaming internals, or restructuring code.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t test private methods\n- Don''t assert on internal state\n- Don''t verify method call sequences\n- Don''t couple tests to data structures users never see\n\n<instructions>\n\n## Test Structure (AAA)\n\nEvery test follows Arrange-Act-Assert:\n\n```\nArrange -- Set up preconditions and inputs\nAct     -- Execute the behavior under test\nAssert  -- Verify the expected outcome\n```\n\nSeparate the three sections with blank lines. One Act per test. One logical assertion per test.\n\n<examples>\n\n<example type=\"good\" title=\"Clear AAA structure, one behavior per test\">\n```python\ndef test_expired_subscription_denies_access():\n    # Arrange\n    user = create_user(subscription_end=yesterday())\n\n    # Act\n    result = check_access(user, resource=\"premium-content\")\n\n    # Assert\n    assert result.denied is True\n    assert result.reason == \"subscription expired\"\n```\nClear name, tests one behavior, obvious structure.\n</example>\n\n<example type=\"bad\" title=\"Multiple behaviors, internal state tested\">\n```python\ndef test_subscription():\n    user = create_user(subscription_end=yesterday())\n    assert check_access(user, \"premium-content\").denied\n    user.subscription_end = tomorrow()\n    assert check_access(user, \"premium-content\").allowed\n    assert user.access_log == [(\"denied\", \"premium-content\"), (\"allowed\", \"premium-content\")]\n```\nTwo behaviors in one test, tests internal log, vague name.\n</example>\n\n</examples>\n\n### Keep Tests DAMP, Not DRY\n\nPrefer **Descriptive And Meaningful Phrases** over eliminating duplication. Duplicating setup across tests is fine if it makes each test self-contained and readable. Extract shared setup into helpers only when it improves clarity, not to reduce line count.\n\n### No Logic in Tests\n\nTests are straight-line code. No loops, conditionals, ternaries, or string concatenation. If you need logic, the test is too complex -- split it or simplify the design.\n\n## What to Test\n\n### Test These\n\n- **Behaviors:** What the system does from a user''s perspective\n- **Edge cases:** Empty inputs, boundaries, overflow, zero, null\n- **Error paths:** Invalid input, missing dependencies, timeouts\n- **State transitions:** Before and after an operation\n\n### Skip These\n\n- Trivial getters/setters with no logic\n- Generated code (protobuf, ORM migrations)\n- Configuration files\n- Third-party library internals\n\n### Test Via Public APIs\n\nInvoke the system the same way its callers do. If the only way to test something is through a private method, the design needs to change -- extract it into a collaborator with its own public interface.\n\n## Naming Tests\n\nName tests after the behavior, not the method.\n\n| Good | Bad |\n|------|-----|\n| `rejects_empty_email_with_validation_error` | `test_validate` |\n| `returns_cached_result_when_within_ttl` | `test_cache` |\n| `retries_three_times_before_failing` | `test_retry_logic` |\n| `grants_access_when_subscription_active` | `test_check_access_method` |\n\nPatterns that work:\n- `[action]_[condition]_[expected_result]`\n- `should [expected behavior] when [condition]`\n- Plain descriptive sentence\n\nA test name containing \"and\" usually means two tests.\n\n## Choosing Test Level\n\n```dot\ndigraph test_level {\n    rankdir=TB;\n    start [label=\"What are you testing?\", shape=diamond];\n    pure [label=\"Pure logic?\\nNo I/O, no side effects\", shape=diamond];\n    boundary [label=\"System boundary?\\nDB, API, file, queue\", shape=diamond];\n    journey [label=\"Critical user journey?\\nLogin, checkout, signup\", shape=diamond];\n\n    unit [label=\"UNIT TEST\\nFast, isolated, many\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    integration [label=\"INTEGRATION TEST\\nBoundary focused, fewer\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffffcc\"];\n    e2e [label=\"E2E TEST\\nFull stack, minimal\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n\n    start -> pure;\n    pure -> unit [label=\"yes\"];\n    pure -> boundary [label=\"no\"];\n    boundary -> integration [label=\"yes\"];\n    boundary -> journey [label=\"no\"];\n    journey -> e2e [label=\"yes\"];\n    journey -> unit [label=\"no\\n(rethink)\"];\n}\n```\n\n**The pyramid:** Many unit tests. Fewer integration tests. Minimal E2E tests.\n\n**Push tests down.** If a behavior can be tested at a lower level, test it there. Lower = faster, more stable, cheaper to maintain. Only go higher when the lower level can''t verify the behavior (serialization, wiring, full user flow).\n\n**Duplicate coverage?** If a unit test and integration test verify the same behavior, keep the unit test. Remove the integration test unless it adds confidence about wiring.\n\n## Test Isolation and Doubles\n\n### When to Use Test Doubles\n\n| Use doubles for | Use real objects for |\n|----------------|---------------------|\n| Network calls (HTTP, gRPC) | In-process collaborators |\n| Database queries (in unit tests) | Value objects and data structures |\n| Filesystem I/O | Pure functions |\n| Non-deterministic sources (time, random) | Deterministic transformations |\n| Expensive operations (ML inference, rendering) | Lightweight dependencies |\n\n### Types of Doubles\n\n- **Stub:** Returns canned responses. Use when you need a dependency to return specific data.\n- **Fake:** Working implementation with shortcuts (in-memory DB, local file store). Preferred over mocks for complex interactions.\n- **Mock:** Records calls and asserts on them. Use sparingly -- only when the interaction IS the behavior (e.g., \"sends an email\").\n\n### The Mocking Rule\n\n```\nVerify STATE over INTERACTIONS.\nMock only when the side effect IS the behavior under test.\n```\n\n<examples>\n\n<example type=\"good\" title=\"Testing resulting state\">\n```typescript\n// Testing that withdrawal updates balance (state)\ntest(''withdrawal reduces account balance'', () => {\n  const account = new Account(100);\n\n  account.withdraw(30);\n\n  expect(account.balance).toBe(70);\n});\n```\nTests resulting state -- survives internal refactoring.\n</example>\n\n<example type=\"bad\" title=\"Testing internal interaction\">\n```typescript\n// Testing that withdrawal calls the right methods (interaction)\ntest(''withdrawal calls debit'', () => {\n  const ledger = mock(Ledger);\n  const account = new Account(100, ledger);\n\n  account.withdraw(30);\n\n  expect(ledger.debit).toHaveBeenCalledWith(30);\n});\n```\nTests internal interaction -- breaks if refactored.\n</example>\n\n</examples>\n\n## Unchanging Tests\n\nA well-written test changes only when requirements change. It survives:\n- **Refactoring** -- internal restructuring, no behavior change\n- **Bug fixes** -- new tests added, existing tests unchanged\n- **New features** -- unrelated tests unaffected\n\nIf your tests break during refactoring, they''re testing implementation details. Fix the tests to test behavior instead.\n\n## Clear Failure Messages\n\nA failure message should let you diagnose the problem without reading the test code.\n\n<examples>\n\n<example type=\"good\" title=\"Descriptive failure message\">\n```\nFAIL: rejects_empty_email_with_validation_error\n  Expected: ValidationError(\"email is required\")\n  Actual:   None (no error raised)\n```\nShows expected vs actual with context.\n</example>\n\n<example type=\"bad\" title=\"Opaque failure message\">\n```\nFAIL: test_validate\n  AssertionError: False is not True\n```\nNo context, unclear what was tested.\n</example>\n\n</examples>\n\nUse assertion libraries that produce descriptive messages. Prefer `assertEqual(expected, actual)` over bare `assert`.\n\n</instructions>\n\n<rules>\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |\n|-------------|---------|-----|\n| Testing implementation | Breaks on refactor | Test observable behavior via public API |\n| Over-mocking | Tests verify mocks, not code | Use real objects; mock only at boundaries |\n| Flaky tests | Non-deterministic (time, order, network) | Control inputs; isolate state; use fakes |\n| Ice cream cone | Too many E2E, few unit tests | Push tests down the pyramid |\n| Logic in tests | Bugs in test code hide bugs in prod | Straight-line code only |\n| Shared mutable state | Tests depend on run order | Fresh state per test (setup/teardown) |\n| Test-only production code | Methods exist only for testing | Test via public API; redesign if needed |\n| Assertion-free tests | Test runs but verifies nothing | Every test must assert expected outcome |\n| Giant setup | 50 lines before the act | Simplify design; extract builder/factory |\n\n## Red Flags -- STOP and Rethink\n\n- Mocking more than 2 dependencies -- class has too many responsibilities\n- Test setup exceeds 20 lines -- design is too complex or test scope too broad\n- Test name contains \"and\" -- split into two tests\n- Tests break when you refactor -- testing implementation, not behavior\n- Tests pass but bugs ship -- testing the wrong things\n- Can''t explain what behavior a test verifies -- rewrite or delete it\n- All tests use mocks -- not testing real behavior\n- Test file is longer than production file -- over-testing or testing internals\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Need mocks for everything\" | Design is too coupled. Inject dependencies, use fakes. |\n| \"100% coverage = quality\" | Coverage measures execution, not correctness. 80% covering behaviors > 100% covering lines. |\n| \"E2E tests cover everything\" | Slow, flaky, expensive. Unit tests catch most bugs faster. |\n| \"Test is too hard to write\" | Hard to test = hard to use. Fix the design. |\n| \"It''s just test code\" | Test code deserves production standards. Sloppy tests rot fast. |\n| \"One big test is easier\" | One big test = one useless failure message. Split by behavior. |\n| \"Helper makes it DRY\" | If the helper obscures what''s tested, inline it. DAMP > DRY. |\n\n</rules>\n\n## Quick Reference: FIRST Principles\n\n- **Fast** -- Tests run in seconds, not minutes. Slow tests get skipped.\n- **Independent** -- No test depends on another. Any order, any subset.\n- **Repeatable** -- Same result every run, any machine, any time.\n- **Self-checking** -- Pass/fail without human inspection.\n- **Timely** -- Written close to the code. Not \"later.\" Not \"before release.\"\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nTest what your users care about, through the interfaces they use.\nEverything else is an implementation detail.\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:55:04.687Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing structured test lifecycle management and quality gates in Claude Code projects.","zh":"适合需要结构化测试生命周期管理和质量门控的Claude Code项目的代码分析代理。","ja":"Claude Codeプロジェクトで構造化されたテストライフサイクル管理と品質ゲートが必要なコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 테스트 生命周期 관리 및 품질 게이트가 필요한 Claude Code 프로젝트를 위한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para los agentes de análisis de código que necesitan una gestión de ciclo de vida de pruebas estructurada y puertas de calidad en proyectos de Claude Code.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une gestion de cycle de vie de tests structurée et des portes de qualité dans les projets Claude Code.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine strukturierte Testlebenszyklusverwaltung und Qualitätsprüfungen in Claude-Code-Projekten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de gerenciamento de ciclo de vida de teste estruturado e portões de qualidade em projetos Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, которым необходим структурированный менеджмент жизненного цикла тестирования и ворота качества в проектах Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة دورة حياة الاختبار المهيكلة وأبواب الجودة في مشاريع Claude Code."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write effective tests, decide between unit, integration, and E2E tests, and utilize mocks, stubs, or fakes with discipline and parallel agents, streamlining test infrastructure setup and debugging of flaky tests.","zh":"赋予代理编写有效测试、在单元测试、集成测试和E2E测试之间进行选择，并使用模拟、存根或伪造对象来纪律并行代理，简化测试基础设施设置和调试易出错的测试。","ja":"エージェントが効果的なテストを書き、ユニットテスト、統合テスト、E2Eテストのどれを使用するかを決定し、並行エージェントを規律化してモック、スタブ、またはフェイクを使用し、テストインフラストラクチャの設定と不安定なテストのデバッグを簡素化する。","ko":"에이전트가 효과적인 테스트를 작성하고, 단위 테스트, 통합 테스트, E2E 테스트 중에서 선택하고, 모의, 스텁 또는 가짜를 사용하여 규율을 갖춘 병렬 에이전트를 사용하여 테스트 인프라 설정과 불안정한 테스트의 디버깅을 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas efectivas, decidir entre pruebas unitarias, de integración y E2E, y utilizar mocks, stubs o fakes con disciplina y agentes paralelos, racionalizando la configuración de la infraestructura de pruebas y la depuración de pruebas caprichosas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests efficaces, de choisir entre les tests unitaires, d''intégration et E2E, et d''utiliser des mocks, des stubs ou des fakes avec discipline et des agents parallèles, rationalisant la configuration de l''infrastructure de test et le débogage des tests capricieux.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, effektive Tests zu schreiben, zwischen Unit-, Integrations- und E2E-Tests zu entscheiden und Mocks, Stubs oder Fakes mit Disziplin und parallelen Agenten zu verwenden, wodurch die Einrichtung der Testinfrastruktur und die Fehlersuche bei launischen Tests rationalisiert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes eficazes, decidir entre testes unitários, de integração e E2E, e utilizar mocks, stubs ou fakes com disciplina e agentes paralelos, otimizando a configuração da infraestrutura de teste e a depuração de testes instáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать эффективные тесты, выбирать между юнит-тестами, интеграционными и E2E-тестами, а также использовать моки, стабы или фейки с дисциплиной и параллельными агентами, оптимизируя настройку тестовой инфраструктуры и отладку нестабильных тестов.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على كتابة اختبارات فعالة، والاختيار بين اختبارات الوحدة والتكامل واختبارات E2E، واستخدام مواقع الخدعة أو الاستبدال أو التقليد مع الانضباط والوكلاء المتوازيين، وضمن تحسين إعداد بنية الاختبار وتصحيح الاختبارات غير المستقرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating test coverage analysis for Python and Go projects","Debugging brittle or slow tests in test files like *.test.* or *_test.go","Generating testing strategies with quality gates for Claude Code projects","Setting up test utilities and infrastructure for efficient testing"],"zh":["为Python和Go项目自动化测试覆盖率分析","调试脆弱或慢速的测试，如*.test.*或*_test.go文件中的测试","为Claude Code项目生成带有质量门控的测试策略","设置测试工具和基础设施以实现高效测试"],"ja":["PythonとGoのプロジェクトのテストカバレッジ分析を自動化する","*.test.*または*_test.goなどのファイル内のテストをデバッグする","Claude Codeプロジェクトの品質ゲート付きのテスト戦略を生成する","効率的なテストのためのテストユーティリティとインフラストラクチャを設定する"],"ko":["파이썬 및 고 언어 프로젝트의 테스트 커버리지 분석을 자동화하는 것","*.test.* 또는 *_test.go와 같은 파일 내의 테스트 디버깅","클라우드 코드 프로젝트의 품질 게이트가 있는 테스트 전략 생성","효율적인 테스트를 위한 테스트 유틸리티 및 인프라 설정"],"es":["Automatizar el análisis de cobertura de pruebas para proyectos de Python y Go","Depurar pruebas frágiles o lentas en archivos de pruebas como *.test.* o *_test.go","Generar estrategias de prueba con puertas de calidad para proyectos de Claude Code","Configurar utilidades y infraestructura de pruebas para pruebas eficientes"],"fr":["Automatiser l''analyse de la couverture des tests pour les projets Python et Go","Déboguer les tests fragiles ou lents dans les fichiers de test comme *.test.* ou *_test.go","Générer des stratégies de test avec des portes de qualité pour les projets Claude Code","Configurer les utilitaires et l''infrastructure de test pour des tests efficaces"],"de":["Automatisieren der Abdeckungsanalyse von Tests für Python- und Go-Projekte","Fehlerhafte oder langsame Tests in Testdateien wie *.test.* oder *_test.go debuggen","Erzeugen von Teststrategien mit Qualitätsprüfungen für Claude-Code-Projekte","Einrichten von Testutilitäten und -infrastruktur für effiziente Tests"],"pt":["Automatizar a análise de cobertura de teste para projetos Python e Go","Depurar testes frágeis ou lentos em arquivos de teste como *.test.* ou *_test.go","Gerar estratégias de teste com portões de qualidade para projetos Claude Code","Configurar utilitários e infraestrutura de teste para teste eficiente"],"ru":["Автоматизировать анализ покрытия тестов для проектов Python и Go","Отладить хрупкие или медленные тесты в файлах тестов типа *.test.* или *_test.go","Сгенерировать стратегии тестирования с воротами качества для проектов Claude Code","Настроить утилиты и инфраструктуру тестирования для эффективного тестирования"],"ar":["تأتمتة تحليل تغطية الاختبار لمشاريع Python و Go","تصحيح اختبارات هشة أو بطيئة في ملفات الاختبار مثل *.test.* أو *_test.go","توليد استراتيجيات الاختبار بأبواب الجودة لمشاريع Claude Code","تكوين أدوات و بنية الاختبار لاختبار فعال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code project setup","Limited to specific file formats like *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Token budget limited to 400 lines or ~1200 tokens"],"zh":["需要Claude Code项目设置","仅限于特定文件格式，如*.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","令牌预算限制为400行或~1200个令牌"],"ja":["Claude Codeプロジェクトの設定が必要","特定のファイル形式（*.test.*、*.spec.*、*_test.go、test_*.py）のみに限定","トークン予算は400行または約1200トークンに制限"],"ko":["클라우드 코드 프로젝트 설정이 필요합니다.","특정 파일 형식 (*.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py)만 해당","토큰 예산은 400행 또는 약 1200토큰으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de proyecto de Claude Code","Limitado a formatos de archivo específicos como *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Presupuesto de tokens limitado a 400 líneas o ~1200 tokens"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de projet Claude Code","Limité à des formats de fichiers spécifiques comme *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Budget de jetons limité à 400 lignes ou ~1200 jetons"],"de":["Benötigt Claude-Code-Projektkonfiguration","Begrenzt auf bestimmte Dateiformate wie *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Token-Budget begrenzt auf 400 Zeilen oder ~1200 Token"],"pt":["Exige configuração do projeto Claude Code","Limitado a formatos de arquivo específicos como *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Orçamento de token limitado a 400 linhas ou ~1200 tokens"],"ru":["Требует настройки проекта Claude Code","Ограниченเฉพาะ определенными форматами файлов, такими как *.test.*, *.spec.*, *_test.go, test_*.py","Бюджет токенов ограничен 400 строками или ~1200 токенами"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مشروع Claude Code","محدود بالتنسيقات المحددة للملفات مثل *.test.*، *.spec.*، *_test.go، test_*.py","ميزانية رمز محدودة بـ 400 سطر أو ~1200 رمز"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"9823b2391a986386a632e95d43cd6759f1259adc1ae350c0ef0e6bd785fb6d8c","qualityScore":60}');
