m 体验，简化开发流程","ja":"reskill-usageはAIエージェントのスキルにnpmの体験をもたらします","ko":"reskill-usage는 AI 에이전트 기술에 npm 경험을 제공합니다","es":"Reskill Usage ofrece la experiencia de npm a las habilidades de los agentes de AI, simplificando el desarrollo de aplicaciones","fr":"Reskill Usage apporte l''expérience npm aux compétences des agents d''IA, simplifiant le développement d''applications","de":"Reskill Usage bringt die npm-Erfahrung auf die Fähigkeiten von KI-Agents, vereinfacht die Entwicklung von Anwendungen","pt":"Reskill Usage traz a experiência do npm para as habilidades do agente de IA, permitindo que os desenvolvedores usem facilmente as ferramentas de IA.","ru":"Reskill Usage приносит опыт npm в навыки ИИ Агентов, позволяя разработчикам легко использовать инструменты ИИ.","ar":"يحمل Reskill Usage تجربة npm إلى مهارات وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح للمطورين باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي بسهولة.","en":"reskill - brings the npm experience to AI agent skills."},"definition":{"en":"reskill - brings the npm experience to AI agent skills."},"features":{"zh":["提供 npm 体验","简化开发流程","提高开发效率","支持多种开发语言","易于集成和扩展"],"ja":["npmの体験を提供","開発プロセスを簡素化","開発効率を向上","複数の開発言語をサポート","簡単に統合および拡張可能"],"ko":["npm 경험 제공","개발 프로세스簡素化","개발 효율성 향상","다수의 개발 언어 지원","쉽게 통합 및 확장 가능"],"es":["Integración con npm","Desarrollo de aplicaciones simplificado","Compatibilidad con agentes de AI","Experiencia de usuario mejorada","Soporte técnico especializado"],"fr":["Intégration avec npm","Développement d''applications simplifié","Compatibilité avec les agents d''IA","Expérience utilisateur améliorée","Support technique spécialisé"],"de":["Integration mit npm","Vereinfachte Anwendungsentwicklung","Kompatibilität mit KI-Agents","Verbesserte Benutzeroberfläche","Spezialisiertes technisches Support"],"pt":["Integração com o npm","Fácil uso de ferramentas de IA","Melhoria da produtividade do desenvolvedor","Suporte a múltiplos agentes de IA","Flexibilidade e personalização"],"ru":["Интеграция с npm","Легкое использование инструментов ИИ","Повышение производительности разработчика","Поддержка нескольких ИИ Агентов","Гибкость и настройка"],"ar":["التكامل مع npm","استخدام سهل لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين إنتاجية المطور","دعم وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتعددين","المرونة والتخصيص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能体技能","npm体验","reskill-usage","如何使用reskill-usage","reskill-usage安装","reskill-usage设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェントスキル","npmの体験","reskill-usage","reskill-usageの使い方","reskill-usageのインストール","reskill-usageの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 기술","npm 경험","reskill-usage","reskill-usage 사용법","reskill-usage 설치","reskill-usage 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar Reskill Usage","qué es Reskill Usage","alternativas a Reskill Usage","Reskill Usage vs npm","instalación de Reskill Usage","guía de configuración de Reskill Usage"],"fr":["comment utiliser Reskill Usage","qu''est-ce que Reskill Usage","alternatives à Reskill Usage","Reskill Usage vs npm","installation de Reskill Usage","guide de configuration de Reskill Usage"],"de":["wie man Reskill Usage verwendet","was ist Reskill Usage","Alternativen zu Reskill Usage","Reskill Usage vs npm","Installation von Reskill Usage","Konfigurationsanleitung für Reskill Usage"],"pt":["como usar reskill usage","o que é reskill usage","reskill usage vs outros agentes de ia","guia de instalação do reskill usage","configuração do reskill usage","alternativas ao reskill usage","reskill usage para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать reskill usage","что такое reskill usage","reskill usage vs другие ИИ Агенты","руководство по установке reskill usage","настройка reskill usage","альтернативы reskill usage","reskill usage для разработчиков","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام reskill usage","ما هي reskill usage","reskill usage مقابل وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الآخرون","دليل تثبيت reskill usage","تثبيت reskill usage","بديلات reskill usage","reskill usage للمطورين","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"kanyun-inc","repo":"reskill","repoPath":"kanyun-inc/reskill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.975Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"reskill-usage","description":"Teaches AI agents how to use reskill — a Git-based package manager for AI agent skills. Covers CLI commands, install formats, configuration, publishing, and common workflows.","version":"0.1.0","tags":"","bodyPreview":"<!-- source: README.md -->\n<!-- synced: 2026-02-12 -->\n\n# reskill Usage Guide\n\nreskill is a Git-based package manager for AI agent skills. It provides declarative configuration (`skills.json` + `skills.lock`), flexible versioning, and multi-agent support for installing, managing, and sharing skills across projects and teams.\n\n**Requirements:** Node.js >= 18.0.0\n\n**CLI usage:** If `reskill` is installed globally, use it directly. Otherwise use `npx reskill@latest`:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g reskill","body":"<!-- source: README.md -->\n<!-- synced: 2026-02-12 -->\n\n# reskill Usage Guide\n\nreskill is a Git-based package manager for AI agent skills. It provides declarative configuration (`skills.json` + `skills.lock`), flexible versioning, and multi-agent support for installing, managing, and sharing skills across projects and teams.\n\n**Requirements:** Node.js >= 18.0.0\n\n**CLI usage:** If `reskill` is installed globally, use it directly. Otherwise use `npx reskill@latest`:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g reskill        # Global install\nnpx reskill@latest <command>  # Or use npx directly (no install needed)\n```\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Wants to install, update, or manage AI agent skills\n- Mentions `skills.json`, `skills.lock`, or reskill-related concepts\n- Wants to publish a skill to a registry\n- Asks about supported install formats (GitHub, GitLab, HTTP, OSS, registry, etc.)\n- Encounters reskill-related errors or needs troubleshooting\n- Wants to set up a project for skill management\n- Asks about multi-agent skill installation (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, etc.)\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# Initialize a new project\nnpx reskill@latest init\n\n# Install a skill\nnpx reskill@latest install github:anthropics/skills/skills/frontend-design@latest\n\n# List installed skills\nnpx reskill@latest list\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command               | Alias                | Description                               |\n| --------------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `init`                | -                    | Initialize `skills.json`                  |\n| `find <query>`        | -                    | Search for skills in the registry         |\n| `install [skills...]` | `i`                  | Install one or more skills                |\n| `list`                | `ls`                 | List installed skills                     |\n| `info <skill>`        | -                    | Show skill details                        |\n| `update [skill]`      | `up`                 | Update skills                             |\n| `outdated`            | -                    | Check for outdated skills                 |\n| `uninstall <skill>`   | `un`, `rm`, `remove` | Remove a skill                            |\n| `publish [path]`      | `pub`                | Publish a skill to the registry ¹         |\n| `login`               | -                    | Authenticate with the registry ¹          |\n| `logout`              | -                    | Remove stored authentication ¹            |\n| `whoami`              | -                    | Display current logged in user ¹          |\n| `doctor`              | -                    | Diagnose environment and check for issues |\n| `completion install`  | -                    | Install shell tab completion              |\n\n> ¹ Registry commands (`publish`, `login`, `logout`, `whoami`) require a private registry deployment. Not available for public use yet.\n\nRun `reskill <command> --help` for complete options and detailed usage.\n\n### Common Options\n\n| Option                    | Commands                             | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-save`               | `install`                            | Install without saving to `skills.json` (for personal skills) |\n| `-g, --global`            | `install`, `uninstall`, `list`       | Install/manage skills globally (user directory)               |\n| `-a, --agent <agents...>` | `install`                            | Specify target agents (e.g., `cursor`, `claude-code`)         |\n| `--mode <mode>`           | `install`                            | Installation mode: `symlink` (default) or `copy`              |\n| `--all`                   | `install`                            | Install to all agents                                         |\n| `-y, --yes`               | `install`, `uninstall`, `publish`    | Skip confirmation prompts                                     |\n| `-f, --force`             | `install`                            | Force reinstall even if already installed                     |\n| `-s, --skill <names...>`  | `install`                            | Select specific skill(s) by name from a multi-skill repo      |\n| `--list`                  | `install`                            | List available skills in the repository without installing    |\n| `-r, --registry <url>`    | `install`                            | Registry URL override for registry-based installs             |\n| `-j, --json`              | `list`, `info`, `outdated`, `doctor` | Output as JSON                                                |\n\n## Source Formats\n\nreskill supports installing skills from multiple sources:\n\n```bash\n# GitHub shorthand\nnpx reskill@latest install github:user/skill@v1.0.0\n\n# GitLab shorthand\nnpx reskill@latest install gitlab:group/skill@latest\n\n# Full Git URL (HTTPS)\nnpx reskill@latest install https://github.com/user/skill.git\n\n# Full Git URL (SSH)\nnpx reskill@latest install git@github.com:user/skill.git\n\n# GitHub/GitLab web URL (with branch and subpath)\nnpx reskill@latest install https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/web-design-guidelines\n\n# Custom registry (self-hosted GitLab, etc.)\nnpx reskill@latest install gitlab.company.com:team/skill@v1.0.0\n\n# HTTP/OSS archives\nnpx reskill@latest install https://example.com/skills/my-skill-v1.0.0.tar.gz\nnpx reskill@latest install oss://bucket/path/skill.tar.gz\nnpx reskill@latest install s3://bucket/path/skill.zip\n\n# Registry-based (requires registry deployment)\nnpx reskill@latest install @scope/skill-name@1.0.0\nnpx reskill@latest install skill-name\n\n# Install multiple skills at once\nnpx reskill@latest install github:user/skill1 github:user/skill2@v1.0.0\n```\n\n### Monorepo Support\n\nFor repositories containing multiple skills, specify the path to the skill directory:\n\n```bash\n# Shorthand format with subpath\nnpx reskill@latest install github:org/monorepo/skills/planning@v1.0.0\nnpx reskill@latest install gitlab:company/skills/frontend/components@latest\n\n# URL format with subpath\nnpx reskill@latest install https://github.com/org/monorepo.git/skills/planning@v1.0.0\nnpx reskill@latest install git@gitlab.company.com:team/skills.git/backend/apis@v2.0.0\n\n# GitHub web URL automatically extracts subpath\nnpx reskill@latest install https://github.com/org/monorepo/tree/main/skills/planning\n```\n\n**Requirements**: The specified directory must contain a valid `SKILL.md` file following the [Agent Skills Specification](https://agentskills.io).\n\n### HTTP/OSS URL Support\n\nSkills can be installed directly from HTTP/HTTPS URLs pointing to archive files:\n\n| Format       | Example                                                    | Description              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| HTTPS URL    | `https://example.com/skill.tar.gz`                         | Direct download URL      |\n| Aliyun OSS   | `https://bucket.oss-cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/skill.tar.gz` | Aliyun OSS URL           |\n| AWS S3       | `https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/skill.tar.gz`             | AWS S3 URL               |\n| OSS Protocol | `oss://bucket/path/skill.tar.gz`                           | Shorthand for Aliyun OSS |\n| S3 Protocol  | `s3://bucket/path/skill.tar.gz`                            | Shorthand for AWS S3     |\n\n**Supported archive formats:** `.tar.gz`, `.tgz`, `.zip`, `.tar`\n\n### Version Formats\n\n| Format | Example           | Description                        |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Exact  | `@v1.0.0`         | Lock to specific tag               |\n| Latest | `@latest`         | Get the latest tag                 |\n| Range  | `@^2.0.0`         | Semver compatible (>=2.0.0 <3.0.0) |\n| Branch | `@branch:develop` | Specific branch                    |\n| Commit | `@commit:abc1234` | Specific commit hash               |\n| (none) | -                 | Default branch (main)              |\n\n## Configuration\n\n### skills.json\n\nThe project configuration file, created by `reskill init`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skills\": {\n    \"planning\": \"github:user/planning-skill@v1.0.0\",\n    \"internal-tool\": \"internal:team/tool@latest\"\n  },\n  \"registries\": {\n    \"internal\": \"https://gitlab.company.com\"\n  },\n  \"defaults\": {\n    \"installDir\": \".skills\",\n    \"targetAgents\": [\"cursor\", \"claude-code\"],\n    \"installMode\": \"symlink\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `skills` — Installed skill references (name → source ref)\n- `registries` — Custom Git registry aliases\n- `defaults.installDir` — Where skills are stored (default: `.skills`)\n- `defaults.targetAgents` — Default agents to install to\n- `defaults.installMode` — `symlink` (default, recommended) or `copy`\n\n### Environment Variables\n\n| Variable            | Description                                     | Default                        |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `RESKILL_CACHE_DIR` | Global cache directory                          | `~/.reskill-cache`             |\n| `RESKILL_TOKEN`     | Auth token (takes precedence over ~/.reskillrc) | -                              |\n| `RESKILL_REGISTRY`  | Default registry URL                            | `https://registry.reskill.dev` |\n| `DEBUG`             | Enable debug logging                            | -                              |\n| `NO_COLOR`          | Disable colored output                          | -                              |\n\n## Multi-Agent Support\n\nSkills are installed to `.skills/` by default and can be integrated with any agent:\n\n| Agent          | Path                                  |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Cursor         | `.cursor/rules/` or `.cursor/skills/` |\n| Claude Code    | `.claude/skills/`                     |\n| Codex          | `.codex/skills/`                      |\n| Windsurf       | `.windsurf/skills/`                   |\n| GitHub Copilot | `.github/skills/`                     |\n| OpenCode       | `.opencode/skills/`                   |\n\nUse `--agent` to target specific agents, or `--all` to install to all detected agents:\n\n```bash\n# Install to specific agents\nreskill install github:user/skill -a cursor claude-code\n\n# Install to all detected agents\nreskill install github:user/skill --all\n```\n\n## Publishing\n\n> **Note:** Publishing requires a private registry deployment.\n\n### Authentication\n\n```bash\n# Login with a token (obtain from the registry web UI)\nreskill login --registry <url> --token <token>\n\n# Check current login status\nreskill whoami\n\n# Logout\nreskill logout\n```\n\nTokens are stored in `~/.reskillrc`. You can also use the `RESKILL_TOKEN` environment variable (takes precedence, useful for CI/CD).\n\nRegistry URL resolution priority:\n1. `--registry` CLI option\n2. `RESKILL_REGISTRY` environment variable\n3. `defaults.publishRegistry` in `skills.json`\n\n### Publishing a Skill\n\n```bash\n# Validate without publishing (recommended first step)\nreskill publish --dry-run\n\n# Publish the skill\nreskill publish\n\n# Publish from a specific directory\nreskill publish ./path/to/skill\n\n# Skip confirmation\nreskill publish -y\n```\n\nThe skill directory must contain a valid `SKILL.md`. A `skill.json` with `name`, `version`, and `description` is also required for publishing.\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### First-Time Project Setup\n\n```bash\n# 1. Initialize the project\nreskill init -y\n\n# 2. Install skills your project needs\nreskill install github:user/skill1@v1.0.0 github:user/skill2@latest -y\n\n# 3. Verify installation\nreskill list\n\n# 4. Commit skills.json and skills.lock to version control\n# (These files ensure team members get the same skill versions)\n```\n\n### Team Collaboration\n\nWhen a teammate clones the project, they run:\n\n```bash\n# Reinstall all skills from skills.json (like npm install)\nreskill install\n```\n\nThis reads `skills.json` + `skills.lock` and installs the exact same versions.\n\n### Checking and Updating Skills\n\n```bash\n# Check which skills have newer versions\nreskill outdated\n\n# Update all skills\nreskill update\n\n# Update a specific skill\nreskill update skill-name\n```\n\n### Global vs Project-Level Installation\n\n| Scope   | Flag | Directory               | Use Case                                   |\n| ------- | ---- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| Project | -    | `.skills/` (in project) | Team-shared skills, committed to git       |\n| Global  | `-g` | `~/.agents/skills/`     | Personal skills, available in all projects |\n\n```bash\n# Project-level (default)\nreskill install github:user/skill\n\n# Global (personal, all projects)\nreskill install github:user/skill -g\n\n# Personal project-level (not saved to skills.json)\nreskill install github:user/skill --no-save\n```\n\n### Diagnosing Issues\n\n```bash\n# Run environment diagnostics\nreskill doctor\n\n# JSON output for programmatic use\nreskill doctor --json\n```\n\nThe `doctor` command checks: reskill version, Node.js version, Git availability, cache directory, `skills.json` validity, `skills.lock` sync, installed skills integrity, and network connectivity.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Error Message                        | Cause                                 | Solution                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `skills.json not found`              | Project not initialized               | Run `reskill init`                                       |\n| `Unknown scope @xyz`                 | No registry configured for this scope | Check `registries` in `skills.json` or use full Git URL  |\n| `Skill not found`                    | Skill name doesn''t exist in registry  | Verify skill name; check `reskill find <query>`          |\n| `Version not found`                  | Requested version doesn''t exist       | Run `reskill info <skill>` to see available versions     |\n| `Permission denied`                  | Auth issue when publishing            | Run `reskill login`; check token scope                   |\n| `Token is invalid or expired`        | Stale authentication                  | Re-authenticate with `reskill login --token <new-token>` |\n| `Network error`                      | Cannot reach Git host or registry     | Check network; run `reskill doctor` for diagnostics      |\n| `Conflict: directory already exists` | Skill already installed               | Use `--force` to reinstall                               |\n\n### Private Repositories\n\nreskill uses your existing git credentials (SSH keys or credential helper). For CI/CD environments:\n\n```bash\n# GitLab CI\ngit config --global url.\"https://gitlab-ci-token:${CI_JOB_TOKEN}@gitlab.company.com/\".insteadOf \"https://gitlab.company.com/\"\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:55:05.914Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agent Developers needing streamlined skill management and versioning across projects.","zh":"非常适合需要跨项目简化技能管理和版本管理的AI代理开发人员。","ja":"プロジェクトを跨いだスキル管理とバージョン管理を簡素化する必要があるAIエージェント開発者に最適です。","ko":"프로젝트를跨越한 스킬 관리 및 버전 관리를 간소화해야하는 AI 에이전트 개발자를 위한 최적의 솔루션입니다.","es":"Perfecto para desarrolladores de agentes de IA que necesitan una gestión y versionado de habilidades optimizados en varios proyectos.","fr":"Parfait pour les développeurs d''agents IA ayant besoin d''une gestion et de versionning de compétences rationalisés à travers les projets.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Agent-Entwickler, die eine optimierte Fähigkeitsverwaltung und -versionierung über mehrere Projekte hinweg benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para desenvolvedores de Agentes de IA que precisam de gerenciamento de habilidades e versionamento simplificados em vários projetos.","ru":"Идеально для разработчиков агентов ИИ, которым необходим упрощенный менеджмент навыков и управление версиями в нескольких проектах.","ar":"مثالي لمطوري وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة مهارات ومصادقة إصدارات مبسطة عبر المشاريع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage skills declaratively using skills.json and skills.lock files, supporting flexible versioning and multi-agent installations via Git-based package management and Node.js.","zh":"通过skills.json和skills.lock文件使代理能够声明性地管理技能，支持灵活的版本管理和通过Git基于的包管理和Node.js的多代理安装。","ja":"skills.jsonとskills.lockファイルを使用してエージェントがスキルを宣言的に管理できるようにし、柔軟なバージョン管理とGitベースのパッケージ管理およびNode.jsを介したマルチエージェントインストールをサポートします。","ko":"skills.json 및 skills.lock 파일을 통해 에이전트가 스킬을 선언적으로 관리할 수 있도록 하며, 유연한 버전 관리 및 Git 기반 패키지 관리 및 Node.js를 통한 멀티 에이전트 설치를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar habilidades de forma declarativa utilizando los archivos skills.json y skills.lock, lo que admite una versionado flexible y una instalación multiagente a través de la gestión de paquetes basada en Git y Node.js.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des compétences de manière déclarative en utilisant les fichiers skills.json et skills.lock, ce qui prend en charge une version flexible et des installations multi-agents via une gestion de packages basée sur Git et Node.js.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Fähigkeiten deklarativ über die Dateien skills.json und skills.lock zu verwalten, was eine flexible Versionierung und eine Multi-Agent-Installation über Git-basiertes Paketmanagement und Node.js unterstützt.","pt":"Habilita agentes a gerenciar habilidades de forma declarativa usando arquivos skills.json e skills.lock, com suporte a versionamento flexível e instalações multiagentes via gerenciamento de pacotes baseado em Git e Node.js.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять навыками декларативно с помощью файлов skills.json и skills.lock, поддерживая гибкий/versioning и многоагентные установки через систему управления пакетами на основе Git и Node.js.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إدارة المهارات بطريقة إعلانية باستخدام ملفات skills.json و skills.lock، مع دعم مصادقة إصدارات مرنة وتثبيتات متعددة الوكلاء عبر إدارة حزم قائمة على Git و Node.js."},"useCases":{"en":["Installing skills across multiple projects","Managing skill versions for consistent performance","Sharing skills between teams using Git"],"zh":["跨多个项目安装技能","管理技能版本以实现一致的性能","使用Git在团队之间共享技能"],"ja":["複数のプロジェクトにわたってスキルをインストールする","一貫性のあるパフォーマンスを実現するためにスキルバージョンを管理する","Gitを使用してチーム間でスキルを共有する"],"ko":["여러 프로젝트에 스킬을 설치하는 것","일관된 성능을 위한 스킬 버전 관리","Git을 사용하여 팀 간에 스킬을 공유하는 것"],"es":["Instalar habilidades en varios proyectos","Gestionar versiones de habilidades para un rendimiento coherente","Compartir habilidades entre equipos mediante Git"],"fr":["Installer des compétences sur plusieurs projets","Gérer des versions de compétences pour des performances cohérentes","Partager des compétences entre équipes en utilisant Git"],"de":["Fähigkeiten in mehreren Projekten installieren","Fähigkeitsversionen für ein konsistentes Leistungsvermögen verwalten","Fähigkeiten zwischen Teams unter Verwendung von Git teilen"],"pt":["Instalar habilidades em vários projetos","Gerenciar versões de habilidades para desempenho consistente","Compartilhar habilidades entre equipes usando Git"],"ru":["Установка навыков в нескольких проектах","Управление версиями навыков для последовательной производительности","Обмен навыками между командами с помощью Git"],"ar":["تثبيت المهارات عبر مشاريع متعددة","إدارة إصدارات المهارات من أجل أداء متسق","مشاركة المهارات بين الفرق باستخدام Git"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"zh":["需要Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"ja":["Node.js >= 18.0.0が必要"],"ko":["Node.js >= 18.0.0이 필요"],"es":["Requiere Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"fr":["Nécessite Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"de":["Benötigt Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"pt":["Requer Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"ru":["Требуется Node.js >= 18.0.0"],"ar":["يتطلب Node.js >= 18.0.0"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"bbc9d4f633b9327929d40431e1bf069e91df79cfe1aed87ac0b3e8290332e863","qualityScore":60}');
